hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3601","Another (no. 141): And with it, from Ibn Abbas who said: (And withhold al-maun) (107:7): he said: Lending (ariyah)."
"3602","No. 142: And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr who said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer, no prayer for him. Al-Tabarani said: Thus al-Qatirani narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb mawquf (stopped). And Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb marfu (raised). And Adi ibn Thabit narrated it from Said, and it is in his biography, coming later."
"3603","Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 143: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - by reading to him while present -: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding Allah's saying, mighty and majestic: (Whatever linah you cut or left standing upon its roots, it is by Allah's permission) (59:5): he said: Al-linah is the palm tree; (and to disgrace the defiantly disobedient): he said: They brought them down from their forts, and they were ordered to cut the palms, and it weighed in their chests; so the Muslims said: We cut some and left some; shall we ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Have we reward in what we cut? And is there sin upon us in what we left? So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (Whatever linah you cut or left standing upon its roots, it is by Allah's permission, and to disgrace the defiantly disobedient). Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Amrah except Hafs ibn Ghiyath; Affan is alone in it. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasai both narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani from Affan, and al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Tirmidhi also narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Harun ibn Muawiyah from Hafs ibn Ghiyath mursal, not mentioning Ibn Abbas."
"3604","No. 144: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (Alif-Lam-Mim; the Romans are defeated) (30:1-2): he said: Defeated and defeating. He said: The idolaters loved that Persia prevail over Rome because they are people of idols, and the Muslims loved that Rome prevail over Persia because they are People of the Book; so they mentioned it to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: They shall indeed prevail. He said: Abu Bakr mentioned it to them, and they said: Set between us and you a term; if we prevail we have such-and-such, and if you prevail you have such-and-such. So he set a term of five years, and they did not prevail; so Abu Bakr mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Why did you not make it to less - I think - than ten? He said: Said ibn Jubayr said: Al-bid (a few) is less than ten. Then Rome prevailed after. He said: That is His saying: (Alif-Lam-Mim; the Romans are defeated) to His saying: (And on that day the believers rejoice) (30:4): he said: They rejoice in Allah's victory. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it. And he also narrated with this chain, he said: Rome prevailed (after their defeat, they shall prevail within a few years) (30:3-4). He said: Rome was defeated, then prevailed after. He said: (To Allah belongs the command before and after, and on that day the believers rejoice in Allah's victory) (30:4-5): he said: The believers rejoice in Allah's victory."
"3605","No. 145: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us from Abi Ishaq from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Muslims loved that Rome prevail over Persia because they are People of the Book, and the idolaters loved that Persia prevail over Rome because they are people of idols; so the Muslims mentioned that to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: They shall indeed be defeated. So Abu Bakr mentioned that to them, and they said: Set between us and you a term; if they prevail you have such-and-such, and if we prevail we have such-and-such. So he set between them a term of five years, and they did not prevail; so Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Why did you not make it - I think he said - less than ten? He said: Said said: Al-bid is less than ten. He said: Rome prevailed after; that is His saying: (Alif-Lam-Mim; the Romans are defeated in the nearest land, and they after their defeat shall prevail within a few years) (30:1-4). He said: Rome was defeated, then prevailed after. He said: (To Allah belongs the command before and after, and on that day the believers rejoice in Allah's victory) (30:4-5). Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Husayn ibn Hurayth from Muawiyah ibn Amr, saying: A hasan gharib hadith, and in a narration: sahih. We know it only from the hadith of Sufyan from Habib."
"3606","Another (no. 146): Abu Jafar Muhammad also informed us that al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them - by reading to him - while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Burani narrated to us: Fadl ibn Muhalhal, brother of Mufaddal, narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks with his right to his brother to fulfill it, for him is charity; whoever guides the traveler, for him is charity; whoever removes harm from the road, for him is charity; whoever helps carry a beast, for him is charity; and every good is charity."
"3607","Another (no. 147): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud al-Isbahani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Mazini narrated to us: Jafar ibn Salamah al-Warraq narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ali ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us: Habib ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition with al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad; when they came to the people they found them dispersed, and a man with much wealth remained; so he said: I testify there is no god but Allah. Al-Miqdad inclined to him and killed him. A man of his companions said: Did you kill a man who said: There is no god but Allah? By Allah, we shall mention that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they said: O Messenger of Allah, a man testified there is no god but Allah and al-Miqdad killed him. He said: Call al-Miqdad to me. He said: O Miqdad, you killed a man who said: There is no god but Allah! How shall you do with: There is no god but Allah? He said: So Allah revealed: (O you who believe, when you go forth in Allah's way, verify, and do not say to one who offers you salaam: You are not a believer, seeking the goods of worldly life; with Allah are many gains; thus you were before, and Allah favored you) (4:94). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was a believing man hiding his faith among disbelieving people, and you killed him; likewise you before hid your faith in Makkah. Al-Bukhari narrated its end in commentary, saying: Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Miqdad: If a believing man hides his faith among disbelieving people and manifests his faith and you kill him, likewise you hid your faith in Makkah before. Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated it from Abi Ishaq al-Fazari from Sufyan from Habib from Said ibn Jubayr who said: Al-Miqdad went out, without mentioning Ibn Abbas, abridged."
"3608","Another (no. 148): Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan, he is Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (The fornicator marries only a fornicatress or idolatress) (24:3): he said: None fornicates except with a fornicatress."
"3609","Another (no. 149): Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abu Amr - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim - narrated to us: Abu Hatim - he is al-Razi - narrated to us: Said ibn Awn narrated to us in al-Bakarat: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Habib ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (or two others than you) (5:106): he said: Of non-Muslims, of the People of the Book."
"3610","Another (no. 150): Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Husayn al-Harbi narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Amrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Musa, peace be upon him, said: (Indeed I am in need of whatever good You send down to me) (28:24): he said: He said this while the noblest of Allah's creation to Him, and he was in need of half a date, his belly stuck to his back from hunger."
"3611","Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 151: Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Quran was separated from the dhikr and placed in the Bayt al-Izzah in the lowest heaven; so Jibril descended with it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), chanting tartil (measured recitation)."
"3612","Nos. 152-153: Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz known as Qafak in Isfahan informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us. Ibn Marduwayh said: And Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (So I swear by the places of stars) (56:75): he said: The stars of the Quran; the Quran was separated from the dhikr and placed in the Bayt al-Izzah in the lowest heaven; so Jibril descended it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), chanting it tartil. Sufyan said: Five verses and like."
"3613","No. 154: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad al-Sulami informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Imam informed us: Said ibn Abdus ibn Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Hassan from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Quran was separated from the dhikr and placed in the Bayt al-Izzah - meaning in the lowest heaven -; Jibril brought it down to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), chanting it tartil. Sufyan said: Five verses and like. Al-Nasai narrated it in Fada'il al-Quran from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim from al-Firyabi. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Maryam: we transmitted it for consideration."
"3614","Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 155: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn al-Fadl al-Hafiz informed us that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us: Harun narrated to us from Aban ibn Taghlib from al-Hakam from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: (when they are fortified) (4:25): he said: Husbands fortified them; and the slave woman was not lashed if she had no husband."
"3615","Hammad - I deem him Ibn Salamah - from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 156: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them while present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Duhaym narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Sufyan from Hammad from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (hawala)."
"3616","No. 157: The qadi Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Samad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Ansari informed us in Damascus that Abu Muhammad Tahir ibn Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed them: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Uthman ibn Abdullah al-Azdi al-Misri informed us, it was said to him: Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Khurshid informed you in his saying - by reading to him -: Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Marwazi known as Ibn al-Hamid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Hammad from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I find in my chest a thing; to be charcoal is dearer to me than to speak it. He said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah who reduced his affair to whispering. The wording of al-Hasan ibn Muhammad. And in Duhaym's narration - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim -: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah... mentioning it. Al-Nasai narrated it - in the book of deeds of day and night - from Duhaym, saying: I know none who followed Ishaq in this narration. And the correct is what Ibn Mahdi narrated, from Sufyan from Hammad from Ibrahim from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal."
"3617","Another (no. 158): Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Utaybah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us: Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us from al-Hakam from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (You are only a warner, and for every people a guide) (13:7): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warner and the guide: Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"3618","Salim ibn Ajlan al-Jazari al-Aftas from Said ibn Jubayr. Nos. 159-160: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me (hawala). Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Rabah ibn Abi Maruf al-Makki narrated to us from Salim ibn Ajlan al-Aftas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayy said his father told him: O son, seek for me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a garment of his garments to shroud me in, and order him to pray over me. Abdullah said: I knew the honor of Abdullah, and that he ordered me to ask you for a garment to shroud him in, and to pray over him. So he gave him a garment of his garments, and intended to pray over him. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you knew Abdullah and his hypocrisy; do you pray over him, while Allah forbade you to pray over him! He said: Where? He said: (If you seek forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will not forgive them) (9:80). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall increase. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (And do not pray over any of them who died ever, nor stand over his grave) (9:84); and Allah revealed: (Equal upon them whether you seek forgiveness for them or not, Allah will not forgive them) (63:6). He said: And a man entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... to the end of the verses; so Umar said: Blessed be Allah, best of creators (23:14); so was revealed: (So blessed be Allah, best of creators). Rabah ibn Abi Maruf al-Makki: Yahya ibn Main weakened him; al-Daraqutni said: No harm in him. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Salih al-hadith. Abu Zurah said: Salih. Ibn Adi said: I saw no harm in his narrations. Salim ibn Ajlan al-Aftas: Ahmad ibn Hanbal trusted him, al-Bukhari narrated from him; Ibn Hibban al-Busti criticized him; Imam Ahmad and al-Bukhari know better than Ibn Hibban, Allah knows best. In al-Bukhari and Muslim from the hadith of Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the grave of Abdullah ibn Ubayy after he was buried, took him out, blew of his saliva in him, and dressed him his shirt. And in al-Bukhari from the hadith of Umar ibn al-Khattab: When Abdullah ibn Ubayy died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called to pray over him; when he stood I rushed to him and said: Do you pray over Ibn Ubayy... the hadith; then was revealed: (And do not pray over any of them who died ever). As for the story of the Badr captives, Muslim narrated it from the narration of Abu Zumayl Simak al-Hanafi from Ibn Abbas in sequel of the hadith of Abu Zumayl from Ibn Abbas from Umar about Badr."
"3619","Another (no. 161): And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ubayd ibn Fistas al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Salim al-Aftas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (Allah confirms those who believe with the firm word in worldly life) (14:27): he said: The questioning in the grave: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? And in the Hereafter likewise. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sad ibn Ubaydah from al-Bara ibn Azib that the believer, when he testifies there is no god but Allah and knows Muhammad in his grave, that is His saying: (Allah confirms those who believe with the firm word in worldly life)."
"3620","Another (no. 162): And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tahawi narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Salim al-Aftas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Quran descended at once, then was sent upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in portions."
"3621","Another (no. 163): Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid, both Thaqafi, informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Rijal al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us from Salim, he is al-Aftas, from Said from Ibn Abbas who said: No one exaggerated in Qadar but exited faith. Al-Bukhari transmitted the hadith: Healing is in three: a drink of honey, a cupping cut, and cauterization by fire; and I forbid my nation cauterization; raising the hadith from Husayn, not ascribed, from Ahmad ibn Mani with this chain."
"3622","Sulayman ibn Fayruz al-Shaybani from Said ibn Jubayr. Nos. 164-165: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me (hawala). And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal informed us from Sulayman al-Shaybani from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and wore it, then said: This distracted me from you since today; to it a glance and to you a glance. Then he cast it away. In al-Tabarani's narration: Malik ibn Mighwal from al-Shaybani. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Harb al-Marwazi from Uthman ibn Umar. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Awn from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi from Uthman ibn Umar."
"3623","Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim al-Ahwal from Said ibn Jubayr. Nos. 166-167: Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us: my father narrated to us (hawala). Al-Tabarani said: And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakim al-Samarqandi narrated to us: Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, both from Shibl ibn Abbad al-Makki from Sulayman al-Ahwal from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that he poured wudu for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his aunt Maymunah; when he came out he said: Who placed my wudu for me? She said: Your sister's son, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, make him understand religion and teach him interpretation. We intended from this hadith... and teach him interpretation; as for His saying: Make him understand religion, it is transmitted in the two Sahihs."
"3624","Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah al-Absi Abu Abdullah al-Kufi from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 168: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us in Makkah: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us: Abu Ubayd Allah Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Sulayman from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (of the average of what you feed your families) (5:89): he said: A man fed his family food with surplus, and fed his family food less; so Allah, exalted, revealed: (of the average of what you feed your families): he said: Neither the highest nor the lowest."
"3625","No. 169: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Abu Tahir Sahl ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Uyaynah from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (of the average of what you feed your families): he said: A man fed his family food in plenty, and food less than that; so it was said: of the average: neither the highest nor the lowest. Added in this narration Sulayman ibn Uyaynah; I saw no mention of him in Ibn Abi Hatim's book. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah. I say: Perhaps Ibn Uyaynah heard it from Sulayman ibn Uyaynah from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah, then heard it from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah; or he concealed it; I deem Sulayman ibn Uyaynah an addition of some narrators, an error, Allah knows best."
"3626","Sulayman ibn Mihran al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 170 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim and Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz - at Isfahan - informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning: {And We wrote in the Zabur after the Reminder} - he said: the Zabur is the Qur'an, the Torah and the Gospel, and the Reminder is the Reminder that is in heaven; {that My righteous servants shall inherit the land} - the land is Paradise."
"3627","Another. 171 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us; he said: my father narrated to me; al-A'mash narrated to us; he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {He knows the treachery of the eyes} - when you look at her, do you intend treachery or not? {and what the breasts conceal} - when you are able to have her, will you commit adultery with her or not? Shall I not inform you of what follows it: {And Allah judges with the truth} - He is able to reward good with good and evil with evil: indeed Allah is the Hearing, the Seeing. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"3628","Another. 172 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abu Amr - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Adam narrated to us; Hibban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {the whisperer, the retreater} - it is Satan who attends the newborn and casts whispering upon his heart, and he turns him wherever he wills; when he remembers Allah he retreats, and when he is heedless he crouches upon his heart and whispers."
"3629","Another. 173 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us. (Another chain:) 174 - Al-Tabarani said: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dispense with asking people, even with a sliver of a tooth-stick."
"3630","175 - Al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Qafan - at Baghdad - informed us that Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn al-Banna informed them; Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us; Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dispense with asking people, even with a sliver of a tooth-stick. Hamdan ibn Ali said: I asked Ahmad about the hadith of Abd al-Aziz al-Qasmali: Dispense with asking people; he said: It is rejected (munkar); I have not seen a hadith more rejected than it."
"3631","Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 176 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will enter upon you a man who looks with the eye of a devil, or with the two eyes of a devil. He said: Then a blue-eyed man entered and said: O Muhammad, why did you revile me or insult me, or something like this. He said: And he began to swear oaths. He said: This verse was revealed concerning disputation: {And they swear to a lie while they know}, and the other verse."
"3632","177 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr at Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us; both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of a chamber over which the shade had almost shrunk, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come to you who will look at you with the two eyes of a devil, so when he comes to you do not speak to him. They had scarcely waited when a man appeared, so he called him and said: Why do you revile me, you and your companions? He said: Call them, so they called them, and they began to swear by Allah that they had neither said nor done, until he pardoned them. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {On the Day Allah resurrects them all, they will swear to Him as they swear to you} ... the verse."
"3633","178 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3634","179 - And al-Tabarani said: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3635","180 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was... (Another chain:)"
"3636","181 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Simak ibn Harb narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me that Ibn Abbas narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the shade of one of his chambers, with a group of Muslims with him from whom the shade had almost shrunk. He said: He said: A man will come to you who looks at you with the two eyes of a devil, so when he comes to you do not speak to him. He said: Then a blue-eyed man came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and spoke to him. He said: Why do you revile me - you and so-and-so and so-and-so - a group whose names he called. He said: The man went and called them, and they swore to him by Allah and offered excuses. He said: Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {They will swear to Him as they swear to you, and they think} ... the verse. The wording is that of the hadith of Imam Ahmad. And in the wording of Ibn Mani': ... and so-and-so, a group whose names he called; with him: they swore to him and offered excuses; and at its end: {and they think that they are upon something}."
"3637","182 - And with it my father narrated to me; Mu'ammal narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us; Simak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of a chamber from which the shade had almost shrunk ... then he mentioned it. In the hadith of Shu'bah, the man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in the hadith of Zuhayr and Isra'il, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Why do you revile me; and I think it is the correct view, and Allah knows best. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abu Ahmad and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, from Isra'il, similarly."
"3638","Another. 183 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Husayn and Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; both said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {You are the best nation brought forth for mankind} - he said: They are those who emigrated with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah. Abu Nu'aym said: With the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3639","184 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us; he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Abu Nu'aym informed us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {You are the best nation brought forth for mankind} - he said: They are those who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah."
"3640","185 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {You are the best nation brought forth for mankind} - he said: They are those who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal also narrated it from Hashim and Yahya ibn Adam, from Isra'il."
"3641","Another. 186 - And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate (qunut) in Fajr, supplicating against a clan of Banu Sulaym."
"3642","Another. 187 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo - informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them; Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us - recited to him - Abu Ya'qub Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun al-Harbi informed us; Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud al-Nahdi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the idolaters said: Bring us a sign - he said: The sending of a man with his signet-ring, meaning a token. So this is the sign."
"3643","Sharik ibn Abd Allah, the judge, al-Nakha'i al-Kufi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 188 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us that his father informed them - recited to him - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us; Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Ali narrated to us; Sharik informed us, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas; and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas; and al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Ibrahim - both said - concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And married women, except those your right hands possess} - from among the captives who have husbands, there is no harm concerning them; they are lawful for you."
"3644","Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 189 - The shaykh, the imam, the learned Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Jawzi informed us - recited to him while we listened, at Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Dinawari informed you - recited to him - he said: The ascetic shaykh Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Qazwini dictated to us - in his mosque in al-Harbiyyah - Muhammad ibn Ali - he is Ibn Suwayd al-Mu'addib - narrated to us; Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us at Harran; Muhammad ibn al-Ala - meaning Abu Kurayb - narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, You made the first of Quraysh taste affliction, so make the last of them taste favor."
"3645","190 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me from his book; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us; al-A'mash said - meaning - he narrated, from Tariq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, You made the first of Quraysh taste affliction, so make the last of them taste favor."
"3646","191 - Abu Ali Diya ibn al-Khurayq informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Sukaynah informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us; my father narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, You made the first of Quraysh taste affliction, so make the last of them taste favor. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Yahya Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himmani; and from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam al-Warraq, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, with his chain, similarly; and he said: A fair (hasan), sound (sahih), strange (gharib) hadith."
"3647","Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 192 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When wine was prohibited, the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to one another and said: Wine has been prohibited and made equal to idolatry."
"3648","Another. 193 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Rafi'i narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Malik al-Muqri narrated to us; Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from Talhah, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The seven oft-repeated - he said: The seven long surahs."
"3649","Talhah ibn Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 194 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; he said: And he mentioned Talhah ibn Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man of the Ansar married a woman of Banu al-Ajlan and consummated with her and spent the night with her; in the morning he said: I did not find her a virgin. Their case was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called the girl and asked her, and she said: Rather, I was a virgin. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning the two of them, and he gave her the dower. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Salamah, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father. And I think Ibn Ishaq did not hear it from Talhah, and Allah knows best."
"3650","Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 195 - Abu al-Tahir Isma'il ibn Salih ibn Yasin ibn Imran al-Shari'i - at al-Shari' between Egypt and Cairo - informed us that Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Farisi informed us - at al-Fustat - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shuja', known as Ibn al-Mufassir al-Dimashqi, informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Sa'id al-Qadi narrated to us; Abu Khaythamah narrated to us. (Another chain:) 196 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Mansur informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us. (Another chain:) 197 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, known as Ibn Akhi Mimi, informed us; Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Uthman - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us. (Another chain:) 198 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym informed us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Nasibi narrated to us; al-Harith - he is Ibn Abi Usamah - narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Isa ibn Nujayh narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us - both said together - from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you. Their wording is one. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-A'mash. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Barmaki, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from al-A'mash."
"3651","Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 199 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your kohl is ithmid at bedtime; it grows hair and clears vision; and the best of your garments are white - wear them and shroud your dead in them."
"3652","200 - The imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at bedtime, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"3653","201 - And with it Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear these garments and shroud your dead in them."
"3654","202 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu Ahmad narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your kohl is ithmid at bedtime; it grows hair and clears vision; and the best of your garments are white, so wear them and shroud your dead in them."
"3655","203 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl informed them; Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us; al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you wear is white, so wear it and shroud your dead in it; and the best of your kohl is ithmid, so apply it, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"3656","204 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white from your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it grows hair and clears vision."
"3657","205 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: The best of your garments are white, so clothe your living in them and shroud your dead in them."
"3658","206 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us; Za'idah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym al-Makki narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Wear white from your garments, for they are the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"3659","207 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white from your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohl is ithmid; it clears vision and grows hair. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Waki', from al-Mas'udi, from Ibn Khuthaym, similarly; and from Abu Kamil, from Zuhayr; and from Abd al-Razzaq, from Sufyan - both from Abd Allah ibn Uthman. Abu Dawud narrated it - mentioning Wear white from your garments - from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Zuhayr. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki - all from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym; and al-Tirmidhi said: A fair, sound hadith. The hadith of Among the best of your kohl is ithmid was narrated by al-Nasa'i from Qutaybah, from Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yahya ibn Adam. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in al-Shama'il from Qutaybah, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal - all from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid, from Wuhayb, from Ibn Khuthaym. And he narrated the mention of kohl from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, and from Imran ibn Musa, from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid."
"3660","Another. 208 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone has a tongue and two lips that will testify on the Day of Resurrection for whoever touches it rightfully."
"3661","209 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will surely raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, testifying for whoever touches it rightfully."
"3662","210 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone has a tongue and two lips that will testify on the Day of Resurrection for whoever touches it rightfully. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Ali ibn Asim, from Ibn Khuthaym; and from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah; and from Yunus, from Hammad; and from Rawh, from Hammad."
"3663","211 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them; Abu al-Ghana'im Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Shadhan al-Harbi, known as al-Sukkari, informed us; Ahmad - he is Ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi - narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone will surely be raised on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, testifying concerning whoever touches it rightfully."
"3664","212 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abd Allah Samuwayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It will come on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, testifying for whoever touches it rightfully. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Jarir. Ibn Majah narrated it from Suwayd ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Rahim al-Razi - both from Abd Allah ibn Khuthaym. Al-Tirmidhi said: A fair hadith. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Fudayl al-Jahdari, from Fudayl ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Khuthaym."
"3665","Another. 213 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Surayj and Yunus narrated to us; both said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions performed Umrah from al-Ji'ranah, and they tucked their cloaks under their armpits. Yunus said: They placed their cloaks. Yunus said: And they threw them over their left shoulders."
"3666","214 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us; Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions performed Umrah from Ji'ranah, tucking their cloaks under their armpits over their left shoulders."
"3667","215 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions performed Umrah from al-Ji'ranah, tucking their cloaks and placing their cloaks under their armpits, throwing them over their shoulders, then trotting. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Rawh, from Hammad. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Salamah al-Tabudhaki, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"3668","Another. 216 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Makkah: How pleasant and beloved you are to me! Had your people not expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere."
"3669","217 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at Makkah: How pleasant and beloved you are to me; had my people not expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere."
"3670","218 - Abu al-Ma'ali Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Ball - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed them; al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Aziz ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Kharaqi informed us; Qasim - he is Ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym; Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Makkah: How pleasant a land and beloved you are to me; had my people not expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Basri al-Harashi in agreement, exactly like our narration, and said: A fair, sound, strange hadith from this angle. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Kamil Fudayl ibn al-Husayn al-Jahdari."
"3671","Another. 219 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us; Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims descent from other than his father, and allies himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Wuhayb."
"3672","220 - Abu Ja'far - also - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or allies himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"3673","221 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Affan narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims descent from other than his father or allies himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"3674","222 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa Abdan al-Ahwazi al-Hafiz informed us; Uthman and Abu Bakr narrated to us; both said: Affan narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or allies himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Ibn Abi al-Dayf, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, from Abu Khaythamah, from Affan ibn Muslim. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the narration of Yazid ibn Sharik al-Taymi, from Ali."
"3675","Another. 223 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Dawud, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us - all from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with the permission of a guiding guardian, or a ruler."
"3676","224 - Abu Ja'far - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman and Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"3677","Another. 225 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; both said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioning his Lord, Mighty and Majestic; He said: When My servant remembers Me alone, I remember him alone; and when he remembers Me in an assembly, I remember him in an assembly better than the assembly in which he remembered Me. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"3678","Another. 226 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him - while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us; Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us. (Another chain:) 227 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them - recited to him - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us; Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us; Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye. The hadith of Abu Nu'aym ends here ... and Ibn Ridhah added: And ajwah dates are from Paradise, and they are a cure from poison. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica the fat tail of a ram, divided into three parts, then melted and drunk, one part each day on an empty stomach. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym except Ibn Jurayj, nor from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid; al-Hasan alone narrated it from Ibn Mahdi."
"3679","228 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Sulami al-Dimashqi informed us - recited to him - it was said to him: Muhammad - he is Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Nasir ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Umar - at Baghdad - informed you; Muhammad ibn al-Saqr - he is Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Saqr al-Anbari - informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed us; Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq ibn Utbah al-Razi narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb ibn Sa'id ibn Mihran al-Azdi narrated to us; Mahdi ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ajwah is from Paradise, and in it is a cure from poison; truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye; and the black Arab ram is a cure for sciatica - its meat is eaten and its broth is sipped. Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad - Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not strong. Abu Hatim al-Busti criticized him, Yahya ibn Ma'in deemed him trustworthy, and Muslim narrated from him. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the hadith of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."
"3680","Another. 229 - The imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli al-Mufti, Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl - at Isfahan - and Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi - at Damascus - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them - recited to her - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Walid ibn al-Abbas al-Addas al-Misri narrated to us; Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: (in a muddy spring). Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym except Hammad; Abu Salih al-Harrani alone narrated it."
"3681","Another. 230 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that men of Quraysh gathered in al-Hijr, then pledged by al-Lat, al-Uzza, Manat the third, the other, Na'ilah and Isaf that if they saw Muhammad they would rise against him as one man and kill him before dispersing. His daughter Fatimah came weeping until she entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: These chiefs of your people have pledged that if they see you they will rise against you and kill you; there is not one man among them but knows his share of your blood. He said: O my daughter, bring me water for ablution. He performed ablution, then entered the mosque upon them. When they saw him they said: Here he is; they lowered their gazes and their chins fell upon their chests; they did not raise their eyes to him, and no man among them rose toward him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he stood over their heads, took a handful of dust, then said: May the faces be disgraced. Then he pelted them with it; no man among them was struck by a pebble of that gravel but was killed as a disbeliever on the Day of Badr."
"3682","231 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the chiefs of Quraysh gathered in al-Hijr and pledged by al-Lat, al-Uzza, Manat the third, the other, Na'ilah and Isaf that if they saw Muhammad they would rise against him as one man and not disperse until they killed him. His daughter Fatimah came weeping until she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: These chiefs of Quraysh have pledged against you; if they see you they will rise against you and kill you; there is not a man among them but knows his share of your blood. He said: O my daughter, show me ablution water. He performed ablution, then entered the mosque upon them. When they saw him they said: Here he is; they lowered their gazes, their chins fell upon their chests, and they were transfixed in their seats; they did not raise their eyes to him, and no man among them rose toward him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he stood over their heads, took a handful of dust and said: May the faces be disgraced. Then he pelted them with it; no man among them was struck by a pebble of that gravel but was killed as a disbeliever on the Day of Badr."
"3683","232 - And with it my father narrated to me; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the chiefs of Quraysh gathered in al-Hijr and pledged by al-Lat, al-Uzza and Manat the third, the other that if they saw Muhammad they would rise against him as one man and not disperse until they killed him. Fatimah came weeping until she entered upon her father ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"3684","Another. 233 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani - with my recitation to each of them at Isfahan - informed us; I said to each of them: Abu Tahir Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed you while you were present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us while I was present; Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf informed us; Ali ibn Muhammad - he is Ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib - narrated to us; Abu Salamah narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was in the house of Maymunah bint al-Harith, and I placed purifying water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who placed this? Maymunah said: Abd Allah ibn Abbas placed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation."
"3685","234 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Zuhayr Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand on my shoulder, or on my upper arm - Sa'id doubted - then said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation."
"3686","235 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand on my shoulder, or said: my upper arm - Sa'id doubted - and said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Zuhayr; and from Abd al-Samad, from Hammad. Al-Bukhari and Muslim brought from the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, and I placed ablution water for him; when he came out he said: Who placed this? It was said: Ibn Abbas. He said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion - and they did not bring - and teach him interpretation - and this is a fair addition."
"3687","Another. 236 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Katib narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us. 237 - Ahmad ibn Musa said: And Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Sabiq narrated to us; both said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {And We gave you seven of the oft-repeated} - he said: He repeats with examples, lessons and reports."
"3688","Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 238 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us; Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The seven oft-repeated is the Opening of the Book."
"3689","239 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Salamah narrated to us; Sunayd ibn Dawud narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd and Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: My father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he informed him that he asked Ibn Abbas about the seven oft-repeated? He said: The Mother of the Qur'an. Sa'id said: He recited it, reciting in it {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate}; and Sa'id ibn Jubayr recited it as Ibn Abbas recited it, reciting in it {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate}. I said to Ibn Abbas: What are the oft-repeated? He said: It is the Mother of the Qur'an; Allah excepted it for the nation of Muhammad, raising it in the Mother of the Book, storing it for them until He brought it forth, and He did not give it to anyone before them. He said: I said to my father: Did Sa'id ibn Jubayr inform you that Ibn Abbas said to him: {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate} is a verse of the Qur'an? He said: Yes."
"3690","240 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: My father informed me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed him, saying to him: {And We gave you seven of the oft-repeated} - he said: It is the Mother of the Qur'an. My father said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr recited it to me {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate} until he finished it, then said: {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate} ... is the seventh verse. Sa'id ibn Jubayr said to my father: And Ibn Abbas recited it to me as I recited it to you, saying: {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate} is the seventh verse. Ibn Abbas said: Allah stored it for you and did not bring it forth for anyone before you."
"3691","Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father. 241 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Sami al-Kufi narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Abu Muhayyah Yahya ibn Ya'la, from his father, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I hold you back by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, saying: Beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments; when I die I shall precede you, and your appointment is at the Hawd - whoever comes to it will prosper. And people will come and be seized to the left, and I shall say: O Lord, my nation! It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you, apostatizing upon their heels. It was narrated in the two Sahihs from the narration of Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - mentioning the end of this hadith, without the mention of what is at its beginning."
"3692","Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 242 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Fudayli informed them; Muhallim ... al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz - he is Ibn Muhammad - narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: We did not know the end of a surah except by: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"3693","Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah al-Zarrad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 243 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us; Abu Ubayd Allah Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {And their father was righteous} - he said: He preserved them by their father's righteousness; he did not mention any righteousness of theirs."
"3694","Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 244 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People will dye with black at the end of time, like the crops of pigeons; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"3695","245 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them; the noble Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us; he said: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Sukkari informed us; Ahmad - he is Ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi - narrated to us; Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There will be at the end of time people who dye with this black, like the crops of pigeons; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"3696","246 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Husayn and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us; both said: Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ibn Jubayr. Ahmad said: From Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will be people at the end of time who dye with this black. Husayn said: Like the crops of pigeons; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Tawbah al-Rabi'. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd al-Halabi - both from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi."
"3697","Uthman ibn al-Aswad ibn Musa ibn Badhan al-Makki, freedman of Banu Jumah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 247 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to me; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muqri al-Baghdadi narrated to me; Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us; Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us; Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {Have you seen al-Lat and al-Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other} - those are the exalted cranes, and their intercession is hoped for ... The idolaters rejoiced at that and said: He has mentioned our gods. Jibril came to him and said: Recite to me what I brought you. He said: He recited: {Have you seen al-Lat and al-Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other} - those are the exalted cranes, and their intercession is hoped for. He said: I did not bring you this; this is from Satan - or he said: this is of Satan; I did not bring it to you. Then Allah revealed: {We did not send before you any messenger or prophet but that when he wished, Satan cast into his wish} to the end of the verse."
"3698","Uthman ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 248 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - informed us that the chief Abu Muhammad Hamzah ibn al-Abbas ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Alawi al-Husayni informed them while he was present; Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Makfuf narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sharik ibn al-Fadl al-Asadi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus al-Yarbu'i narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim; Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: You see a man walking in the markets while his name has been raised among the dead. Then he recited: {We sent it down on a blessed night} to His saying: {In it every wise matter is decreed} - on that night the affair of the world is decreed until its like the next year."
"3699","Uthman ibn Abi Zar'ah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 249 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo - informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zar'ah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {Pour upon us some water} - he said: A man calls his acquaintance among the people of Paradise: Aid me, O so-and-so, for I have burned; and he says: {Allah has forbidden them both to the disbelievers}."
"3700","Uthman ibn Asim Abu Husayn, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 250 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo - informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafi'i informed us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {And there is none of the People of the Book but will believe in him before his death} - he said: Before the death of Isa, peace be upon him."
"3701","Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 251 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sibt - at Baghdad - informed us that his father Abu Ali al-Hasan informed them; he said: My father Abu Sa'd al-Muzaffar informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nubakhti informed us - at Baghdad - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mubashshir narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us; Hushaym informed us, from Shu'bah, from Adi ibn Thabit; Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."
"3702","252 - Abu al-Hasan al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi at Naysabur informed us that Fatimah bint Ali ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Za'bal informed us; Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Ghafir ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghafir informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan al-Yashkuri al-Wasiti narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."
"3703","253 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi - at Baghdad - informed us that his father Abu Mansur Ali informed them; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us; Abd Allah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Ali - meaning Ibn al-Ja'd - narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse. Al-Baghawi said: Hushaym narrated it from Shu'bah ascribed (musnad)."
"3704","254 - And with it Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Amr ibn Awn narrated to us; Hushaym informed us, from Shu'bah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3705","255 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us of it that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever hears and does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."
"3706","256 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, raising it; he said: Whoever hears the call then does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse. Abu Dawud narrated it from Qutaybah, from Jarir, from Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Maghra al-Abdi, from Adi ibn Thabit. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan al-Wasiti. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan."
"3707","Another. 257 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: One of them raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Jibril, peace be upon him, used to stuff mud into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing he would say: There is no god but Allah."
"3708","258 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah have mercy on him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Had you seen me taking from the silt of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing mercy would reach him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah with his chain, similarly. And he narrated mentioning one of them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far."
"3709","Another. 259 - Abu Ali ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali al-Nasri informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them; Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi informed us; the judge Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad, known as Ibn al-Saffar al-Maliki, informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Fadl ibn Idris al-Samiri narrated to us - by dictation - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Adam ibn Sulayman, from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3710","Azrah ibn Thabit ibn Abi Zayd ibn Akhtab al-Basri al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 260 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us; Abduh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, and said: O you reciting talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, who is Shubrumah? He said: A brother of mine, or a relative of mine. He said: Have you performed Hajj for yourself? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubrumah."
"3711","261 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us; Abduh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Who is Shubrumah? He said: My brother, or a relative of mine. He said: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubrumah."
"3712","262 - Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Barri ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Nahwi informed us in his book. And my maternal uncle, the imam Abu Umar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us of it that Marshad ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed them; Yahya ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa al-Qassas informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Faraj al-Muhandis informed us; Abu Shaybah Dawud ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us; Abduh narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Who is Shubrumah? He said: My brother, or a relative. He said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Make this one for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubrumah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ishaq ibn Isma'il and Hannad. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr - all from Abduh ibn Sulayman. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Abduh. Al-Athram said: I said to Abu Abd Allah - meaning Ahmad ibn Hanbal - : The hadith of Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah - Abduh - meaning Ibn Sulayman - raised it. He said: That is a mistake; Abduh narrated it halted (mawquf), meaning upon Ibn Abbas, with nothing in it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Muhanna mentioned from Abu Abd Allah something similar."
"3713","Another. 263 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {And upon those who can bear it, a ransom of feeding a poor person} - he said: It was a concession for the very old man and the very old woman, while they could fast, to break fast and feed a poor person in place of each day; and the pregnant and nursing woman, when they fear. Abu Dawud said: Meaning upon their children. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"3714","Another. 264 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us by license, and my maternal uncle, the learned imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, informed us of it that Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Husayn al-Tammar, known as Ibn Sawsan, informed them; Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran narrated to us; Abu Ahmad Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas informed us; Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us; Hudbah narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pray witr with {Glorify}, {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One}; and when he finished he said three times: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy. Abu Dawud narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Harb, from Waki', from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id. He said: And Waki' was contradicted in this. Abu Waki' and Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas halted. And it was raised to us from the narration of Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id."
"3715","Ata ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Zayd al-Thaqafi al-Kufi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 265 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them; Abd al-Samad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi informed us; Umar ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Ghaylan narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a bowl of tharid was brought to him, and he said: Eat from around it, and do not eat from its middle; for blessing descends in its middle."
"3716","266 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl of tharid, and said: Eat from around it and do not eat from its middle; for blessing descends in its middle."
"3717","267 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us; Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl of tharid, and said: Eat from its sides and do not eat from its middle; for blessing descends in its middle."
"3718","268 - Abu Ja'far - also - informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When food is placed, eat from its edges and leave its middle; for blessing descends in its middle. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq and Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, from Sufyan; and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Shu'bah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Jarir, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, and said: A fair, sound hadith, known only from the hadith of Ata. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Khalid, from Shu'bah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn al-Mundhir, from Ibn Fudayl, from Ata, similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, from Khalid."
"3719","Another. 269 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to me; Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Jews disputed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Do you eat what we killed and not eat what Allah killed! Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."
"3720","270 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us; Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: The idolaters said: O Muhammad, why do you not eat what Allah slaughtered, while you eat what we slaughtered? Then Allah revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."
"3721","271 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar narrated to us; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Jews said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You eat what you killed, and do not eat what Allah killed. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi al-Basri, from Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, similarly, and said: A fair, strange hadith. And some narrated it from Ata, from Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disconnected (mursal). Imran ibn Uyaynah: Abu Hatim al-Razi criticized him, and he is a witness for others."
"3722","Another. 272 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When: {And do not approach the property of the orphan except with what is best} was revealed, they isolated the property of orphans until food spoiled and meat stank. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and: {And if you mix with them, they are your brothers; and Allah knows the corrupter from the reformer} was revealed. He said: Then they mixed with them."
"3723","273 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us; Abu al-Mughirah and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Allah revealed: {And do not approach the property of the orphan except with what is best} and {Those who consume the property of orphans unjustly} - the verse - he said: Whoever had an orphan with him went and isolated his food and drink from his own drink; surplus of his food was kept for him until he ate it or it spoiled and was thrown away. That was hard upon them, and they mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Allah revealed: {And they ask you about orphans; say: Reform for them is best} to His saying: {Allah is Mighty, Wise}. Then they mixed their food with his food and their drink with his drink. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi, from Muhammad ibn al-Salt, from Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, similarly. Al-Nasa'i also narrated concerning His saying: {Those who consume the property of orphans unjustly} from Amr ibn Ali, from Imran ibn Uyaynah, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib."
"3724","Another. 274 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Black Stone descended from Paradise whiter than snow; then the sins of the children of Adam blackened it."
"3725","275 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Affan narrated to us; Hammad informed us; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Black Stone is from Paradise, and it was whiter than snow until the sins of the people of idolatry blackened it."
"3726","276 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Black Stone was whiter than snow until the sins of the children of Adam blackened it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yunus, from Hammad. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Jarir, and said: A fair, sound hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub, from Musa ibn Dawud, from Hammad ibn Salamah, abridged: The Black Stone is from Paradise. End of the section; praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace."
"3727","The sixty-first part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant abundant peace. Remainder of the hadith of Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 277 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja al-Wa'iz - in Egypt - informed us that Abd al-Sabur al-Harawi informed them; Mahmud ibn al-Qasim al-Azdi informed us; Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Jarrahi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi narrated to us; Abu Isa al-Tirmidhi narrated to us; Qutaybah narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the two units after Asr only because wealth came to him and distracted him from the two units after Zuhr, so he prayed them after Asr, then did not repeat them. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said: A fair hadith. He said: More than one narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed two units after Asr, and this contradicts what was narrated that he forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets; and the hadith of Ibn Abbas is more sound, where he said: He did not repeat them."
"3728","278 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them; Ali ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu al-Sha'tha narrated to us; Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought wealth after Zuhr, and he distributed it until he prayed Asr, then entered the house of A'ishah and prayed the two units after Asr, saying: This wealth distracted me from the two units after Zuhr, so I did not pray them until now."
"3729","279 - Zahir informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the two units after Asr only because wealth had come to him and he was distributing it, so it distracted him from the two units after Zuhr, and he prayed them afterwards."
"3730","Another. 280 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us; Abu al-Abbas Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Bazzaz - at Baghdad - informed us; Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan - meaning al-Thawri. (Another chain:) 281 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Khabbaz - known as Qafak - al-Asbahani - there - informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Katib narrated to us; Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us; he said: Abu Amir al-Asadi narrated to me. (Another chain:) 282 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us - all from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There were kings after Isa, peace be upon him, who altered the Torah and the Gospel, and among them were believers who recited the Torah and the Gospel. It was said to their king: We find no insult harsher than the insult these insult us with - they recite: {Whoever does not judge by what Allah revealed, they are the disbelievers} - these verses, along with what they reproach us with in their recitation. Call them to recite as we recite and believe in it as we believe. He said: He called them and gathered them, offering them killing or abandoning recitation of the Torah and Gospel except what they altered. They said: What do you want with that - leave us. A group of them said: Build us a pillar, then raise us to it, then give us something with which to lift our food and drink, and we shall not come to you. A group said: Let us wander the earth and roam, drinking as beasts drink; if you overpower us in your land, kill us. A group said: Build us houses in the deserts; we shall dig wells and cultivate herbs, neither coming to you nor passing by you - and there is none of the tribes but has a close one among them. They did so, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And monasticism they innovated; We did not prescribe it upon them except seeking Allah's pleasure, but they did not observe it as it should be observed}. The others said: We shall worship as so-and-so worshipped, wander as so-and-so wanders, and take houses as so-and-so took - while upon their idolatry, with no knowledge of the faith they imitated. When Allah sent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none of them remained but few, a man descended from his hermitage, one came from his wandering, and the monastery-dweller from his monastery, and they believed in him and affirmed him. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {O you who believe, fear Allah and believe in His Messenger; He will give you two shares of His mercy}. He said: Two rewards for following Isa, for their faith in Isa ibn Maryam and affirming the Torah and Gospel, and their faith in Muhammad, peace be upon him, and affirming him. He said: {And He will make for you a light by which you walk} ... the Qur'an and their following the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: {So that the People of the Book} who resemble them {may know that they have no power over anything of Allah's bounty, and that bounty is in Allah's hand; He gives it to whom He wills; and Allah is Possessor of great bounty}."
"3731","283 - And with it Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us; Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn Abbas said concerning this verse: {And He placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy, and monasticism they innovated; We did not prescribe it upon them except seeking Allah's pleasure} - when there was the interval between Isa and Muhammad, peace be upon them both, there were kings over the Children of Israel who altered the Torah and Gospel, while people remained among them acting upon the command of Isa ... and he mentioned the hadith similarly. The wording is that of the hadith of Musa ibn Ishaq al-Asadi. The narration of Hamid ibn Muhammad - he did not write its copy. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, similarly."
"3732","Another. 284 - My maternal uncle, the learned imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu Zur'ah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir informed them - recited to him at Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham informed you; Abu Talhah al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah ibn Bahr al-Qattan informed us; Abu Abd Allah Ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Sa'id and Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us; both said: Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: Pride is My cloak, and grandeur is My garment; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I shall cast him into the Fire."
"3733","285 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus al-Dabbi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us; al-Muharibi narrated to us; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Grandeur is My garment and pride is My cloak; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I shall cast him into Hell."
"3734","286 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them; Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us; Muhammad ibn Zuhayr at al-Ubullah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us; Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, from Allah, Majestic and Exalted: Pride is My cloak, grandeur is My garment; whoever contends with Me for anything of them, I shall admit him to the Fire. Thus Ibn Hibban narrated it; and this indicates that Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj used to narrate it from two shaykhs, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi, and Allah knows best. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id."
"3735","287 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us of it that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Arubah narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Pride is My cloak, grandeur is My garment; whoever contends with Me for them, I shall cast him into the Fire."
"3736","Another. 288 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Hudbah narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by a pleasant scent, and said: What is this scent, O Jibril? He said: This is the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter. She was combing her when the comb fell from her hand, and she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: My Lord, your Lord, and your father's Lord. She said: Shall I tell my father? She said: Tell him. He said to her: Do you have a lord other than me? She said: My Lord and your Lord, who is in heaven. He said: He heated a copper cow for her. She said: I have a request to you. He said: What is your request? She said: That you gather my bones and my children's bones. He said: That is yours upon us, for the right you have upon us. He cast her children into the cow one by one; the last of them was an infant boy, who said: O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth. Ibn Abbas said: Four spoke while infants: the son of Pharaoh's hairdresser, the infant of Jurayj, Isa ibn Maryam, and the fourth - I do not remember it."
"3737","289 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Umar al-Darir Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us. (Another chain:) 290 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Ma'n Thabit ibn Nu'aym al-Huji narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us. (Another chain:) 291 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night in which I was taken, I found a pleasant scent and said: What is this pleasant scent, O Jibril? He said: This is the scent of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter and her children. I said: What is her story? He said: While she was combing Pharaoh's daughter, the comb fell from her hand and she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: No, but my Lord, your Lord, and your father's Lord is Allah. She said: Do you have a lord other than my father! She said: Yes. She said: Shall I inform him of that? She said: Yes. She informed him, and he called her and said: O so-and-so, do you have a lord other than me? She said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. He ordered a copper cow, and it was heated; then her children were taken and cast into it one by one. She said: I have a request to you. He said: What is it? She said: I wish you would gather my bones and my children's bones in one cloth and bury us together. He said: That is yours upon us. Her children kept being cast into the cow until it reached a nursing infant of hers, and she seemed to hesitate for his sake. He said to her: O mother, plunge in, for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. Ibn Abbas said: Four infants spoke: Isa ibn Maryam, the companion of Jurayj, the witness of Yusuf, and the son of Pharaoh's hairdresser. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Umar al-Darir. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Umar al-Darir in full, and from Affan ibn Muslim and Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad, similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sulay' al-Wasiti, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan, from Yazid ibn Harun; and al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hudbah - both from Hammad ibn Salamah, similarly."
"3738","Another. 292 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us; Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When: {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab} was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Abu Bakr with him. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: O Messenger of Allah, she is a foul-tongued woman, and I fear she will harm you - if only you would stand. He said: She will not see me. She came and said: O Abu Bakr, your companion lampooned me. He said: No, and he does not speak poetry. She said: You are truthful in my view. And she left. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did she not see you? He said: No, an angel kept shielding me from her with his wing. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"3739","Another. 293 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I never saw people better than the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they asked him only thirteen questions until he died, all of them in the Qur'an, among them: {They ask you about the sacred month}, {They ask you about wine and gambling; and they ask you about orphans}, {And they ask you about menstruation}, {They ask you about the spoils}, {And they ask you what they spend} - they asked only about what benefited them. He said: The first to circumambulate the House were the angels; and what is between the Stone and the Yamani corner are graves of prophets' graves - when his people harmed a prophet, he would leave from among them and worship Allah there until he died."
"3740","294 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I never saw people better than the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they asked him only about thirteen questions until he died, all of them in the Qur'an, among them: {They ask you about the sacred month}, {They ask you about wine and gambling; and they ask you about orphans}, {And they ask you about menstruation} - they asked only about what benefited them."
"3741","295 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Aquli informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them; Abu Ja'far ibn al-Muslimah informed us; Isa ibn Ali al-Jarrah informed us; Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Surayj narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The first to circumambulate the House were the angels; and between the Corner and the Stone are the graves of prophets - when his people harmed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would leave to Makkah and remain there until he died."
"3742","Another. 296 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi - at al-Harbiyyah - informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yunus narrated to us; Hammad informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, took Ibrahim, peace be upon him, to the middle Jamrat al-Aqabah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank; then he came to the farthest Jamrah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank. When Ibrahim wanted to slaughter his son Ishaq, he said to his father: O father, bind me so I do not shake and my blood spatters upon you when you slaughter me. He bound him; when he took the blade and wanted to slaughter him, he was called from behind him: {O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision}."
"3743","297 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us; Surayj - he is Ibn al-Nu'man - narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril took the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Jamrat al-Aqabah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank; then he came to the middle Jamrah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank; then he brought him to the farthest Jamrah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank. In this narration he mentioned the middle Jamrah."
"3744","298 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us; Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril, peace be upon him, took the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Jamrat al-Aqabah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank; then he came to the farthest Jamrah, and Satan appeared to him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles. When Ibrahim, peace be upon him, wanted to slaughter Ishaq, he said to his father: When you slaughter me, withdraw so I do not shake and my blood spatters upon you. He bound him; when he took the blade and wanted to slaughter him, he was called from behind him: {O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision}."
"3745","299 - And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us; Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show him the rites; Thabir split open for him, and he entered Mina, and he showed him the Jamarat; then he showed him Jam', and showed him Arafat. When he was at the Jamrah, Iblis followed him, and he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he sank; then he followed him until he mentioned Jamrat al-Aqabah, and he sank, and he left."
"3746","Another. 300 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When: {When Allah's help and victory come} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My death has been announced to me, that he will be taken in that year."
"3747","301 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid; Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When: {When Allah's help and victory come} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My death has been announced to me, that he will be taken in that year. Imam Ahmad added Yazid in his chain; perhaps Muhammad ibn Fudayl heard it from Yazid, then heard it from Ata, and used to narrate it from both, and Allah knows best. Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh narrated it in his Tafsir from Da'laj ibn Ahmad, from Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr, from Ali ibn Khashram, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, similarly."
"3748","Another. 302 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa al-Muqri - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah informed us; Abd Allah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us. (Another chain:) 303 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord a request, and I wished I had not asked Him. I said: O Lord, there were prophets before me - among them one for whom You subjugated the winds, and among them one who gave life to the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and shelter you, find you astray and guide you, expand your breast for you? He said: I said: Yes, O Lord. The wording is al-Baghawi's. In the narration of al-Tustari: There were messengers before me, among them - and with him: Did I not find you astray and guide you, find you poor and enrich you, expand your breast for you, and remove your burden from you? He said: I said: Yes, O Lord. 304 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib. Hammad ibn Zayd said: I think it is from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then he mentioned it - it and the first are one hadith - and he said: Their wording is one."
"3749","Another. 305 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr at Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Sami al-Kufi narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Sabbah al-Muzani - he is Ibn Yahya - narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you sneezes and says: Praise be to Allah, the angels say: Lord of the worlds; and when he says: Lord of the worlds, the angels say: May Allah have mercy on you."
"3750","Another. 306 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas. (Another chain:)"
"3751","307 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abu Isma'il Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Tirmidhi narrated to us. (Another chain:) 308 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Abd al-Khaliq ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Harith narrated to us; both said: Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sulayman, the prophet of Allah, peace be upon him, when he stood in his prayer place would see a tree growing before him, and would say to it: What is your name? It would say: Such-and-such; and he would say: What are you for? It would say: For such-and-such. If it was for planting, it was planted; if it was for medicine, it was recorded. While he was one day thus, a tree stood before him. He said to it: What is your name? It said: The carob. He said: For what have you grown - perhaps you are - ? It said: For the ruin of this House. Sulayman said: O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn, so mankind may know the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: He carved it into a staff and leaned upon it for a year while the jinn worked. He died while leaning, and the termite ate it, and he fell. Mankind knew the jinn {had they known the unseen, they would not have remained in humiliating punishment}. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to recite it thus. He said: The jinn thanked the termite and used to bring it water. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Isma'il al-Tirmidhi. The narration of Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz lost part of it."
"3752","Another. 309 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets prayed in the mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa - as if I see him, wearing two Qatawani cloaks, in ihram upon a Shanawi camel bridled with a fiber bridle, with two braids."
"3753","Another. 310 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Amr ibn Yazid Abu Burayd al-Jarmi informed us; Sayf ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us; Warqa narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prostration is upon seven bones: the two hands, the two feet, the two knees, and the forehead. And raising the hands when you see the House, upon al-Safa and al-Marwah, at Arafah, at Jam', when stoning the Jamarat, and when prayer is commenced. As for the mention of prostration, it was narrated in the two Sahihs from the narration of Tawus, from Ibn Abbas; we intended from it only the raising of the hands."
"3754","Another. 311 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Sa'd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us; my grandfather Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to me; my father narrated to me; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I was commanded with the tooth-stick until I feared for my teeth."
"3755","Another. 312 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Sulami - outside Damascus - informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - by license - and it was said to our shaykh: Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed you - recited to him while you listened, at Baghdad - Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us; both said: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; the judge Abu Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Does your Lord dye? He said: Yes, with a dye that does not fade - red, yellow and white."
"3756","313 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, does your Lord dye? He said: Yes, with a dye that does not fade - red, white and yellow."
"3757","Another. 314 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them. (Another chain:) 315 - The memorizer Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja al-Hanbali - at Isfahan - informed us that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them; both said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abbas ibn Hamdan narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, concerning His saying: {And if you are ill or on a journey} - he said: When a man has wounds in Allah's path, or sores, or smallpox, and he fears dying if he bathes, let him perform tayammum."
"3758","Another. 316 - Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us; Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {And do not approach indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is concealed} - he said: What is apparent: marrying mothers in Jahiliyyah; and what is concealed: adultery."
"3759","Another. 317 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought they were denied} - he said: The messengers despaired of their people's help, and their people thought the messengers had lied to them. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought they were denied} - light (without doubling)."
"3760","Another. 318 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi informed us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us; Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their backs, their offspring, and made them testify} - he said: He wiped his back at Dahna."
"3761","Another. 319 - And with it, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad} - he said: Kaf from Kafi (Sufficient), Ha from Hadi (Guide), Sad from Sadiq (Truthful), Ayn from Alim (Knower), and Ya from Hakim (Wise)."
"3762","Another. 320 - And with it, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {They are given to drink of sealed nectar} to His saying: {And its mixture is of Tasnim} - he said: Tasnim is the noblest drink of the people of Paradise; the near ones drink it pure, and it is mixed for the companions of the right."
"3763","Another. 321 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ahwazi narrated to us; Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim! Inform us about Sunday - what Allah created in it. He said: Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {Do you disbelieve in Him who created the earth in two days}. To His saying: {That is the Lord of the worlds}. He said: Allah created the earth on Sunday and Monday. They said: Then what? He said: Then Allah revealed: {And He placed firm mountains above it} to His saying: {For the questioners}. Then He decreed its sustenance on Tuesday and Wednesday. He said: Then what? He said: Then Allah revealed: {Then He rose to the heaven while it was smoke} to His saying: {The command of each heaven; then He decreed them seven heavens in two days} - Thursday and Friday. He said: Then what? He said: Allah knows best. They said: Inform us about Saturday? He said: Allah knows best. They said: But we know. Then he raised one leg over the other and rested. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah. Then Allah revealed: {We created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six days, and no fatigue touched Us}. So be patient, O Muhammad, over what they say."
"3764","Another. 322 - Abu Bakr Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Amir ibn Amir narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {And Musa chose seventy men of his people for Our appointment} to His saying: {And those who believe in Our signs} - when the tremor seized them, Musa supplicated, and Allah sent the seventy to him; when he supplicated, he made his supplication for those among them who believed in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and who followed Muhammad, peace be upon him."
"3765","323 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Adam narrated to us; Hibban narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Musa asked his Lord a request, and Allah gave Muhammad, peace be upon him - when the seventy burned, Musa, peace be upon him, said: {Had You willed, You would have destroyed them before, and me - will You destroy us} to His saying: {And decree for us in this world good and in the Hereafter}. Allah gave it to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Allah said: {My punishment - I afflict with it whom I will, and My mercy embraces all things} to His saying: {They are the successful} - meaning the nation of Muhammad, peace be upon him."
"3766","Another. 324 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us; Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When this verse was revealed: {You and what you worship besides Allah are fuel for Hell; you shall enter it} - the idolaters said: Isa, peace be upon him, is worshipped, and the sun, the moon and Uzayr are worshipped. Then Allah revealed: {Those for whom good has preceded from Us - they shall be kept far from it} - Isa and Uzayr, peace be upon them both."
"3767","Another. 325 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas: {And were it not for believing men and believing women} - he said: When they turned back the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (Another chain:)"
"3768","326 - Ibn Mardawayh said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Farisi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us; Abdan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: {And were it not for believing men and believing women} - when they turned back the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Whom you did not know, lest you trample them and a disgrace befalls you from them without knowledge, that Allah may admit into His mercy whom He wills - had they separated} - meaning: Had the disbelievers separated from the believers, He would have punished them with a painful punishment for killing them."
"3769","Another. 327 - And with it Affan narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: {He will give you two shares of His mercy} - he said: Whoever among the People of the Books reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon faith shall have two shares."
"3770","Another. 328 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed them; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us; Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali informed us; Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Ata, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: {And when they commit an indecency, they say: We found our fathers upon it} - he said: They used to circumambulate the House naked, and that is the indecency."
"3771","Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As al-Makhzumi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 329 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade silk that is solid and unmixed."
"3772","330 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk that is solid and unmixed."
"3773","'Ammar al-Duhni al-Bajali al-Kufi, freedman of al-Hakam ibn Nufayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 331 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding {His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth}: he said: It is the place of the two Feet, and the measure of His Throne cannot be estimated. Al-Tabarani narrated it thus in al-Mu'jam, and he narrated it in al-Sunnah with Muslim al-Batin added in the isnad."
"3774","332 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu 'Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding {His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth}: he said: It is the place of the two Feet, and His Throne cannot be estimated. Shuja' ibn Makhlad al-Fallas narrated it from Abu 'Asim, agreeing in mentioning Muslim, except that he raised it (to the Prophet)."
"3775","333 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali ibn 'Ali al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them; Abu al-Ghana'im 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ma'mun transmitted to us; Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi al-Khuttali known as al-Sukkari transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, he is al-Sufi, narrated to us; Shuja' ibn Makhlad al-Fallas narrated to us in his Tafsir; Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Allah's saying {His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth}: he said: His Kursi is the place of His two Feet, and the Throne, its measure cannot be estimated. Al-Sufi said to us: This is how he said to us: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked. I said: The mawquf (stopped at Ibn 'Abbas) is more correct, and Allah knows best."
"3776","Another. 334 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us; Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Humayd al-Kharrat, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {My Lord, make this a secure city and provide its people with fruits, whoever of them believes in Allah and the Last Day}: Ibn 'Abbas said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) had restricted it to the people, so Allah revealed {and whoever disbelieves} - meaning I too shall provide for them as I provide for the believers; would I create creatures and not provide for them? I shall grant them enjoyment {a little, then I shall drive him to the punishment of the Fire}. Then Ibn 'Abbas recited {To each, these and these, We extend from the gift of your Lord, and the gift of your Lord is not restricted}."
"3777","Another. 335 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salim narrated to us; Mu'afa ibn 'Imran narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Every tasbih (glorification) in the Qur'an means prayer, and every sultan (authority) means proof."
"3778","'Amr ibn Dinar al-Athram al-Qurashi, freedman of Musa ibn Badhan, freedman of Banu Jumah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 336 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Yahya al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib transmitted to us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Lu'lu'i transmitted to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi and Ibn al-Sarh said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. Qutaybah said: from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not recognize the end of a surah until 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' was revealed to him. And this is the wording of Ibn al-Sarh."
"3779","337 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us; Fuhayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he knew that the surah had been sealed, and he turned to the next one."
"3780","338 - And with the same isnad Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Qays, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Jibril (peace be upon him) would bring the revelation down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he said 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' he would open another surah."
"3781","339 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Zunbur narrated to us; 'Abd al-Majid ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas who said: When Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Qur'an, the first thing cast upon him was 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' [lacuna in the source]; when (he heard) 'the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' the second time, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that he had sealed the surah and opened the next one."
"3782","Another. 340 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Id al-Bayyi' narrated to me; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Harun ibn Ziyad al-Hinna'i narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Do not abandon reciting 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' for it is among the Seven Oft-Repeated about which Allah said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated and the Great Qur'an}."
"3783","'Amr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hamdani al-Sabi'i Abu Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 341 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them; al-Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us; he said: I read to Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Sukkari; Ahmad, he is Ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sughi, narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us; he said: Sharik informed us, from Mukhawwal, Muslim al-Batin and Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three rak'ahs: with {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}, in each rak'ah one surah."
"3784","342 - Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi and Abu 'Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal transmitted to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq transmitted to us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Mani' transmitted to us; Husayn, he is Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas (ha)."
"3785","343 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three rak'ahs (ha). 344 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Husayn ibn Muhammad and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said: Sharik narrated to us; and Hajjaj, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three: with {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Say: O you disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}. Their wording is one."
"3786","345 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ... and he mentioned the like of it."
"3787","346 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us; 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with {Glorify} and {Say: O you disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}, in each rak'ah one surah."
"3788","347 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Shabab ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three: with {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Say: O you disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Waki', from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr; thus he said: from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim. And he also narrated it from Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i both narrated it from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from Sharik. Al-Nasa'i also narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam, from Shabab ibn Sawwar, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, similarly. And from al-Husayn ibn 'Isa, from Abu Usamah, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Abu Ishaq. And from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Abu Nu'aym, from Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, and he did not raise it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Nasr ibn 'Ali, from Abu Ahmad, from Yunus; and from Ahmad ibn Mansur and Abu Bakr, from Shabab ibn Sawwar, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from Sa'id. Ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi mentioned that it is from Ahmad ibn Mansur Abu Bakr al-Ramadi alone, while in our audition copy it is: Ahmad ibn Mansur and Abu Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Shabab narrated to us; and Allah knows best what is correct."
"3789","Another. 348 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born in the Year of the Elephant."
"3790","349 - Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi in Damascus informed us that Hibah Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Akfani and 'Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath al-Sulami both informed them, both saying: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kattani transmitted to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman ibn al-Qasim ibn Ma'ruf transmitted to us; Abu al-Maymun 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Rashid al-Bajali transmitted to us; Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Nasri narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me; Hajjaj narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born on the Day of the Elephant."
"3791","350 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar transmitted to us. 351 - Al-Saydalani said: And Abu Muhammad Hamzah ibn al-'Abbas al-'Alawi transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn al-Qasim al-Khayyat narrated to us; both said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Sukkari al-Harbi transmitted to us; Abu 'Abd Allah Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi narrated to us; Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born on the Day of the Elephant."
"3792","Another. 352 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-'Askari narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn Yahya narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The noblest of surahs is al-Baqarah, and the noblest verse revealed is {Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer}."
"3793","'Amr ibn Murrah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Tariq al-Muradi al-A'ma al-Kufi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 353 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad, recitation to him while he was present, transmitted to us; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr, he is Ibn Muslim al-Khallal, narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Imran narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no hadd (prescribed punishment) upon a slave woman until she is fortified by marriage; then when she is fortified by a husband, upon her is half of what is upon free chaste women."
"3794","354 - Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja' ibn al-Fadl al-Hanbali in Asbahan informed us that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Sakuni narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us (ha). 355 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar narrated to us; both said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Imran al-'Abidi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no hadd upon a slave woman until she is fortified by a husband; then when she is fortified by a husband, upon her is half of what is upon free chaste women."
"3795","Al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab ibn Yazid ibn Ruwaym al-Shaybani al-Rab'i from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 356 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi, there, informed us that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them; 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani transmitted to us; Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Busti transmitted to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-'Ijli narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Khirash narrated to us; al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah as a habitual drinker of wine meets Him like a worshipper of an idol. Abu Hatim said: The meaning of this report is likely: whoever meets Allah as a habitual drinker of wine, deeming its drinking lawful, meets Him like a worshipper of an idol, due to their equality in the state of disbelief."
"3796","Fudayl ibn 'Amr al-Fuqaymi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 357 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hajjaj narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Fudayl ibn 'Amr, he said: I think, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu' (Hajj), whereupon 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Abu Bakr and 'Umar forbade mut'ah. Ibn 'Abbas said: What does 'Urayyah say? He said: He says: Abu Bakr and 'Umar forbade mut'ah. Ibn 'Abbas said: I see them about to perish; I say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and they say: Abu Bakr and 'Umar forbade!"
"3797","Al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, he is Ibn Nafi' ibn Yasar al-Farisi, and Abu Bazzah is Yasar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 358 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani, there, informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Mutayr al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Zayd, from 'Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Allah created was the Pen, and He said to it: Flow. It said: With what shall I flow? He said: With what is to be until the Day of Resurrection."
"3798","359 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us (ha). 360 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us; Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Zayd, from 'Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah created the Pen, He said to it: Write. So it flowed with what is to be until the establishment of the Hour."
"3799","361 - Abu Ja'far also transmitted to us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Zayd, from 'Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first thing Allah created was the Pen, so He commanded it and it wrote everything that will be. 'Umar ibn Habib is the Makki, trustworthy, and he is not al-'Adawi al-Basri."
"3800","Qatadah ibn Di'amah from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 362 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi transmitted to us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us; my father narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi' al-Dabbi, from Qatadah and Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying {And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears}: he said: They were sailors, meaning seamen, who came with Ja'far ibn Abi Talib from Abyssinia; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qur'an they believed and their eyes overflowed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps when you return to your land you will turn away from your religion. They said: We shall never turn away from our religion, so Allah revealed that about their saying."
"3801","Another. 363 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Hamid ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us; Surayj narrated to us; Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah and al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding {And the truth has come to you in this}: both said: In this surah. Abu Sufyan is Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Ma'mari al-Yashkuri; Ibn Ma'in deemed him trustworthy."
"3802","Another. 364 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi ... narrated to us; Isma'il ibn 'Umar narrated to us; al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding this verse {And those who disbelieve will not cease to be struck by a calamity for what they did, or it will alight near their home}: he said: It is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), {until the promise of Allah comes}: he said: The conquest of Makkah. Note: the copyist left the name of Yahya's father blank with dots (truncated transmission)."
"3803","365 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us; Hibban ibn Musa narrated to us; he said: Ibn al-Mubarak transmitted to us; Sufyan transmitted to us, from 'Asim, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Concession was given to the sick person in ablution by tayammum with earth, and he said: What do you think if he is afflicted with smallpox, what should he do?"
"3804","Kulthum ibn Jabr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 366 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam at Na'man, meaning 'Arafah, and brought forth from his loins every progeny He created, scattered them before Him like dust, then spoke to them directly, saying: {Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bear witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: Indeed we were unaware of this} up to His saying {the falsifiers}."
"3805","367 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim and Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Bazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir al-Sa'igh narrated to us (ha). 368 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us; both said: Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwudhi narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam at Na'man, meaning 'Arafah, and brought forth from his loins every progeny He originated, scattered them before Him like dust, then spoke to them directly, saying: {Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bear witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: Indeed we were unaware of this * Or lest you say: Our fathers associated partners before, and we were progeny after them; will You destroy us for what the falsifiers did}."
"3806","369 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwudhi narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam (peace be upon him) at Na'man, meaning 'Arafah, and brought forth from his loins every progeny He created, scattered them before Him like dust, all alike, and said: {Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bear witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: Indeed we were unaware of this}, the verse. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah, from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad, and Kulthum said: He is not strong, and his hadith is not preserved. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said in his book: Kulthum ibn Jabr Abu Muhammad al-Basri, father of Rabi'ah ibn Kulthum, narrated from Abu Ghadiyah, Muslim ibn Yasar and Sa'id ibn Jubayr; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Awn, Hammad ibn Salamah, 'Abd al-Warith, Marthad ibn 'Amir and his son Rabi'ah narrated from him. I said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Ma'in deemed him trustworthy."
"3807","Another. 370 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Rabi'ah ibn Kulthum ibn Jabr narrated to us, from his father Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The prohibition of wine was revealed concerning two tribes of the Ansar who drank until they became intoxicated and abused one another; when they sobered up, a man would see the mark on his face, head and beard and say: My brother so-and-so did this to me; by Allah, had he been compassionate and merciful to me he would not have done this to me. They were brothers with no rancor in their hearts, then rancor fell into their hearts, so Allah revealed {Wine, gambling, idols and divining arrows are but filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper * Satan only wants to cause enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer; will you then desist?}. Then some pedantic people said: It is filth, yet it is in the belly of so-and-so who was killed on the Day of Badr, and so-and-so who was killed on the Day of Uhud. So Allah revealed {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted}, the verse. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah, from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal."
"3808","Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn 'Ali ibn al-Qamus al-'Abdi al-Basri, judge of Marw, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 371 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Mihrabzud and Abu Mansur al-Fath Mansur ibn ... transmitted to us; [lacuna in the printed text: Sa'id ibn Sabiq]; Khalid ibn Humayd narrated to me, from Muslim ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The bite of an ant is harder upon the martyr than the touch of weapons; rather it is more delightful to him than a cool, delicious drink on a hot summer day. Note: there is a lacuna in the isnad as printed (flagged truncated chain)."
"3809","372 - Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abi Zayd ibn Hamad ibn Nasr al-Karrani, by ijazah, informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sabiq al-Saluli of al-Rashid narrated to us; Khalid ibn Humayd al-Mahri narrated to us, from Muslim ibn 'Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The bite of an ant is harder upon the martyr than the touch of weapons; rather it is more delightful to him than a cool drink on a hot summer day. The author says: Thus it is, and I deem it an error; the correct is: Muslim from Muhammad ibn Zayd, and Allah knows best."
"3810","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi Abu 'Awn al-Kufi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 373 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A delegation of Banu Asad came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke, saying: O Messenger of Allah, all of Mudar fought you while we did not fight you, and we are neither the fewest of them in number nor the weakest of them in might, and we have upheld your kinship. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr when he heard their speech: Do they speak thus? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Their understanding is little, and Satan speaks upon their tongues."
"3811","374 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Mus'ab transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Ma'bad transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr, he is Ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq, narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us; my father narrated to us (ha). Ahmad ibn 'Amr said: And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu 'Awn al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Banu Asad came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we embraced Islam and did not fight you, while the Arabs fought you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Their understanding is little, and Satan speaks upon their tongues. And there was revealed {They count it as a favor to you that they embraced Islam}. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Sa'id ibn Yahya; and from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Yahya, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, similarly. Perhaps '(from his father)' here is an error, and Allah knows best."
"3812","Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Tadrus al-Makki Abu al-Zubayr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 375 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Abu 'Uthman Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr al-Buhayri transmitted to us; Abu 'Amr ibn Hamdan al-Hiri, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to us; Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb transmitted to us (ha). 376 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad also informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; both said: 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your brothers were struck at Uhud, Allah placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that visit the rivers of Paradise, eat of its fruits, and shelter in lamps of gold suspended in the shade of the Throne; when they found the goodness of their food, drink and rest, they said: Who will convey from us to our brothers that we are in Paradise being provided for, so that they do not flinch at war nor lose interest in jihad. He said: Allah said: I shall convey from you to them. So Allah revealed {And never think those killed in the way of Allah as dead; rather they are alive with their Lord, being provided for}. In Hamid's narration the word 'green' is absent; the rest is the same. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah similarly. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili also narrated it from Abu Khaythamah, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah ibn 'Amr ibn Sa'id, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, without mentioning Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 'Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Yusuf ibn Buhlul, from 'Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq likewise. 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it in al-Musnad from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah like Abu Dawud's narration."
"3813","Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 377 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib transmitted to us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Lu'lu'i transmitted to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us; Musarrif ibn 'Amr al-Ayami narrated to us; Yunus, meaning Ibn Bukayr, narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck Quraysh on the Day of Badr and arrived in Madinah, he gathered the Jews in the market of Banu Qaynuqa' and said: O assembly of Jews, embrace Islam before there befalls you the like of what befell Quraysh. They said: O Muhammad, let it not delude you that you killed a group of Quraysh who were inexperienced and knew not fighting; had you fought us you would have known that we are the people, and you have never met our like. So Allah revealed concerning that {Say to those who disbelieve: You shall be overcome}. Musarrif recited up to His saying {a party fighting in the way of Allah} at Badr {and another disbelieving}."
"3814","378 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Da'laj ibn Ahmad and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: A freedman of the family of Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: These verses were revealed only concerning them, meaning Banu Qaynuqa': {Say to those who disbelieve: You shall be overcome and gathered to Hell, an evil resting place * There was a sign for you in the two parties that met}, meaning the companions of Badr among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Quraysh: {a party fighting in the way of Allah and another disbelieving}, up to His saying {Indeed in that is a lesson for those of insight}."
"3815","Another. 379 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah or Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: 'Adiyy ibn Zayd said: O Muhammad, we do not know that Allah revealed anything to a human after Musa. So Allah revealed {Indeed We revealed to you as We revealed to Nuh and the prophets after him} ... all the verses."
"3816","Another. 380 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Hannad narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr or from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Jews said: This world is but seven thousand years, and people will be punished on the Day of Resurrection for each thousand years of worldly days one day of the days of the Hereafter, and they are but seven days. He said: So Allah revealed {And they say: The Fire shall not touch us except numbered days} until {abiding therein}. Allah informed them that reward in good and evil is everlasting."
"3817","Another. 381 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to me; Sa'id ibn Jubayr, or 'Ikrimah, narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: When 'Abd Allah ibn Salam, Tha'labah ibn Sa'yah, Asad ibn 'Ubayd and those Jews who embraced Islam believed, affirmed and desired Islam, the rabbis of the Jews, the people of disbelief, said: None believed in Muhammad and followed him except our worst; had they been of our best they would not have left the religion of their fathers. So Allah revealed concerning their saying {They are not alike; among the People of the Book} up to His saying {of the righteous}."
"3818","Muslim ibn 'Imran, and it is said Ibn Abi 'Imran al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 382 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, recitation to him; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn al-Naqqur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Daqqaq transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Uthman, he is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us; Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given seven of the long oft-repeated chapters, and Musa (peace be upon him) was given six; when he cast down the Tablets, two were lifted and four remained."
"3819","383 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Abu Khaythamah narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given seven of the long oft-repeated chapters, and Musa was given six; when he cast down the Tablets, two were lifted and four remained. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it abridged from Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from Jarir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given seven of the long oft-repeated. And he narrated it from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"3820","Another. 384 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ishaq, he is Ibn Yusuf, narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was expelled from Makkah, Abu Bakr said: They expelled their Prophet! To Allah we belong and to Him we return; they shall surely perish. Then there was revealed {Permission is given to those who are fought because they were wronged, and Allah is Able to grant them victory}. So it was known that there would be fighting. Ibn 'Abbas said: It is the first verse revealed concerning fighting. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Sufyan ibn Waki', from his father and Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq, from Sufyan al-Thawri, and said: a hasan hadith. More than one narrated it from Sufyan without Ibn 'Abbas in it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Tarsusi, from Ishaq al-Azraq."
"3821","Another. 385 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us; Ayyub ibn Mansur al-Khurasani narrated to us; Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Iblis said: O Lord, You have clarified the provision of every creature of Yours, so wherein is my provision? He said: In that over which My name is not mentioned."
"3822","Another. 386 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them. 387 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; both saying: Waki' narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, would say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. The wording is one, except that Zuhayr said with {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}. Abu Dawud narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Harb, saying: Waki' was contradicted in this. Abu Waki' and Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, mawquf."
"3823","Another. 388 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three: reciting in the first {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, in the second {Say: O you disbelievers}, and in the third {Say: He is Allah, the One}. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Abi al-'Abbas, from Sharik."
"3824","Another. 389 - Abu Bakr Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them; Ahmad transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad, he is Ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Rawh narrated to us; he said: Ja'far ibn al-Hudhayl narrated to me; Ibrahim ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated}: he said: The seven long ones."
"3825","390 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad narrated to us; 'Isa ibn Ja'far al-Warraq narrated to us; Qabisah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"3826","Another. 391 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas; and Mis'ar, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding {Then I swear by the setting places of the stars}: he said: The Qur'an was sent down entire to the lowest heaven, then it came down in portions afterwards to the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"3827","Another. 392 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad al-Sabbagh informed us that Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi informed them, recitation to her; it was said to her: Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed you; Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated to us; Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' al-Hamdani narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {What is the matter with you that you do not expect dignity from Allah}: he said: What is the matter with you that you do not know the true measure of His greatness."
"3828","Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir al-Sulami Abu 'Attab al-Kufi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 393 - Abu al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them; Ahmad transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa transmitted to us; Da'laj ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur and another man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {the whisperer, the retreater}: he said: Man is born with Satan crouching upon his heart; when he comprehends and remembers Allah, he retreats, and when he is heedless, he whispers."
"3829","Minhal ibn 'Amr al-Asadi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 394 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani, there, informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris transmitted to us; Isma'il ibn 'Abd Allah known as Sammuwayh transmitted to us; al-Rabi' ibn Yahya narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person whose term has not come, and says seven times in his presence: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you, Allah will cure him of that illness."
"3830","395 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah transmitted to us (ha). 396 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; both said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Ubayd al-'Ijl narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Humayd, son-in-law of 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, narrated to us; al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters upon a sick person whose term has not come and says seven times in his presence: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you, he will be cured."
"3831","397 - Muhammad ibn Ridhah said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Abu al-Mu'afa al-Harrani narrated to us. 398 - And Ahmad ibn Fadhshah said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; Abu 'Aqil Anas ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us; Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who visits a sick person and says: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you, seven times, while there is delay in his term, except that it will be lightened for him. 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated it, adding in the isnad 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith between Ibn 'Abbas and Sa'id."
"3832","399 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' informed them; Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Qasim and Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah transmitted to us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb transmitted to us; 'Amr, he is Ibn al-Harith, informed me, from 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id; al-Minhal ibn 'Amr and Murrah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person he would sit at his head, then say seven times: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you; if there was delay in his term, he would be cured of that ailment. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid. And he narrated it from Abu Mu'awiyah, from Hajjaj, from al-Minhal, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn 'Abbas [Abu Mu'awiyah said: I think he raised it; Imam Ahmad said: And Yazid narrated to us] without doubting its raising, agreeing on the isnad; he narrated it from Yazid, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Minhal, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Rabi' ibn Yahya. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, saying: a hasan gharib hadith known only from the hadith of Minhal. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Busri al-Dimashqi, from Abu al-Nadr Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Faradisi, from Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, from Shu'bah, from Maysarah, from Minhal; and from 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Abu al-Nadr Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, from a man, from Shu'bah, from Maysarah, from Minhal; and from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Yazid Abu Khalid, from Minhal. And he narrated it in 'Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah also from Wahb ibn Bayan, from Ibn Wahb, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith; and from al-Hasan ibn Isma'il al-Mujalidi, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from al-Hajjaj, from Minhal, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, without mentioning anyone between them [lacuna]. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Harun ibn Ma'ruf and from 'Abd Allah ibn Salm, from Harmalah, both from Ibn Wahb, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, without mentioning Murrah in the isnad. Yazid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dallani Abu Khalid al-Wasiti: Imam Ahmad said: There is no harm in him. Abu Zur'ah said: He is truthful. Ibn Hibban said: Very mistaken, grossly deluded, contradicting the trustworthy in narrations; argument by him is not permitted. Imam Ahmad and Abu Zur'ah are more knowledgeable than Ibn Hibban. Shu'bah's narration from him strengthens his standing. Al-Minhal ibn 'Amr was deemed trustworthy by Yahya ibn Ma'in, and al-Bukhari narrated from him."
"3833","Another. 400 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' al-Hamdani narrated to us; Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us; 'Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three whose prayer Allah does not accept: a man who leads a people while they dislike him, a woman whose husband sleeps angry with her, and a slave who flees from his masters."
"3834","401 - Abu Ja'far also informed us, in Asbahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo, that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us, from 'Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three whose prayer Allah does not accept: an imam of a people while they dislike him, a woman who sleeps while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who shun each other. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hayyaj, from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi, like al-Tustari's narration. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Kurayb, ending with: and two brothers who shun each other."
"3835","Another. 402 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Da'laj ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: When Allah intended to raise 'Isa (peace be upon him), he came out to his companions from a spring in a house, his head dripping water, and they were twelve men. He said: Among you is one who will disbelieve after having believed in me; which of you will have my likeness cast upon him and be killed in my place, and be with me? A youth stood up and said to him: I. He said to him: Sit. Then he repeated to them, and the youth said: I. He said: Sit. Then he repeated to them a third time, and the youth said: I. He said: You are the one. So the likeness of 'Isa was cast upon him, and 'Isa was raised from a corner of the house to heaven. The seekers from the Jews came and seized the likeness, killed him, then crucified him. He said: And they split into three sects. One sect said: Among us was the servant of Allah and His Messenger as long as Allah willed, then Allah raised him to Himself; these are the Muslims. One sect said: Among us was Allah as long as He willed, then He ascended to heaven; these are the Jacobites. One sect said: Among us was the son of Allah as long as He willed, then He raised him to Himself; these are the Nestorians. The two disbelieving ones prevailed over the believing one, fought them and killed them. Islam remained obscured until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and Allah revealed {So a party of the Children of Israel believed}, meaning the party that believed in the time of 'Isa, {and a party disbelieved}, the one that disbelieved in the time of 'Isa, {so We supported those who believed} in the time of 'Isa, by the manifestation of Muhammad (peace be upon him), their religion over the religion of the disbelievers. Al-Nasa'i narrated it similarly from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3836","Another. 403 - Abu al-Fath 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Dubi informed them; Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi transmitted to us, from Khalid ibn Makhlad; 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: I was with Ibn 'Abbas at 'Arafat, and he said: Why do I not hear the people chanting talbiyah? I said: They fear Mu'awiyah. So Ibn 'Abbas came out of his tent and said: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk; for they have abandoned the Sunnah out of hatred for 'Ali."
"3837","Another. 404 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sari narrated to us; he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us (ha). 405 - He said: And Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; both said: Waki' narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Maysarah al-Nahdi, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {Did you not see those who left their homes in thousands, fearing death}: he said: Four thousand, fearing death, fleeing from it, until when they were at such-and-such place, Allah said to them: Die, so they died. Then a prophet among the prophets passed by them, supplicated to Allah, and He revived them. He said: They had fled from the plague, so Allah revealed {Did you not see those who left their homes in thousands}, the verse."
"3838","Another. 406 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Abu Bakr narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {And they followed what the devils recited over Sulayman's kingdom}, meaning the scrolls they buried, {and Sulayman did not disbelieve, but the devils disbelieved, teaching people magic}: Allah thus revealed his exoneration in this verse."
"3839","Another. 407 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us; Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us; Sufyan, he is Ibn 'Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {And when We raised the mountain above them as if it were a canopy}: he said: They were brought the Torah and told: Take it. He said: They had one eye to the mountain and one eye to the Torah, looking at the mountain fearing it would fall upon them. Ibn 'Abbas said: You will not see a Jew prostrating except that he prostrates upon his eyebrow."
"3840","Another. 408 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; Abu Musa narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: A man asked Ibn 'Abbas about {And His Throne was upon the water}: upon what was the water that day? He said: Upon the back of the wind."
"3841","Another. 409 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us that Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Mahmud al-Zawzani informed them, recitation to him; Imam Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Farra' transmitted to us; Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Shadhan al-Sukkari transmitted to us; Abu al-Layth Nasr ibn al-Qasim ibn Nasr ibn Yazid al-Fara'idi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: For Sulayman ibn Dawud (peace be upon him) six hundred thousand chairs would be placed; then the nobles of men would come and sit nearest him, then the nobles of jinn would come and sit next to the men, then he would call the birds and they would shade them, then he would call the wind and it would carry them, covering in a single morning a month's journey. He said: While he was traveling one day, he needed water while in a desert land. He said: So he called the hoopoe, and it pecked the earth and hit the spot of water. Then the devils came to the place and stripped it as a hide is stripped until they brought out the water. Nafi' al-Azraq said to him: O describer, what of your saying: the hoopoe comes and pecks the earth and hits the spot of water, yet how does it know this but not know the trap until it falls around its neck? Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Woe to you, decree veils sight."
"3842","Another. 410 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying {So We caused the earth to swallow him and his home}: he said: It was said to the earth: Seize them, so it seized them to their heels. He said: It was said to it: Seize them, so it seized them to their waists. It was said to it: Seize them, so it seized them to their necks. It was said to it: Seize them, so they were swallowed. Abu 'Awanah narrated it from al-A'mash."
"3843","Another. 411 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us; Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; Sayfi ibn Rib'i narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I spent the night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called for a coarse hair pillow for me and placed it under my head."
"3844","Another. 412 - Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad, may Allah have mercy on him, Makki ibn Abi al-Raja' in Asbahan narrated to us that Abu al-Mutahhar al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed them; 'Umar ibn Ahmad al-Simsar transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Milah transmitted to us; Abu 'Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Madini transmitted to us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us; 'Aththam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When Musa (peace be upon him) left Egypt for Madyan, between them eight nights, he said: about the distance from Basra to Kufa. He said: He had no food except tree leaves; he left barefoot, and did not reach it until the soles of his feet were worn."
"3845","Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, freedman of the family of Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah al-Kufi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 413 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Jarbadhqani informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Bundar narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Imran narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding {Woe to you, and woe}: he said: Abu Jahl ibn Hisham."
"3846","Yahya ibn 'Abbad, and it is said Ibn 'Umarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 414 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad al-Mu'adhdhin al-Sabbagh in Asbahan informed us that Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi informed them; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi transmitted to us; Ja'far ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated to us; Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' al-Hamdani narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Abu Talib fell ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him while they sat around him, with an empty seat at his head. Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. Abu Talib said: O son of my brother, why does your people complain of you? He said: O uncle, I invite them to a word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay jizyah to them for it. He said: What is it? He said: There is no god but Allah. They stood saying {We never heard of this in the latter religion; this is but fabrication}. And the Qur'an was revealed: {Sad, by the Qur'an full of reminder}, full of honor, {Rather those who disbelieve are in pride and dissension}, up to His saying {Has he made the gods one God?}."
"3847","415 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn so-and-so, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Abu Talib fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began visiting him, with a man's seat at his head. Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. They complained of him to Abu Talib, saying: He reviles our gods. He said: O son of my brother, what do you want with these? He said: O uncle, I only invite them to a word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay jizyah to them for it. He said: And what is it? He said: There is no god but Allah. He said: {Has he made the gods one God? Indeed this is a wondrous thing}."
"3848","416 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan; Sulayman, meaning al-A'mash, narrated to me, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Abu Talib fell ill, so Quraysh came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him, with a man's seat at his head. Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. They said: Your nephew reviles our gods. He said: What is the matter with your people complaining of you? He said: O uncle, I invite them to a single word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay jizyah to them. He said: What is it? He said: There is no god but Allah. They stood saying {Has he made the gods one God?}. And there was revealed {Sad, by the Qur'an}. He recited until he reached {Indeed this is a wondrous thing}. 'Abd Allah said: My father said: And Abu Usamah narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us; 'Abbad narrated to us, mentioning similarly. My father said: And al-Ashja'i said: Yahya ibn 'Abbad."
"3849","417 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to us; Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us; he said: I heard al-A'mash; 'Abbad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When Abu Talib fell ill, a group of Quraysh entered upon him, among them Abu Jahl, saying: O Abu Talib, your nephew reviles our gods, says such-and-such, does such-and-such; send for him and forbid him. Abu Talib sent for him; near Abu Talib was a man's place, and he feared that if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon his uncle he would be gentler to him, so he jumped and sat in that seat. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and found no seat except by the door, he sat. Abu Talib said to him: O son of my brother, your people complain of you, claiming you revile their gods and say and do such-and-such. He said: O uncle, I only invite them to a single word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay jizyah to them for it. They said: And what is it, yes, by your father, and ten? He said: There is no god but Allah. They stood shaking their garments, saying {Has he made the gods one God? Indeed this is a wondrous thing}. Then he recited until he reached {before they taste punishment}. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan and 'Abd ibn Humayd, from Abu Ahmad, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya; 'Abd said: he is Ibn 'Abbad, from Sa'id. And from Bundar, from Yahya, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, saying: a hasan hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Bundar, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya, from Sa'id; and from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, from Yahya, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah; and from al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Habib al-Kirmani, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Abu Usamah, from al-A'mash; 'Abbad narrated to us, from Sa'id, similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Musaddad, from Yahya, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah."
"3850","Another. 418 - Imam Abu 'Ubayd Allah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghanim al-Asbahani, there, informed us that Abu al-Mutahhar al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani; 'Umar ibn Ahmad al-Simsar transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Milah transmitted to us; Abu 'Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah al-Razi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sa'id, he is Ibn Sabiq, narrated to me; 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he would never abandon: O Allah, make me content with what You have provided me, bless me in it, and succeed me in every absent matter of mine with good."
"3851","419 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi in Damascus informed us that his grandfather, Hafiz Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, informed them; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Ishaq transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sunni al-Dinawari narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Jammal informed me; Muhammad ibn 'Ammar al-Razi narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah al-Dashtaki narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, make me content with what You have provided me and bless me in it, and succeed me in every absent matter of mine with good."
"3852","And among the kunyas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: Abu Sinan, whose name is Dirar ibn Murrah al-Shaybani al-Kufi, from Sa'id. 420 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi transmitted to us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas transmitted to us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli transmitted to us; Abu 'Ubayd Allah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us; Sufyan, he is Ibn 'Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas that a man died a Christian, leaving a Muslim son who did not attend him. Ibn 'Abbas said: What would be wrong had he washed him, shrouded him and supplicated for him while he was alive? And he recited {And Ibrahim's seeking forgiveness for his father was only due to a promise he had made him; when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of Allah, he dissociated from him}. He said: When he died upon disbelief."
"3853","Another. 421 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; Da'laj, Ahmad ibn Kamil and 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari transmitted to us; Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us; Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Abu Sinan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying {And We did not send you except as a mercy to the worlds}: he said: Whoever believes in him, mercy is completed for him in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever disbelieves in him, the punishment with which nations were punished is averted from him, meaning in this world."
"3854","422 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in elevated form that 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them while both were present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Abu 'Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sawwaf transmitted to us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us; Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us; Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Abu Sinan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying {And We did not send you except as a mercy to the worlds}: he said: Whoever believes in him, mercy is completed in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever disbelieves, the punishment with which nations were punished is averted from him."
"3855","Abu Mu'awiyah al-Bajali, he is 'Ammar ibn Mu'awiyah, and it is said Ibn Abi Mu'awiyah, and it is said Ibn Hubab, and it is said Ibn Salih al-Duhni al-Bajali al-Kufi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 423 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Abu Tahir Sahl ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Abu Sakhr informed me, from Abu Mu'awiyah al-Bajali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: While I and Mujahid sat with Ibn 'Abbas, a man came and stood at his head, saying: O Abu 'Abbas, or O Abu al-Fadl, will you not give me a fatwa about the verse of menstruation? He said: Yes, and recited {And they ask you about menstruation; say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation}, the verse. Ibn 'Abbas said: From where the blood comes, from there you were commanded to approach. The man said to him: O Abu al-Fadl, what of the verse that follows it: {Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish}? He said: Fie upon you, is there tilth in the anus? Had what you say been true, menstruation would be abrogated: when occupied from here, you would come from there. Rather, if you wish by night or day. Abu Sakhr is Humayd, and it is said Ibn Sakhr al-Kharrat al-Madini; Muslim transmitted from him in his Sahih."
"3856","Abu Hashim al-Rummani, his name Yahya ibn Dinar al-Wasiti, and it is said Ibn al-Aswad, and it is said Ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. 424 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, meaning al-Hadrami, narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your women among the people of Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prolific, loving one who, when angered, says: My hand is in your hand; I shall not sleep until you are pleased."
"3857","425 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us; Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not inform you of your men of this world in Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, the Siddiq is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the child born in Islam is in Paradise, and a man in a distant town who visits his brother visiting him only for Allah is in Paradise. Shall I not inform you of your women among the people of Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prolific, loving one who, when angered or when he is angered, says: My hand is in your hand; I shall not sleep."
"3858","426 - And with the same isnad Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. We did not rely on the narration of Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti and 'Amr ibn Khalid. Al-Nasa'i narrated the mention of women from Hilal ibn al-'Ala', from his father, from Khalaf ibn Khalifah, similarly."
"3859","Sa'id ibn Shufi from Ibn 'Abbas. 427 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar, from Sa'id ibn Shufi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: People began asking him about prayer while traveling. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his family, he would pray only two rak'ahs until he returned to his family."
"3860","428 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Shufi; he heard Ibn 'Abbas say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, he would pray two rak'ahs."
"3861","429 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr transmitted to us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard Abu al-Safar narrating from Sa'id ibn Shufi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his house traveling, he would pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until he returned. Abu al-Safar's name is Sa'id ibn Yuhmid al-Hamdani. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hajjaj, from Shu'bah. Al-Bukhari narrated from the hadith of 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and stayed nineteen days shortening the prayer; so when we travel and stay nineteen we shorten, and if more we complete. Muslim narrated from the narration of Musa ibn Salamah ibn al-Muhabbiq, from Ibn 'Abbas: I asked Ibn 'Abbas: How should I pray when in Makkah if not with the imam? He said: Two rak'ahs, the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: And this is his wording, other than what we mentioned."
"3862","Sa'id ibn Abi Hind from Ibn 'Abbas. 430 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sulayman, he is Ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, narrated to us; Isma'il, he is Ibn Ja'far, transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind informed me, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For whomever Allah intends good, He grants him understanding in religion."
"3863","431 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Yazid, he is al-Qaratisi, narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim, he is al-Azraq, narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For whomever Allah intends good, He grants him understanding in religion. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from Isma'il, saying: a sahih hadith. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan."
"3864","Simak ibn al-Walid al-Hanafi Abu Zumayl al-Yamami from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas. 432 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; he said: Abu Zumayl narrated to me; he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Hudaybiyyah made peace with the polytheists, saying: O 'Ali, write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has made peace upon. They said: We do not know that you are the Messenger of Allah; had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Erase, O 'Ali, and write: This is what Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah has made peace upon. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah is better than 'Ali, yet he erased himself, and his erasing was not an erasure of prophethood. Have I come out of this one? They said: Yes."
"3865","433 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and others informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; Abu Zumayl narrated to me; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: When the Haruriyyah went out and secluded themselves, I said to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Hudaybiyyah made peace with the polytheists, saying to 'Ali: Write, O 'Ali: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has made peace upon. They said: Had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Erase, O 'Ali. O Allah, You know I am Your Messenger. Erase, O 'Ali, and write: This is what Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah has made peace upon. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah is better than 'Ali, yet he erased himself, and his erasing did not erase him from prophethood. Have I come out of this one? They said: Yes."
"3866","434 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Asbahan informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq (ha). 435 - Al-Tabarani said: And 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us; both, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar; Abu Zumayl narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to us, saying: When Harura' secluded themselves, being in a house apart (ha)."
"3867","436 - And [Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Mawazini informed us that Abu 'Ali] al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by ijazah; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud al-Nahdi narrated to us (ha). 437 - Sulayman ibn Ahmad said: Ishaq narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; both said: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Haruriyyah secluded themselves, I said to 'Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, delay the prayer that I may go to these people and speak to them. He said: I fear them for you. I said: Never, if Allah wills. He said: So I wore the finest of these Yemeni garments I could, then entered upon them while they rested at midday. I entered upon people never having seen people more striving than them, their hands like camels' knees, their faces marked from prostration. He said: I entered and they said: Welcome, O Ibn 'Abbas, what brings you? He said: I came to narrate to you from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); revelation descended while they are most knowledgeable of its interpretation. Some said: Do not narrate to him, others said: We shall indeed narrate to him. He said: I said: Tell me what you hold against the cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his son-in-law, the first to believe in him, while the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are with him? They said: We hold three things against him. I said: What are they? They said: First, he appointed men as judges in Allah's religion, while Allah said {Judgment belongs only to Allah}. He said: I said: And what else? They said: He fought yet took no captives nor spoils; if they were disbelievers their wealth was lawful to him, and if they were believers their blood was forbidden to him. He said: I said: And what else? They said: He erased himself from Commander of the Faithful; if he is not Commander of the Faithful then he is commander of the disbelievers. He said: I said: What if I recite to you from Allah's decisive Book and narrate to you from your Prophet's sunnah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you cannot deny; will you return? They said: Yes. He said: I said: As for your saying he appointed men as judges in Allah's religion, He says {O you who believe, do not kill game while in ihram}, up to His saying {judged by two just men among you}, and He said concerning a woman and her husband {And if you fear discord between them, appoint an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from hers}. I adjure you by Allah: is men's judgment in sparing their blood and lives and reconciling between them more rightful, or concerning a rabbit worth a quarter dirham? They said: O Allah, in sparing their blood and reconciling between them. He said: Have I come out of this one? They said: O Allah, yes. As for your saying he fought yet took no captives nor spoils: would you take your mother captive or deem lawful from her what you deem lawful from others? Then you have disbelieved; and if you claim she is not your mother, you have disbelieved and left Islam, for Allah says {The Prophet is closer to the believers than themselves, and his wives are their mothers}. You waver between two misguidances, so choose whichever you will. Have I come out of this one? They said: O Allah, yes. As for your saying he erased himself from Commander of the Faithful: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Quraysh on the Day of Hudaybiyyah to write a document between him and them, saying: Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon. They said: By Allah, had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you; rather write Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah. He said: By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah though you deny me. Write, O 'Ali: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was superior to 'Ali. Have I come out of this one? They said: O Allah, yes. Twenty thousand of them returned, and four thousand remained and were killed. The wording is one."
"3868","438 - 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan at Bab al-Basrah in Baghdad informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz transmitted to us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i transmitted to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Khalid Abu Thawr narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Yunus ibn al-Qasim al-Yamami narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; Abu Zumayl narrated to us; he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: When the Haruriyyah went out, I came to 'Ali, and he said: Go to these people. So I wore the finest Yemeni robes. Abu Zumayl said: Ibn 'Abbas was a handsome, loud-voiced man. Ibn 'Abbas said: I came to them and they said: Welcome, O Ibn 'Abbas, what is this robe? He said: What do you blame me for? I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the finest robes. This is Abu Dawud's narration."
"3869","439 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal narrated to us; Hamdan ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; Abu Zumayl narrated to me; Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the finest Yemeni garments. Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak, from 'Ikrimah. Al-Nasa'i narrated part of it in the story of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) treaty with the disbelievers of Quraysh, from 'Amr ibn 'Ali, from Ibn Mahdi, similarly."
"3870","Another. 440 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu 'Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi transmitted to us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas in Makkah transmitted to us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us; Abu 'Ubayd Allah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us; Sufyan, he is Ibn 'Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Simak al-Hanafi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Between the first of al-Muzzammil and its end was a year. He said: His saying {Indeed your Lord knows that you stand less than two-thirds of the night and half}, the verse. He said: They would stand like the standing of the month of Ramadan until there was revealed {So recite what is easy of it}."
"3871","441 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Mis'ar narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: When the beginning of al-Muzzammil was revealed, their standing was like their standing in Ramadan, or nearly their standing in Ramadan, and between its beginning and its end was a year. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Shabbuwayh, from Waki', from Mis'ar, like Abu Nu'aym's narration."
"3872","Another. 442 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib transmitted to us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i transmitted to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us; 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ikrimah, meaning Ibn 'Ammar, narrated to us; he said: And Abu Zumayl narrated to us; he said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas, saying: What is something I find in my chest? He said: What is it? I said: By Allah, I shall not utter it. He said: He said to me: Something of doubt? He said: And he laughed. He said: None escaped that. He said: Until Allah revealed {So if you are in doubt about what We revealed to you, ask those who read the Book before you}, the verse. He said: He said to me: When you find something in yourself, say {He is the First and the Last, the Manifest and the Hidden, and He is Knowing of all things}. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it in his Sunan."
"3873","Another. 443 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us (ha). 444 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us (ha). 445 - He said: And 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; they said: 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated to us; Simak al-Hanafi narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my ummah has two forerunners (children who died before him) die, Allah will admit him to Paradise. 'A'ishah said: And whoever has one forerunner die? He said: And whoever has one forerunner die, O Muwaffaqah. She said: And whoever has no forerunner? He said: Then I am the forerunner of my ummah; they shall never be afflicted with the like of me."
"3874","446 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us; 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated to us; Simak Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated to us; he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of my ummah has two forerunners, he enters Paradise. 'A'ishah said: By my father, what of whoever has one forerunner? He said: And whoever has one forerunner, O Muwaffaqah. She said: And whoever of your ummah has no forerunner? He said: Then I am the forerunner of my ummah; they shall never be afflicted with the like of me."
"3875","447 - Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi al-Qasim known as Ibn al-Tawilah informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed them; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari transmitted to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Khiraqi transmitted to us; Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn 'Umar ibn Musa ibn Zanjawayh al-Qattan narrated to us; Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us; 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated to us that he heard his grandfather Simak ibn al-Walid al-Hanafi say: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrate that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) [say]: Whoever of my ummah has two forerunners, Allah will admit him thereby to Paradise. She said: O Prophet of Allah, what of whoever of your ummah has one forerunner? He said: And whoever has one forerunner, O Muwaffaqah. She said: And whoever of your ummah has no forerunner? He said: Then I am the forerunner of my ummah; they shall never be afflicted with the like of me. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Nasr ibn 'Ali and Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Basri, from 'Abd Rabbihi al-Hanafi who said: I heard my grandfather, my mother's father, Simak ibn al-Walid narrate that he heard, mentioning it. And from Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Murabiti, from Hibban ibn Hilal, from 'Abd Rabbihi, mentioning similarly, saying: a gharib hadith known only from 'Abd Rabbihi's hadith, though more than one of the imams narrated from him. I said: 'Abd Rabbihi was criticized by more than one, while Imam Ahmad said: There is no harm in him, and 'Amr ibn 'Ali praised him."
"3876","Another. 448 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal narrated to us; Hamdan ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us; Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated to us; Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: The polytheists would say: Labbayk, no partner have You. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Woe to you, enough, enough. Then they would say: Except a partner belonging to You, whom You own and what he owns. They would say this while circumambulating the House."
"3877","Shurahbil ibn Sa'd al-Ansari Abu Sa'd al-Madani from Ibn 'Abbas. 449 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Fitr, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him, or he accompanies them, except that they admit him to Paradise."
"3878","450 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us, from Fitr; and Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Fitr narrated to us, from Shurahbil Abu Sa'd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has two sisters and treats them well enters Paradise. Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd said: He has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him, except that Allah admits him to Paradise."
"3879","451 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Ya'la narrated to us; Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Yahya, from 'Ikrimah who said: I sat with Zayd ibn 'Ali in Madinah when an old man called Shurahbil Abu Sa'd passed. He said: O Abu Sa'd, whence have you come? He said: From the Commander of the Faithful, to whom I narrated a hadith. He said: That this hadith be true is dearer to me than red camels. He said: Narrate it to the people. He said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him, or he accompanies them, except that they admit him to Paradise. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Fitr, similarly. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili. Discussion of Shurahbil has preceded. End of the juz', praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family with peace."
"3880","Shihab ibn Mudlij al-'Anbari from Ibn 'Abbas. 1 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya narrated to us, from Habib ibn Shihab; my father narrated to me; he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day he addressed the people at Tabuk, said: Among people there is none like a man holding his horse's head, striving in the way of Allah and avoiding people's evils, and like another dwelling in his livestock, honoring his guest and giving his due."
"3881","2 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Rawh narrated to us; Habib ibn Shihab al-'Anbari narrated to us; he said: I heard my father say: I and a companion of mine came to Ibn 'Abbas, and we met Abu Hurayrah at Ibn 'Abbas's door. He said: Who are you two? We informed him. He said: Let us go to people with dates and water; every valley flows according to its measure. He said: We said: May your good be abundant; seek permission for us from Ibn 'Abbas. He said: So he sought permission for us. He said: We heard Ibn 'Abbas narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the Day of Tabuk, saying: Among people there is none like a man holding his horse's bridle, striving in the way of Allah and avoiding people's evils, and like a man dwelling in his sheep, honoring his guest and discharging his due. He said: I said: Did he say it? He said: He said it. I said: Did he say it? He said: He said it. He said: I said: Did he say it? He said: He said it. He said: So I magnified Allah, praised Allah, and thanked."
"3882","3 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Habib ibn Shihab; my father narrated to me; he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among people there is none like a man holding his horse's head, striving in the way of Allah and restraining his evil from people, and like a man dwelling in his livestock, honoring his guest and giving his due."
"3883","4 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Junayd al-Sufi informed us in writing that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation to him; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; al-Muqaddami narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Habib ibn Shihab who said: My father narrated to me; he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the Day of Tabuk, saying: Among people there is none like a man holding his horse's head in the way of Allah and avoiding people's evils, and like another dwelling in his sheep, honoring his guest and giving his due."
"3884","Shahr ibn Hawshab al-Shami from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, discussion of Shahr having preceded. 5 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was forbidden categories of women except believing emigrant women. He said: {It is not lawful for you to marry women after this, nor to exchange them for other wives, though their beauty pleases you, except what your right hand possesses}. So Allah made lawful your believing slave girls, {and a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet}, and He forbade every woman of a religion other than Islam. He said: {And whoever disbelieves in faith, his work has perished and he is in the Hereafter among the losers}. And He said: {O Prophet, We have made lawful for you your wives to whom you gave their dowries and what your right hand possesses}, up to His saying {exclusively for you apart from the believers}. And He forbade other than that of the categories of women."
"3885","6 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was forbidden women except believing emigrant women. He said: {It is not lawful for you to marry women after this}, the verse, up to His saying {and a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet}. And He forbade every woman of a religion other than Islam. He said: {And whoever disbelieves in faith, his work has perished}, the verse: {O Prophet, We have made lawful for you your wives}, up to His saying {the believers}. And He forbade what is besides that of the categories of women. Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah married a Jewish woman, and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman married a Christian woman, so 'Umar grew severely angry until he nearly assaulted them. They said: We shall divorce, so do not be angry. 'Umar said: If their divorce is lawful, their marriage was lawful, but we shall take them away in humiliation and disgrace. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a slaughtered animal be hamstrung before it dies. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it (up to his saying: categories of women, similarly) from 'Abd ibn Humayd, from Rawh, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, saying: a hasan hadith known only from 'Abd al-Hamid's hadith."
"3886","Another. 7 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us; Abu 'Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us; 'Abd al-Jalil ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Awn. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn 'Amr ibn Nufayl (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3887","Another. 8 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali and Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah, who had children - she had five or six boys by a husband of hers who died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What prevents you from me? She said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, nothing prevents me from you that you are not the dearest of creation to me, but I honor you that these boys should clamor at your head morning and evening. He said: Has anything besides that prevented you? She said: No, by Allah, O Prophet of Allah, nothing prevents me from you that you are not the dearest of creation to me, but I honor you that these boys should clamor at your head morning and evening. He said: Has anything besides that prevented you? She said: No, by Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: May Allah have mercy on you; indeed the best women to ride camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, most tender to a child in infancy and most caring for a husband in his means. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a sitting of his, and Jibril came and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placing his palms upon the Messenger's knees, saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is Islam? He said: That you submit your face to Allah, testify that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said: If I do that, have I submitted? He said: If you do that, you have submitted. He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is faith? He said: Faith is to believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, the prophets, to be certain of death and life after death, to believe in Paradise, Hell, reckoning, the Balance, and to believe in decree, all of it, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that, have I believed? He said: If you do that, you have believed. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), tell me what is ihsan? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ihsan is to act for Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me when is the Hour? The Messenger of Allah said: Glory be to Allah; concerning five of the unseen none knows them but He: {Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, He sends down rain, knows what is in the wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die; indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware}. But if you wish, I shall inform you of its signs short of that. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, tell me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the slave woman give birth to her mistress or master, see sheep-herders vie in building, and see the barefoot, hungry poor as heads of people, that is among the signs and portents of the Hour. He said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the sheep-herders and the barefoot, hungry poor? He said: The Bedouins."
"3888","9 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Khalifah narrated to us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us; Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah, who had children - she had five or six boys by a husband of hers who died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What prevents you from me? She said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, nothing prevents me from you that you are not the dearest of creation to me, but I honor you that these boys should clamor at your head morning and evening. He said: Does anything besides that prevent you from me? She said: No, by Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: May Allah have mercy on you; indeed the best women to ride camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, most tender to a child in infancy and most caring for a husband in his means."
"3889","10 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of Quraysh called Sawdah, saying to her in his talk: Indeed the best women to ride camels are the women of Quraysh, most tender to a child in infancy and most caring for a husband in his means. His saying 'best women to ride camels' has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah. Muslim narrated it by way of Tawus and Hammam ibn Munabbih from him, and the rest of the hadith has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3890","Another. 11 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Husayn narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas said: A group of Jews came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Abu al-Qasim, tell us of traits we ask you about known only to a prophet. Among what they asked: Which food did Isra'il forbid himself before the Torah was revealed? He said: I adjure you by Allah who revealed the Torah to Musa (peace be upon him): Do you know that Isra'il, Ya'qub (peace be upon him), fell severely ill, his sickness prolonged, so he vowed to Allah that if Allah healed him of his sickness he would forbid himself his dearest drink and dearest food, and his dearest food was camel meat and his dearest drink their milk? They said: O Allah, yes."
"3891","12 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us; Ibn 'Abbas said: A group of Jews came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, saying: O Abu al-Qasim, tell us of traits we ask you about known only to a prophet. He said: Ask me what you will, but give me Allah's covenant and what Ya'qub (peace be upon him) took upon his sons: if I tell you something and you recognize it, you will follow me in Islam. They said: That is yours. He said: Then ask me what you will. They said: Tell us of four traits we ask you of? Tell us which food Isra'il forbade himself before the Torah was revealed? Tell us how is the woman's fluid and the man's fluid, how does the male come from it? Tell us how is this unlettered Prophet in sleep, and who is his guardian among the angels? He said: Upon you is Allah's covenant that if I inform you, you will follow me. They gave him what covenant and pledge he wished. He said: I adjure you by Him who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that Isra'il, Ya'qub, fell severely ill, his sickness prolonged, so he vowed to Allah that if Allah healed him of his sickness he would forbid his dearest drink and dearest food, and his dearest food was camel meat and his dearest drink their milk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. I adjure you by Allah besides whom there is no god, who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that the man's fluid is white and thick, and the woman's fluid yellow and thin, and whichever prevails, to it belong the child and resemblance by Allah's permission: if the man's fluid prevails over the woman's, it is male by Allah's permission, and if the woman's fluid prevails over the man's, it is female by Allah's permission? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by Allah who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that this unlettered Prophet's eyes sleep while his heart does not sleep? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. They said: Now tell us who is your guardian among the angels? Upon that we join or part with you. He said: My guardian is Jibril (peace be upon him); Allah never sent a prophet but he was his guardian. They said: Upon that we part with you; had your guardian been other than him among the angels we would have followed and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him? They said: He is our enemy. He said: Upon that Allah said {Say: Whoever is an enemy of Jibril, for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission}, up to His saying {they cast Allah's Book behind their backs as though they do not know}. Upon that {so they returned with anger upon anger}, the verse."
"3892","13 - And with the same isnad 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us, from Ibn 'Abbas, similarly."
"3893","14 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us; Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas who said: A group of Jews came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, saying: O Abu al-Qasim, tell us of traits we ask you of known only to a prophet? He said: Ask me what you will, but give me Allah's covenant and what Ya'qub took upon his sons: if I tell you something and you recognize it, you will follow me. They said: That is yours. They said: Four traits we ask you of: Tell us which food Isra'il forbade himself before the Torah was revealed? Tell us how is the woman's fluid from the man's, and how does the female and male come from it? Tell us how is this unlettered Prophet in sleep? And who is his guardian among the angels? He said: Upon you is Allah's covenant that if I inform you, you will follow me. They gave him what covenant and pledge he wished. He said: I adjure you by Him who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that Isra'il fell severely ill, his sickness prolonged, so he vowed that if Allah cured him of his sickness he would forbid his dearest drink and dearest food, and his dearest food was camel meat and his dearest drink their milk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides whom there is no god: Do you know that the man's fluid is thick, and the woman's fluid yellow and thin, and whichever prevails, to it belong the child and resemblance by Allah's permission: if the man's fluid prevails it is male by Allah's permission, and if the woman's fluid prevails it is female by Allah's permission? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by Him who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that this unlettered Prophet's eyes sleep while his heart does not sleep? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. They said: Now tell us who is your guardian among the angels? Upon that we join or part with you. He said: My guardian is Jibril (peace be upon him); Allah never sent a prophet but he was his guardian. They said: Upon that we part with you; had your guardian been other than him among the angels we would have followed and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him? They said: He is our enemy. Upon that Allah said {Whoever is an enemy of Jibril, for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission, confirming what is before it, a guidance and glad tidings for the believers * Whoever is an enemy of Allah}, up to {behind their backs as though they do not know}. Upon that {so they returned with anger upon anger}."
"3894","15 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, saying: A group of Jews came one day to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell us of traits we ask you about known only to a prophet. He said: Ask me what you will, but give me Allah's covenant and what Ya'qub (peace be upon him) took upon his sons: if I tell you something you recognize, you will follow me in Islam? They said: That is yours. He said: Then ask me what you will. They said: Tell us of four traits we ask you of: Tell us of the food Isra'il forbade himself before the Torah was revealed? Tell us of the woman's fluid and the man's fluid, how does the male come from it to be male, and how does the female come from it to be female? Tell us how is this Prophet in sleep, and who is his guardian among the angels? He said: Upon you is Allah's covenant that if I tell you, you will follow me. They gave him what covenant and pledge Allah willed. He said: I adjure you by Allah who revealed the Torah to Musa (peace be upon him): Do you know that Isra'il, Ya'qub (peace be upon him), fell severely ill, his sickness prolonged, so he vowed to Allah a vow that if Allah healed him of his sickness he would forbid his dearest drink and dearest food, and his dearest drink was camel milk and his dearest food camel meat? They said: O Allah, yes. The Messenger of Allah said to Allah: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides whom there is no god, who revealed the Torah to Musa: Do you know that the man's fluid is thick and white, and the woman's fluid yellow and thin, and whichever prevails, to it belong the child and resemblance by Allah's permission: if the man's fluid prevails over the woman's it is male by Allah's permission, and if the woman's fluid prevails over the man's it is female by Allah's permission? They said: O Allah, yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Him who revealed the Torah to Musa (peace be upon him): Do you know that this Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his eyes sleep while his heart does not sleep? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. They said: Now tell us who is your guardian among the angels? Upon that we join or part with you? He said: My guardian is Jibril (peace be upon him); Allah never sent a prophet but he was his guardian. They said: Upon that we part with you; had your guardian been other than him among the angels we would have followed and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him? They said: He is our enemy among the angels. So Allah revealed {Say: Whoever is an enemy of Jibril, for he brought it down upon your heart}, to the end of the verse, and there was revealed {so they returned with anger upon anger}."
"3895","Another. 16 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us; he said: Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (ha). Note: the matn (text) of the hadith is missing/truncated in the source after 'he said' (flagged truncated)."
"3896","17 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad transmitted to us; Sulayman al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us; Asad ibn Musa narrated to us (ha). 18 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; both said: 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: Any man who claims kinship to other than his parents or takes as patrons other than his patrons who freed him, upon him is Allah's curse and the angels' until the Day of Resurrection; no sarf nor 'adl (expiation or ransom) is accepted from him. The wording is one."
"3897","Another. 19 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us; Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a sanctuary, and my sanctuary is Madinah. O Allah, I sanctify it by Your sanctity: that no innovator be sheltered in it, its grass not be cut, its thorns not be lopped, and its lost property not be taken except by one announcing it. It is narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Yazid ibn Sharik ibn Tariq al-Taymi, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw 'Ali on the pulpit addressing; I heard him say: By Allah, we have no book to read except Allah's Book and what is in this leaf. He spread it, and in it were camel ages, matters of wounds, and in it ... the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is a sanctuary between 'Ayr and Thawr; whoever innovates in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is Allah's curse, the angels' and all people's; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor 'adl on the Day of Resurrection. The protection of the Muslims is one, extended by the lowest of them; whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is Allah's curse, the angels' and people's; Allah accepts from him neither 'adl nor sarf on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever takes patrons among a people without his patrons' permission. In al-Bukhari's narration ... and whoever claims kinship to other than his father or affiliates to other than his patrons, upon him is Allah's curse, the angels' and all people's; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor 'adl on the Day of Resurrection."
"3898","Another. 20 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Shahr narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to us, saying: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in his house's courtyard in Makkah, 'Uthman ibn Maz'un passed by him and smiled toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you not sit? He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat facing him. While he spoke to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze toward heaven, looked a while at heaven, then lowered his gaze until he placed it to his right on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned from his companion 'Uthman toward where he placed his gaze, nodding his head as though understanding what was said to him, while Ibn Maz'un watched. When he finished his need and understood what was said to him, the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gaze fixed toward heaven as it fixed the first time; he followed it with his gaze until it vanished in heaven. He turned to 'Uthman in his first sitting, saying: O Muhammad, in all my sitting with you and coming to you, I never saw you do as you did this morning. He said: And did you see me do it? He said: I saw you fix your gaze toward heaven, then place it until you placed it to your right; you turned to it leaving me, nodding your head as though understanding something said to you. He said: And did you notice that? 'Uthman said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A messenger of Allah came to me just now while you sat. He said: A messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: And what did he say to you? He said: Indeed Allah says {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, giving to kin, and forbids indecency, evil and transgression; He admonishes you that you may remember}. 'Uthman said: Then faith settled in my heart and I loved Muhammad."
"3899","21 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in his house's courtyard in Makkah, 'Uthman ibn Maz'un passed by him and smiled toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you not sit? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat facing him. While he spoke to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze toward heaven, looked a while at heaven, then lowered his gaze where he placed it to his right on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned from his companion 'Uthman toward where he placed his gaze, shaking his head as though understanding what was said, while Ibn Maz'un watched. When he finished his need and understood, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze until it vanished in heaven. He turned to 'Uthman in his first sitting, saying: O Muhammad, in all my sitting with you I never saw you do as you did this morning. He said: Did you notice that? 'Uthman said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while you sat. He said: A messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)!? He said: Yes. He said: And what did he say to you? He said: {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, giving to kin, and forbids indecency, evil and transgression; He admonishes you that you may remember}. 'Uthman said: Then faith settled in my heart, and I loved Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3900","Al-Salt ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Nawfal ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas. 22 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib transmitted to us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Lu'lu'i transmitted to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: I saw upon al-Salt ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Nawfal ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib a ring on his right little finger. I said: What is this? He said: I saw Ibn 'Abbas wearing his ring thus, with its stone on its back. He said: Ibn 'Abbas would hardly think but that he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore his ring likewise. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi, from Jarir, from Ibn Ishaq, saying: Muhammad ibn Isma'il (meaning al-Bukhari) said: Ibn Ishaq's hadith from al-Salt is a hasan hadith."
"3901","Suhayb al-Basri Abu al-Sahba', freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas. 23 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali ibn 'Ali al-Sufi in Baghdad informed us that his father informed them; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini transmitted to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us; Shu'bah transmitted to us from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, a man of Basra, from Ibn 'Abbas: Two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came running while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed until they seized his knees. Shu'bah said: What I retain from his mouth is (he parted between them), while in my book it is (he separated between them). He did not break his prayer. He said: I and a boy of Banu Hashim came upon a donkey, I think he said: We passed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed; we dismounted and entered prayer with him, and he did not break his prayer."
"3902","24 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came until they seized his knees, and he parted between them."
"3903","25 - And with the same isnad my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far and 'Affan narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb; I said: Who is Suhayb? He said: A man of Basra; from Ibn 'Abbas: He was upon a donkey, he and a boy of Banu Hashim, passing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, and he did not turn away. Two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came and seized the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knees, and he parted between them, or: separated between them, and did not turn away."
"3904","26 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present; Abu Nu'aym transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far transmitted to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb; I said: Who is Suhayb? He said: A man of Basra; from Ibn 'Abbas: He was upon a donkey, he and a boy of Banu Hashim, passing before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, and he did not turn away for that. Two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came and seized the Messenger's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knees, and he parted between them (meaning separated between them), and did not turn away for that."
"3905","27 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, a man of Basra, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I and a boy of Quraysh passed upon a donkey before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, and he did not turn away. Two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came and seized his knees, and he parted between them, and did not turn away."
"3906","28 - And with the same isnad Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us; Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Abu al-Sahba', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I came upon a donkey with a rider behind me of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in open land. We dismounted, then came until we entered prayer, leaving the donkey before them, and he paid no mind. Two slave girls of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came running, one chasing the other, until they reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer while he prayed, and he separated between them, paying no mind. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar who said: Ibn 'Abbas said, without mentioning Suhayb. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Abu 'Awanah, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Abu al-Sahba'. And from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Dawud ibn Mikhraq al-Firyabi, from Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, from Mansur, similarly. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abu al-Ash'ath al-'Ijli, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah. And Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from Yusuf ibn Musa, from Jarir, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, in the mention of the two slave girls. I said: As for Ibn 'Abbas's saying (I came upon a donkey), it is narrated in the Sahih; we intended only the mention of the two slave girls. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the hadith of Tawus, that Abu al-Sahba' said to Ibn 'Abbas: Bring of your oddities: was not triple divorce in the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr's time one? He said: It was so; then in 'Umar's time people persisted in divorce, so he enforced it upon them. We intended from this the meeting of Abu al-Sahba' with Ibn 'Abbas."
"3907","Tawus ibn Kaysan al-Yamani Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Janadi from Ibn 'Abbas. 29 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibah Allah informed them; al-Hasan transmitted to us; Ahmad transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yazid narrated to us; Husayn ibn Dhakwan transmitted to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, that Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The example of one who gives a gift then takes it back is like a dog that ate until full, vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"3908","30 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Asbahan informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; al-Muqaddami narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Habib al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift then take it back, except a father to his child. The example of one who gives a gift then takes it back, except a father, is like a dog that eats until full, then vomits, then returns to its vomit."
"3909","31 - And with the same isnad Ahmad ibn Abi 'Asim informed us; Isma'il ibn Salim narrated to us; Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"3910","32 - Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi in Asbahan informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal transmitted to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq transmitted to us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil transmitted to us; Ahmad ibn Mani' transmitted to us; Yazid and Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of one who takes back his gift is like a dog that ate until full, vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"3911","33 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur transmitted to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' transmitted to us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili transmitted to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Husayn al-Mu'allim transmitted to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus; he heard Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to give a gift then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The example of one who takes back his gift is like a dog that ate until full, vomited, then returned to its vomit. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Husayn al-Mu'allim. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Husayn, with its isnad, similarly. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam, from Ishaq al-Azraq, from Husayn, with its isnad, similarly; and from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Tawus who said: One who met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, mentioning it; and from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Hibban, from 'Abd Allah, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, with it, mursal; and from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad, from Makhlad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mursal. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Husayn, with the first isnad; his saying 'the example of one who takes back his gift...' to its end is narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Ibn 'Abbas, and from Tawus's narration from him also. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Husayn al-Mu'allim, with its isnad, from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas."
"3912","Another. 34 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us (ha). 35 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; both said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in blind partisanship or for a cause not clearly for Allah's sake, among them by a stone, whip or stick, his blood-money is that of manslaughter. Whoever is killed deliberately, retaliation applies; whoever stands between him (the killer) and it (retaliation), upon him is Allah's curse, the angels' and all people's; no sarf nor 'adl is accepted from them. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib, from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, with it; and from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd, from Hammad; and from Ibn al-Sarh, from Sufyan, all from 'Amr, from Tawus, saying 'whoever is killed'. Ibn 'Ubayd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said 'whoever is killed', mentioning it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Hilal ibn al-'Ala', from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, with its isnad; and from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from his brother Sulayman ibn Kathir, with its isnad, similarly, saying: he raises it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, from Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"3913","Another. 36 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Shadhan transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab transmitted to us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim transmitted to us; Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us; Salamah ibn Raja' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Humayd al-Qurashi, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man passed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having dyed with henna and katam, and he said: How fine this is! This is finer than that. Then another passed having dyed with yellow, and he said: How fine this is! This is finer than all of that."
"3914","37 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Asbahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah transmitted to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani transmitted to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us (ha). 38 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us. Hajjaj said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, and Ibn Raja' said: Muhammad ibn Talhah transmitted to us, from Humayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man passed him having dyed with henna, and he said: How fine this is! Then another passed him having dyed with henna and katam, and he said: How fine this is! Then another passed him having dyed with yellow, and he said: This is finer than all of that. Tawus used to dye with yellow."
"3915","39 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Asbahan informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah transmitted to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had changed his gray hair, saying: This is fine. Then he saw a man who had reddened his beard, saying: This is finer than the first. Then he saw a man who had yellowed his beard, saying: This is finer than all of that. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli, from Muhammad ibn Talhah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ishaq ibn Mansur, with the isnad, similarly."
"3916","Another, 40 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned wine, so a man said: O Messenger of Allah, we make a drink from this mizr (barley beer). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. Abu Dawud narrated it with the wording: Every fermented thing is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful, from Muhammad ibn Rafi', from Ibrahim ibn 'Umar al-San'ani, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Shaybah, from Tawus. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Abu al-Juwayriyah who said: We asked Ibn 'Abbas about badhaq (cooked wine), so he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preceded badhaq; whatever intoxicates is unlawful. He said: Upon you is the lawful good drink; there is nothing after the lawful good except the unlawful foul. And he did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"3917","Another, 41 - With it (the same chain to al-Tabarani): Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, 'Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever splits the unity of the Muslims, while the Muslims are in a firm united Islam, has cast off the bond of Islam from his neck. Al-Tirmidhi narrated (the hadith): Allah's Hand is with the congregation, from Yahya ibn Musa, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, and he said: We do not know it from the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas except through this route."
"3918","Another, 42 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not make ruqba (conditional life-gifts) of your properties; whoever gives something as ruqba, it belongs to the one to whom it was given as ruqba. And ruqba is that a man says: This is for so-and-so as long as he lives; if so-and-so dies it is for so-and-so. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Mu'awiyah and Ibn Numayr, both from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, similarly. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Wahb. And he narrated it through another route as mawquf upon Ibn 'Abbas. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Abi Ma'shar, from Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah."
"3919","Another, 43 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas (Ha)."
"3920","44 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ... And 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another. And al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar said: Like matrimony. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi. Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3921","Another, 45 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father (Ahmad ibn Hanbal) narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Zayd - narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas that a Bedouin gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift, so he gave him a return gift for it. He said: Are you pleased? He said: No. So he increased him. He said: Are you pleased? He said: No. So he increased him. He said: Are you pleased? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, or a Thaqafi."
"3922","46 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a she-camel as a gift, so he gave him a return gift for it. He said: Are you pleased? He said: No. So he increased him. He said: Are you pleased? He said: No. So he increased him. He said: Are you pleased? He said: Yes. He said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from an Ansari, a Qurashi, or a Thaqafi. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Salam, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il Ibn 'Ulayyah, from Yunus ibn Muhammad."
"3923","Another, 47 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashi'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: We, the company of the Prophets, were commanded to hasten the breaking of the fast, to delay the pre-dawn meal (suhur), and to place our right hands over our left in prayer."
"3924","Another, 48 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn 'Ufrah al-Bajali narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if there are a hundred conditions. It has a witness (corroboration) in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of 'A'ishah regarding Barirah and her emancipation."
"3925","Another, 49 - With it: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Muhammad ibn Quraysh al-'Anbari al-Basri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: {So no obscenity, no wickedness, and no disputing during Hajj}: Rafath is ... explicit lewd speech and alluding to women about intercourse; fusuq is all acts of disobedience; and jidal is a man's disputing with his companion."
"3926","50 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu 'Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ... in Makkah informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydullah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father who said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas about the saying of Allah Almighty: {So no obscenity and no wickedness}, he said: The rafath mentioned here is not the rafath which Allah Almighty mentioned in the other place. Then he recited: {Intercourse with your wives has been made lawful for you on the night of fasting}. So rafath here is intercourse, and there it is alluding to mention of intercourse, and in the speech of the Arabs it is al-i'rabah (explicit lewd talk)."
"3927","51 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi in Isfahan informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim who said: Ibn Tawus narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding this verse: {So no obscenity, no wickedness, and no disputing during Hajj}, he said: Rafath is al-'arabah (explicit talk) and alluding to women about intercourse; fusuq is all acts of disobedience; and jidal is a man's disputing with his companion. I consider the mawquf (stopped at Ibn 'Abbas) more correct than the marfu' (raised to the Prophet), and Allah knows best. Al-Bukhari narrated something like this as a suspended (ta'liq) report, saying: Abu Kamil said from Abu Ma'shar al-Barra', from 'Uthman ibn Ghiyath al-Rasibi, from 'Ikrimah, and it is a longer hadith than this, and this is in it. Abu Mas'ud al-Dimashqi said: I did not see it with anyone except Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj, and Muslim did not include it in his Sahih because of 'Ikrimah. In my view al-Bukhari took it from Muslim, and Allah knows best. I say: This is a mistake from Abu Mas'ud, for the hadith was also narrated from ... from Ahmad ibn Sinan, from Abu Kamil. And Ahmad ibn Sinan is among the shaykhs of al-Bukhari."
"3928","Another, 52 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Salamah and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas that Safwan ibn Umayyah came to Madinah, stood in the mosque and placed his khamisah (woolen cloak) under his head. A thief came and stole it, so he brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered that his hand be cut. Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah, it is his (i.e., I give it to him). He said: Why not before you brought him to me?"
"3929","Another, 53 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to me, from al-Zubaydi, 'Isa ibn Yazid narrated to us, that Tawus Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to them, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the 'Isha prayer one night until the people of the mosque had left except 'Uthman ibn Maz'un - who is among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and fifteen or sixteen men, not reaching seventeen. 'Uthman said: I will not leave tonight until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes out so I pray with him and know what his matter is. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out close to a third of the night, with Bilal, and saw no one in the mosque when he heard a murmur of their speech in a corner of the mosque. He walked to them until he greeted them, and said: What keeps you seated at this hour? They said: O Prophet of Allah, we waited for you to witness the prayer with you. He said to them: No nation before you ever prayed this prayer of yours, and you have remained in prayer since then. And he said: The stars are a protection for the sky; when the stars are effaced, there will come to the sky what it is promised. And I am a protection for my Companions; when I am gone, there will come to my Companions what they are promised. And my Companions are a protection for my nation; when my Companions are gone, there will come to my nation what it is promised. 'Isa ibn Yazid al-Shami: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him and did not mention any disparagement of him, and he is not Ibn Dabb."
"3930","Another, 54 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah Sammuyah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumambulation of the House is prayer, except that Allah Almighty has permitted speech in it; so whoever speaks, let him speak only good."
"3931","55 - With it: Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas (I know only that he raised it to the Prophet) who said: Circumambulation of the House is prayer, so speak little in it."
"3932","56 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas - raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Jarir and others said: He did not raise it - who said: Circumambulation of the House is like prayer except that you speak in it; and whoever speaks, let him speak only good. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Jarir, from 'Ata'. He said: It has been narrated from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas as mawquf, and we do not know it as marfu' except from the hadith of 'Ata'. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Yusuf ibn Sa'id, from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and from al-Harith ibn Miskin, from Ibn Wahb, both from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from a man who met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, and he did not name Ibn 'Abbas. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari, from Fudayl. Musa ibn A'yan narrated it from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas as marfu'."
"3933","Another, 57 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi there informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them, 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhai informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Zawzi informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani informed us, Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Weight is the weight of Makkah, and measure is the measure of Madinah. Thus Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book."
"3934","Another, 58 - Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Hamzah ibn 'Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi in Cairo informed us that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them - recited to him - Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan al-Bazzaz informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Harbi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Men were restricted to four wives because of the wealth of orphans."
"3935","Another, 59 - With it: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father who said: It was said to Ibn 'Abbas regarding this verse: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers}, he said: It is a disbelief, but not like disbelief in Allah and the Last Day."
"3936","60 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydullah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying Almighty: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers}, he said: It is not the disbelief that you think of. Hisham: a corroborating witness for others."
"3937","Another, 61 - Dawud ibn Ahmad ibn Mula'ib and Musa ibn 'Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih informed us that Sa'id ibn al-Banna' informed them, 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of a house called the bathhouse (hammam). They said: It cleans and benefits. He said: Whoever enters it, let him cover himself."
"3938","62 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Tawus and from al-Sakhtiyani, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of a house called the bathhouse. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt and benefits. He said: Whoever enters it, let him cover himself."
"3939","Talq ibn Habib al-'Anazi from Ibn 'Abbas, 63 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things: whoever is given them has been given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient upon affliction, and a wife who does not betray him regarding herself or his wealth."
"3940","64 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Abu 'Amr ibn Hamdan narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things: whoever is given them has been given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient upon affliction, and a wife who does not betray him regarding herself and his wealth."
"3941","Tulayq ibn Qays al-Hanafi al-Kufi, brother of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Ibn 'Abbas, 65 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali - both in Baghdad - informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, saying: Sufyan dictated it to me up to Shu'bah, saying: I heard 'Amr ibn Murrah, 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Mu'allim narrated to me, Tulayq ibn Qays al-Hanafi, brother of Abu Salih, narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: My Lord, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory against me, plan for me and do not plan against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, grant me victory over whoever transgresses against me, My Lord, make me grateful to You, remembering You, fearful of You, obedient to You, humble before You, oft-sighing and oft-returning to You, My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make firm my proof, guide my heart, make my tongue straight, and remove the rancor of my heart."
"3942","66 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan who said: 'Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, saying: 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, saying: Tulayq ibn Qays narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was (Ha)."
"3943","67 - With it: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id Abu Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: Sufyan narrated to me, saying: 'Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, saying: 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Mu'allim narrated to me, saying: Tulayq ibn Qays al-Hanafi narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: My Lord, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory against me, plan for me and do not plan against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, grant me victory over whoever transgresses against me, My Lord, make me oft-grateful to You, oft-remembering You, oft-fearing You, obedient to You, desirous toward You, humble before You, oft-sighing and oft-returning to You, My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, guide my heart, make firm my proof, make my tongue straight, and remove the rancor of my heart."
"3944","68 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed me that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us (Ha). 69 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Tulayq ibn Qays, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with supplications: My Lord, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory against me, plan for me and do not plan against me, guide me and make Your guidance easy to me, grant me victory over whoever transgresses against me, make me grateful and remembering to You, fearful of You and obedient, humble before You, oft-sighing and oft-returning, My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make firm my proof, guide my heart, make my tongue straight, and remove the rancor of my heart. This is the wording of al-Tammar. In the narration of Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: My Lord. And with him: and make guidance easy for me. And with him: My Lord, make me grateful to You, oft-remembering You, oft-fearing You, obedient to You, humble before You, oft-sighing and oft-returning, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, and the rest is the same. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Kathir, and from Musaddad, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud al-Hafari and Muhammad ibn Kathir al-'Abdi, separating them, from Sufyan al-Thawri, similarly, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the book The Practice of Day and Night from 'Amr ibn 'Ali, from Yahya, and from 'Imran ibn Musa, from 'Abd al-Warith, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, similarly, and he did not mention anyone between them. Ibn Majah narrated it from 'Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', from Sufyan. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, and narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Muhammad ibn Kathir al-'Abdi, similarly."
"3945","'Amir ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi from Ibn 'Abbas, 70 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih, Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, and Abu al-Jarud Mas'ud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli narrated to us, saying: 'Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to me, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah gives long life to dwellings through a people and gives them fruitful wealth, though He has not looked at them since He created them out of hatred for them. It was said: How is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Through their joining of kinship ties."
"3946","Another, 71 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Thabit ibn 'Abbas Abu Bakr al-Ahdab narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love you so much that I remember you, and were I not to come and look at you I would think my soul would depart. Then I remember that if I enter Paradise I will be below you in rank, and that distresses me, and I love to be with you in rank. The Messenger of Allah did not reply anything, so Allah Almighty revealed: {And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, those will be with those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor} ... the verse. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and recited it to him."
"3947","Another, 72 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Malij narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up one day and said: Is there any water? Is there any water? They said: No. He said: Is there a (worn-out leather) waterskin? So they brought the skin, it was placed before the Messenger of Allah, he placed his hand on it, then spread his fingers, and water gushed forth like the staff of Musa from the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Bilal, call the people to ablution. They came performing ablution from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the concern of Ibn Mas'ud was drinking. When they had performed ablution, he led them in the dawn prayer, then sat for the people and said: O people, which creation has the most amazing faith? They said: The angels. He said: How would the angels not believe while they witness the matter?! They said: Then the Prophets, O Messenger of Allah? He said: How would the Prophets not believe while revelation descends upon them from heaven?! They said: Then your Companions, O Messenger of Allah? He said: How would my Companions not believe while they see what they see! Rather, the people with the most amazing faith are a people who come after me, believing in me though they have not seen me, affirming me though they have not seen me; those are my brothers."
"3948","Another, 73 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying Almighty: {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun}, he said: When the sun passes its zenith. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except 'Uthman ibn 'Umar."
"3949","Another, 74 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi who said: Ibn 'Abbas informed me that 'Ali, al-Fadl, and Usamah entered the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Marhab informed me that they admitted 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, so it is as if I am looking at them in the grave, four. Al-Sha'bi said: Who tends to a man except his family?!"
"3950","Another, 75 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Yazid narrated to me, Kathir ibn Shihab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding this verse: {And recite to them the story of him to whom We gave Our verses but he detached himself from them}. He said: He is a man from the Children of Israel called Bal'am ibn Ba'ur. The Ansar used to say: He is Abu Lahab. And Thaqif used to say: He is Umayyah."
"3951","'Amir ibn Wathilah al-Laythi Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn 'Abbas, 76 - Abu 'Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah and his Companions performed 'Umrah from Ji'ranah, and they trotted (ramal) around the House three times and walked four."
"3952","77 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us with its isnad, the same, except that he said: from al-Ji'ranah."
"3953","78 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed 'Umrah from al-Ji'ranah and circumambulated the House walking. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Rawh, from Hammad, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed 'Umrah from Ji'ranah and trotted around the House three times and walked four circuits. Abu Dawud narrated it similarly from Musa, from Hammad, from 'Abdullah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Khuthaym, similarly. His hadith on the virtue of Makkah has preceded in the narration of Sa'id ibn Jubayr."
"3954","Another, 79 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, saying: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us (Ha). 80 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted around the House and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and they erred. I said: How did they speak truth and err? He said: They spoke truth; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did trot. And they erred; it is not Sunnah. Quraysh said at the time of Hudaybiyah: Leave Muhammad and his Companions until they die the death of naghaf (worms). When they made peace that they would come the next year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while the polytheists were on the side of Qu'ayqi'an, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Trot around the House three times, and it is not Sunnah. I said: And your people claim that he circumambulated between Safa and Marwah on a camel and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and they erred. I said: How did they speak truth and err? He said: They spoke truth; he did circumambulate between Safa and Marwah on a camel. And they erred; it is not Sunnah. The people would not be pushed away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor turned from him, so he circumambulated on a camel so they could hear his speech and his hands would not reach them. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith similarly."
"3955","81 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu 'Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House on a camel and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and they erred. He said: I said: How did they speak truth and err? He said: They spoke truth; he circumambulated on a camel. And they erred; it is not Sunnah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the people were not turned away from him nor pushed - so he circumambulated on a camel so they could hear his speech and their hands would not reach him. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith similarly. We intended from this hadith - even though it is mawquf, not musnad - that it is like commentary: His saying that Ibrahim (peace be upon him), when he was commanded with the rites, to its end. As for its beginning, something like it in meaning has been narrated in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn 'Abbas, and something like it has preceded as marfu' from the hadith of 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, except that he mentioned: When Ibrahim intended to slaughter his son Ishaq."
"3956","Another, 82 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Isma'il - meaning Ibn Zakariyya - narrated to us, from 'Abdullah - meaning Ibn 'Uthman - from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended at Marr al-Zahran in his 'Umrah, it reached the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Quraysh were saying: They cannot rouse themselves from thinness. His Companions said: If we slaughter from our riding beasts and eat of its meat and sip of its broth, tomorrow when we enter upon the people we will have vigor. He said: Do not do so; rather gather to me from your provisions. So they gathered for him and spread the leather mats. They ate until they turned away full, and each one stuffed his bag. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advanced until he entered the mosque, while Quraysh sat toward al-Hijr. He threw his cloak over one shoulder (idtiba'), then said: The people must not see any weakness in you. He touched the Corner, then entered until, when he disappeared behind the Yamani Corner, he walked to the Black Corner. Quraysh said: They are not content with walking; they are leaping like gazelles. He did that for three circuits, and it became Sunnah. Abu al-Tufayl said: And Ibn 'Abbas informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that in the Farewell Pilgrimage. We intended from this hadith the gathering of provisions and their eating from it. And I consider his saying that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that in the Farewell Pilgrimage was not mentioned in the Sahih from his hadith, and Allah knows best."
"3957","'Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Basri Abu al-Walid, relative of Ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Abbas, 83 - Abu al-Faraj 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Qasri in Baghdad informed us that Abu Shuja' 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Khalili informed us, Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuza'i informed us, Abu Sa'id al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Surayj ibn Ma'qil al-Adib al-Shashi informed us, Abu 'Isa Muhammad ibn 'Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two straps, doubled. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the book al-Shama'il. Ibn Majah narrated it from 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi, from Waki'. He has another hadith on visiting the sick, which has preceded in the biography of al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"3958","'Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Jarmi Abu Qilabah from Ibn 'Abbas, 84 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa with the same meaning narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn 'Abbas - I know only that he raised it - who said: When he (the Prophet) descended at a stop and the stop pleased him, he would delay Zuhr until combining Zuhr and 'Asr. And when he traveled and no stop was ready for him, he would delay Zuhr until reaching the stop, then combine Zuhr and 'Asr. Hasan said: When he traveled and descended at a stop."
"3959","'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-'Uqayli al-Basri from Ibn 'Abbas, 85 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take from the head while fasting - meaning kisses."
"3960","86 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take from the heads while fasting. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Sa'id, and from Isma'il, from Ayyub, from a shaykh of Banu Sadus who said: Ibn 'Abbas was asked about kissing for the fasting person, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take from the heads while fasting."
"3961","'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, son of the maternal aunt of Ibn 'Abbas, from Ibn 'Abbas, 87 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Dharr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us finds something speaking to himself; to be charred coal is dearer to him than to utter it. One of them (narrators) said: Praise be to Allah who could manage nothing of you except whispering. And the other said: Praise be to Allah who turned his matter back to whispering."
"3962","88 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi in Damascus informed us that Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad al-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Imam informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubdus ibn Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Dharr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a matter presents itself in my chest; to be charred coal is dearer to me than to utter it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah who turned his matter back to whispering."
"3963","89 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Dharr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us speaks to himself and alludes to something; to be charred coal is dearer to him than to utter it. He said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah who turned his matter back to whispering."
"3964","90 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Dharr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I speak to myself about something of the matter of the Lord; to be charred coal is dearer to me than to utter it. Shu'bah said: One of them said: Praise be to Allah who could manage nothing of you except whispering. And the other said: Praise be to Allah who turned his matter back to whispering."
"3965","91 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Dharr ibn 'Abdullah al-Hamdani, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I speak to myself about something; to fall from the sky is dearer to me than to utter it. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah who turned his plot back to whispering. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj, from Shu'bah, like the narration of Abu Dawud from Shu'bah. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from Jarir, from Mansur. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the book The Practice of Day and Night from 'Amr ibn 'Ali, from Ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-A'mash, and from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud, from Shu'bah, from Mansur and al-A'mash. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Qutaybah, from Jarir, from Mansur."
"3966","'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas al-Madani from his uncle 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, 92 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us that Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri and Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, saying: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, saying: My grandfather, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam who said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: We were sitting with Ibn 'Abbas, and he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did not single us out with anything to the exclusion of people except three things: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed donkeys upon horses."
"3967","93 - With it: Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, Musa ibn Salim narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas who said: Ibn 'Abbas said the same and added. Musa said: So I met 'Abdullah ibn Hasan and said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated to me such-and-such. He said: Horses were few among Banu Hashim, so he loved that they increase among them."
"3968","94 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam who said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: I met a man he named. He said: I said: If we entered upon Abu al-Fadl - meaning 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas - perhaps we would take something from him. He said: So we entered upon him, and I said to so-and-so, who was the boldest of us with him: Ask Abu al-Fadl: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: No. I said to him: Perhaps he recited secretly within himself? He said: Khamshan (scratching, i.e., nonsense); this is worse than the first. He was a commanded servant; he conveyed what he was sent with, and he did not single us out to the exclusion of people with anything except three: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed a donkey upon a mare. Musa said: So I met 'Abdullah ibn Hasan and mentioned it to him, and he said: Horses were few among Banu Hashim, so he loved that they increase among them."
"3969","95 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il narrated to us, Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, hearing Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a commanded servant; by Allah he conveyed what he was sent with, and he did not single us out to the exclusion of people with anything except three: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed a donkey upon a mare. Musa said: So I met 'Abdullah ibn Hasan and said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated to me such-and-such. He said: Horses were few among Banu Hashim, so he loved that they increase among them."
"3970","96 - With it: My father narrated to me, 'Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to us, saying: I and youths of Quraysh entered upon Ibn 'Abbas. He said: So they asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: No. He said: They said: Perhaps he recited within himself? He said: Khamshan (scratching, i.e., rubbish); this is evil. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a commanded servant; he conveyed what he was sent with, and he did not single us out to the exclusion of people except with three: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed a donkey upon a mare."
"3971","97 - Abu al-Ma'ali 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ali ibn Sabir al-Sulami informed us - recited to him while we heard in the year 576 in Damascus - it was said to him: al-Sharif al-Sayyid Dhu al-Sharafayn Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Abbas al-Husayni informed you - recited to him - Karimah bint Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwiyyah informed us, saying: Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Faqih informed us in Sarakhs, Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Saqami narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Hammad - he is Ibn Zayd - narrated to us, from Abu Jahdam, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah who said: I was with Ibn 'Abbas when a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: No ... no. He said: Perhaps he recited within himself?! He said: Khamshan (nonsense); this is worse than the first. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a servant whom Allah Almighty commanded with a command and he conveyed it. By Allah, he did not single us out with anything to the exclusion of people except three: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed donkeys upon horses."
"3972","98 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, Abu Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kaysan al-Nahwi informed us, it was said to him: al-Qadi Abu Muhammad Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed you. Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Jahdam narrated to us, saying: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me. He said: We were sitting with 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas among youths of Banu Hashim, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a servant whom Allah commanded with a command, and by Allah he conveyed what he was commanded with. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did not single us out with anything to the exclusion of people except three things: He commanded us to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed donkeys upon horses. Al-Tirmidhi narrated his saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not single us out to the exclusion of people with anything except three - from Abu Kurayb, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Salim, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And he said: al-Thawri narrated this from Abu Jahdam saying: from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, and I heard Muhammad saying: The hadith of al-Thawri is not preserved; al-Thawri erred in it. Al-Nasa'i narrated from it: He commanded us with perfecting ablution, from Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi, saying: Musa ibn Jahdam, but it is Abu Jahdam. More than one narrated it saying: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah, and some say: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Ubaydullah, and the correct is 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah as al-Bukhari said, and Allah knows best."
"3973","'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Mulaykah al-Taymi Abu Bakr al-Makki from Ibn 'Abbas, 99 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A partner has the right of preemption in everything. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yusuf ibn 'Isa, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Ibn Hamzah Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Sukkari, with its isnad, the same. And from Hannad, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash and Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal, saying: There is no Ibn 'Abbas in it, and nothing like this is known as marfu' except from the hadith of Abu Hamzah; the error may be from him. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Abu Hamzah, and from Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, from Isra'il, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah as mursal. I say: Nu'aym ibn Hammad has been criticized, and more than one of the people of knowledge declared him trustworthy, and al-Bukhari narrated from him."
"3974","Another, 100 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The dawn prayer was established, so a man stood praying the two rak'ahs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled him by his garment and said: Would you pray Fajr as four?!"
"3975","101 - With it: My father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The prayer was established and I had not prayed the two rak'ahs, so he saw me praying them and pulled me, saying: Do you intend to pray Fajr as four? It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"3976","102 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz al-Harawi there informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Abu 'Amir, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The prayer was established, so I stood praying two rak'ahs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled me and said: Would you pray the morning prayer as four?!"
"3977","103 - With it: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Salm ibn Junadah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The prayer was established and I had not prayed the two rak'ahs. He saw me praying them, forbade me, pulled me and said: Do you intend to pray Fajr as four? It was said to Abu 'Amir - meaning Salih ibn Rustum: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"3978","104 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The prayer was established and I had not prayed the two rak'ahs. He saw me praying them, pulled me and said: Do you intend to pray Fajr as four? It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we transmitted it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from 'Ali ibn Hamdun ibn Hisham, from Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi, from 'Uthman ibn 'Umar, from Abu 'Amir al-Khazzaz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, with its meaning."
"3979","Another, 105 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Tawbah al-Qazwini narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation will drink wine at the end of time, calling it by other than its name. Abu 'Amir Salih ibn Rustum: Yahya ibn Ma'in criticized him. Imam Ahmad said: Sound in hadith. Abu Dawud declared him trustworthy. Ibn 'Adi said: There is no harm in him. Muslim narrated from him in his Sahih. 'Affan ibn Sayyar al-Jurjani: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him and did not mention any disparagement of him. Isma'il ibn Tawbah al-Thaqafi: his origin from Ta'if, he resided in Qazwin, Abu Sulayman; Abu Zur'ah said: Truthful."
"3980","Another, 106 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us (Ha). 107 - al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar al-Barra' narrated to us (Ha). 108 - al-Tabarani said: And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to me, Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us - all of them from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3981","Another, 109 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us (Ha). 110 - al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, guard Allah and He will guard you, guard Allah and you will find Him before you, know Allah in ease and He will know you in hardship, know that what befell you could never have missed you, and what missed you could never have befallen you, know that if all creation gathered to give you something Allah did not will to give you, they could not do it, or to divert from you something Allah willed to befall you with, they could not do that, so when you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah, know that victory comes with patience, relief comes with distress, ease comes with hardship, and know that the Pen has already run with what is to be. This hadith has preceded in the narration of Hanash al-San'ani, from Ibn 'Abbas. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: 'Isa ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi is not strong."
"3982","Another, 111 - With it: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahib al-Harithi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin (Hawd) is a month's journey, its corners equal, its cups as numerous as the stars of the sky, its water whiter than snow, sweeter than honey, more fragrant than musk; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it. Nafi' ibn 'Umar al-Jumahi narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, the same. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from this narration, so perhaps Ibn Abi Mulaykah preserved it from Ibn 'Abbas and from Ibn 'Amr, and Allah knows best."
"3983","Another, 112 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri al-Razi informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Something is neither in the Book of Allah nor the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet you will find it among all people. It was said: What is it? He said: The inheritance of the sister with the daughter. Allah Almighty says: {If a man dies having no child but has a sister, she has half of what he left}, yet you give her half along with a child (meaning with a daughter)."
"3984","Another, 113 - With it: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying: {And we came with paltry merchandise}, he said: The worn-out sack, dates of poor quality, rope, and things. 'Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im: Imam Ahmad, Yahya ibn Ma'in, and Abu Zur'ah al-Razi declared him trustworthy."
"3985","114 - With it: From Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying: {And she certainly inclined toward him, and he inclined toward her}, he said: He sat with her as a man sits with his wife, and undid the waist-wrapper, then he was called: O son of Ya'qub, would you commit adultery and become like a bird whose feathers are plucked, then it tries to fly but has no feathers?!"
"3986","'Abdullah ibn 'Usm al-Nasibi Abu 'Ulwan from Ibn 'Abbas, 115 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Sharik ibn 'Abdullah al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Usm, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with fifty prayers, then he asked his Lord to make them five prayers."
"3987","116 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu 'Ulwan who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: Fifty prayers were obligated upon your Prophet, then he asked his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He made them five."
"3988","117 - With it: My father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Usm who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with fifty prayers, then he asked his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He made them five prayers."
"3989","118 - With it: My father narrated to me, Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Usm, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, obligated upon His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fifty prayers as prayer, then he asked his Lord and He made them five prayers. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, from Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Tayalisi. 'Abdullah ibn 'Usm: Ibn Hibban and Ibn 'Adi criticized him. Abu Zur'ah al-Razi said: There is no harm in him. And Abu Zur'ah is more knowledgeable than them, and Allah knows best. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih in the hadith of the Night Journey."
"3990","'Abdullah ibn Farrukh, freedman of the family of Talhah ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Taymi, from Ibn 'Abbas, 119 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the night prayer ('atamah) to a third of the night; for that it was called 'atamah, because he would enter the darkness of night with it."
"3991","'Abdullah ibn Qays from Ibn 'Abbas, 120 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abu 'Amr - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim - narrated to us, Abu Hatim narrated to us, Ibn Nufayl narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Qays who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying regarding this verse: {Among them are decisive verses}, they are the verses from al-An'am ... {Say: Come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden you} ... until he finished them."
"3992","'Abdullah ibn Musawir from Ibn 'Abbas, 121 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from 'Abdullah ibn Musawir who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas deeming Ibn al-Zubayr miserly, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one who sleeps while his neighbor is hungry (tawin: empty, hungry). In our hearing: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bishr, and the correct is Bashir, and Allah knows best."
"3993","122 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Musawir who said: Ibn 'Abbas said while deeming Ibn al-Zubayr miserly: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one who is satiated while his neighbor is hungry. In the first narration: 'Abdullah, and in this one 'Ubaydullah, and Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him under 'Abdullah nor 'Ubaydullah."
"3994","123 - [lacuna]. 'Abdullah ibn Abi Musawir narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one who sleeps satiated while his neighbor beside him is hungry."
"3995","'Abdullah ibn Matar al-Basri Abu Rayhanah from Ibn 'Abbas, 124 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Harun ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Abu Rayhanah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mu'aqarah (vain rivalry in slaughtering for show) of the Bedouins. Abu Dawud said: Ghundar stopped it as mawquf upon Ibn 'Abbas."
"3996","'Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Ibn 'Abbas, 125 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Adib Abu 'Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Imam Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydullah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan - he is Ibn 'Uyaynah - narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl who said: Ibn 'Abbas was asked, while I was sitting beside him: From how far did Ya'qub find the scent of Yusuf? Regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: {Indeed I smell the scent of Yusuf}. He said: He found it from eighty farsakhs. Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl said: That is like what is between Basrah and Kufah."
"3997","126 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abu 'Amr - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu Sinan narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying: {Indeed I smell the scent of Yusuf}, he said: He found his scent from about the distance of what is between Basrah and Kufah."
"3998","127 - With it: Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mula'ib narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying ... {And when the caravan departed}, he said: When the caravan left, a wind blew and brought to Ya'qub the scent of Yusuf, so he said ... {Indeed I smell the scent of Yusuf, were you not to deem me senile}. He said: Were you not to deem me foolish. He said: So he found his scent from a journey of three days. Abu Sinan - his name is Dirar ibn Murrah al-Kufi; Muslim narrated from him."
"3999","'Abdullah ibn 'Anbasah from Ibn 'Abbas, 128 - Abu al-Futuh Mas'ud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Karim ibn Ghayth al-Daqqaq at Bab al-Basrah in Baghdad informed us that Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed them, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ali ibn Ahmad informed us [lacuna]. Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Anbasah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: O Allah, whatever blessing has come to me or to anyone of Your creation is from You alone, no partner have You; to You is praise and to You is thanks, has fulfilled the thanks of that day. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Ibn Qutaybah, from Yazid ibn Mawhab, from Ibn Wahb."
"4000","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud al-Hudhali from Ibn 'Abbas, 129 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yunus narrating, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments (saraya) are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will not be defeated due to fewness."
"4001","130 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn narrated to us. Yunus said: Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and a people reaching twelve thousand are not defeated due to fewness, if they are truthful and patient. Except that Hujayn said: from Ibn Shihab, and did not say at the end of the hadith: patient."
"4002","131 - With it: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, I heard Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrating from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated due to fewness. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yunus, from Hibban ibn 'Ali. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi al-Basri and Abu 'Ammar and more than one, from Wahb ibn Jarir, and said: A hasan gharib hadith; not many narrate it with isnad. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili from Zuhayr ibn Harb. Hibban ibn 'Ali: we transmitted it for consideration (i'tibar)."
"4003","Another, 132 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush and Abu Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike."
"4004","133 - With it: My father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: I was narrated from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the bee, the ant, the shrike, and the hoopoe. Yahya said: And I saw in the book of Sufyan: from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Labid, from al-Zuhri."
"4005","134 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad in Naysabur informed us that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike. Abu Dawud narrated it from Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi al-Dhuhli. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Dharih in 'Ukbara, from Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi, from Hibban ibn 'Ali al-'Anazi, from Ibn Jurayj and 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri. [lacuna]."
"4006","Another, 135 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us (Ha). 136 - al-Tabarani said: And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his sword Dhu al-Faqar as extra spoil on the day of Badr, and it is the one about which he saw the dream on the day of Uhud."
"4007","137 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from the blind (?) 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his sword Dhu al-Faqar as extra spoil on the day of Badr, and it is the one about which he saw the dream on the day of Uhud. He said: I saw in my sword Dhu al-Faqar a notch that will be among you, and I saw that I was mounted behind a ram, so I interpreted it as the ram of the squadron, and I saw that I was in strong armor, so I interpreted it as Madinah, and I saw cattle being slaughtered, so cattle, by Allah, is good, cattle, by Allah, is good. So it was as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala', from Muhammad ibn al-Salt, from Abu al-Zinad."
"4008","Another, 138 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-'Abbas narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud. 139 - (Ha) Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Allah Almighty revealed: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers, the wrongdoers}, {the defiantly disobedient}. Ibn 'Abbas said: He revealed it concerning two groups of Jews, one of which had dominated the other in the pre-Islamic period until they agreed and made peace that for every slain one killed by the mighty group from the humble group, his blood-money is fifty wasqs, and for every slain one killed by the humble group from the mighty group, his blood-money is a hundred wasqs. They remained so until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and both groups submitted to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that time had not prevailed over them nor trodden them, and it was a truce. Then the humble group killed one of the mighty group, so the mighty group sent to the humble group: Send us a hundred wasqs. The humble group said: Though their religion is one and their lineage one, is the blood-money of some half the blood-money of others?! We only gave you this out of oppression from you against us and fear of you; now that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, we will not give you that. War almost erupted between them, then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge between them. The mighty group thought: By Allah, Muhammad will not give you from them double what he gives them from you; they spoke truth, they only gave us this out of oppression and domination over them. So send to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one who will learn his view for you: if he gives you what you want, you appoint him judge, and if he does not give it to you, beware of him and do not appoint him. So they sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some hypocrites to test the view of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for them. When they came, Allah informed His Messenger of all their affair and what they intended, and Allah Almighty revealed: {O Messenger, let not those grieve you who hasten into disbelief among those who said} - to His saying - {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the defiantly disobedient}. Then he said: By Allah, concerning them it was revealed, and them Allah meant. This is the wording of Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi. In the narration of Ibrahim ibn Abi al-'Abbas: {Those are the disbelievers, those are the wrongdoers} - {those are the defiantly disobedient}. He said: Ibn 'Abbas said: Allah Almighty revealed it concerning the two groups of Jews, with variants in wording noted. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Yahya al-Ramli, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa', from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, similarly. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad: more than one of the Imams criticized him, and it is narrated that Malik declared him trustworthy, and Allah knows best. End of the juz', praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace. The sixty-third juz' excluding the hadith of Anas, being juz' 76 of the complete book. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace."
"4009","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah from Ibn 'Abbas, 140 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far al-Hashimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that in the year of the Conquest the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib brought him Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, and he embraced Islam at Marr al-Zahran. Al-'Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves this pride, so grant him something. He said: Yes; whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, and whoever closes his door is safe. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it."
"4010","141 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of the Conquest when ten of Ramadan had passed, and when he descended at Marr al-Zahran."
"4011","142 - With it: My father narrated to me, Mu'awiyah - he is Ibn 'Amr - narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Conquest was when thirteen of Ramadan had passed."
"4012","143 - With it: My father narrated to me, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded on his journey, appointing over Madinah Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn Husayn ibn 'Utbah ibn Khalaf al-Ghifari, and set out when ten of Ramadan had passed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted and the people fasted with him, until when he was at al-Kadid between 'Usfan and ... he broke fast in the morning, then proceeded until he descended at Marr al-Zahran among ten thousand Muslims."
"4013","144 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Shu'ayb 'Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for the conquest of Makkah, he appointed over Madinah Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn al-Husayn al-Ghifari."
"4014","145 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad al-Saffar in Naysabur informed us that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, saying: Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hamdun informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris ibn Dhu'ayb al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Buhlul narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: And al-Zuhri said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded on his journey and set out when ten of Ramadan had passed. He fasted and the people fasted with him until when he was at al-Kadid, he broke fast, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded until he descended at Marr al-Zahran among ten thousand Muslims. Sulaym ... and Muzaynah joined. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended at Marr al-Zahran, news had been blinded to Quraysh: no news of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached them, nor did they know what he would do. That night Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, Hakim ibn Hizam, and Budayl ibn Warqa' went out seeking and looking whether they could find or hear news. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended at Marr al-Zahran, al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib said: I said: O morning of Quraysh! If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enters Makkah by force before they come to him seeking security, it will be the destruction of Quraysh forever. He said: So I sat upon the white mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and went out on it until I came to al-Arak, saying: Perhaps I will meet some woodcutter, milk-seller, or needy person who will go to them and inform them of the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so they come out to him. He said: By Allah, while I was riding on it seeking what I went out for, I heard the speech of Abu Sufyan and Budayl ibn Warqa' disputing, Abu Sufyan saying: I have never seen fires or an army like tonight. Budayl said: By Allah, this is Khuza'ah, roused by war. Abu Sufyan said: By Allah, Khuza'ah are too low and vile for these to be their fires and army. I recognized the voice of Abu Sufyan and said: O Abu Hanzalah! He recognized my voice and said: Abu al-Fadl? I said: Yes. He said: What is with you, may my father and mother be ransom for you! I said: Woe to you, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the people; O morning of Quraysh, by Allah! He said: What is the stratagem, may my father and mother be ransom for you? I said: By Allah, nothing except that you ride behind this beast and I bring you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, if he captures you he will strike your neck. So he rode behind the mule and his two companions returned. Every time I passed a fire of the Muslims, they said: Who is this? When they looked they said: The uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his mule, until I passed the fire of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: Who is this? He stood toward me; when he saw him on the back of the beast he recognized him and said: Abu Sufyan, enemy of Allah! Praise be to Allah who has enabled (us) against you. He rushed toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I spurred the mule and outran him as a slow beast outruns a slow man, then I dismounted and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and 'Umar came and entered, saying: O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Sufyan; Allah has enabled (us) against him without pact or covenant, so let me strike his neck. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have granted him protection. Then I sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and took hold of his head, saying: By Allah, no man shall converse with him tonight besides me. When 'Umar persisted about him, I said: Gently, O 'Umar! By Allah, had he been of Banu 'Adi ibn Ka'b you would not have said this, but you knew he is a man of Banu 'Abd Manaf. He said: Gently, O 'Abbas! By Allah, your Islam on the day you embraced Islam was dearer to me than the Islam of al-Khattab, and that only because I knew your Islam was dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the Islam of al-Khattab. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him to your lodging, and in the morning bring him to us. So I took him to my lodging; in the morning I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he saw him he said: Woe to you, O Abu Sufyan, has the time not come for you to testify there is no god but Allah? He said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, how forbearing, generous, and joining you are! By Allah, it almost occurred to me that had there been another with Allah, it would have sufficed something by now. He said: Woe to you, O Abu Sufyan, has the time not come for you to testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, how forbearing, generous, and joining you are! By Allah, as for this, there is still something in the soul about it until now. Al-'Abbas said: I said: Woe to you, embrace Islam and testify there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah before your neck is struck. So he testified the testimony of truth and embraced Islam. Al-'Abbas said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves this pride, so grant him something. He said: Yes; whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, and whoever closes his door upon himself is safe. When I went to leave, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O 'Abbas, detain him at the narrow pass of the valley by the mountain ridge until the cavalry of Allah pass by him and he sees them. So I detained him where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me. The tribes passed by him upon their banners; every time a tribe passed, he said: Who are these? I said: Banu Sulaym. He would say: What have I to do with Banu Sulaym? Then a tribe would pass, and he would say: Who are these? I would say: Muzaynah. He would say: What have I to do with Muzaynah? Until the tribes were exhausted; no tribe passed but he asked me about it and I informed him, and he said: What have I to do with Banu so-and-so? Until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in the green-clad battalion: a squadron of Muhajirun and Ansar of whom nothing was seen but eyes in iron. He said: Glory be to Allah! Who are these, O 'Abbas? I said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the Muhajirun and Ansar. He said: No one has power against these. By Allah, O Abu al-Fadl, the kingdom of your nephew has become great this morning. I said: Woe to you, O Abu Sufyan, it is prophethood. He said: Yes indeed. I said: Safety to your people; go out to them. When he came to them he shouted at the top of his voice: O company of Quraysh, this is Muhammad who has come to you with what you have no power against; whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe. Hind bint 'Utbah stood to him, seized his mustache, and said: Kill the fat bearded one ... an evil scout of a people. He said: Woe to you, let not this deceive you of yourselves; he has come with what you have no power against; whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe. They said: May Allah fight you, what use is your house to us? And whoever closes his door is safe. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the narration of al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Madinah with ten thousand, eight and a half years after his arrival in Madinah. He marched with the Muslims to Makkah fasting and they fasting until he reached al-Kadid - a water between 'Usfan and Qudayd - then he broke fast and they broke fast. Al-Zuhri said: What is taken from the matter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the latest and latest. This is the wording of the hadith of Ma'mar from al-Zuhri with al-Bukhari, the longest narration. In Muslim's narration there is abridgment."
"4015","Another, 146 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When {Alif Lam Mim, the Romans have been defeated, in the nearest land, and they after their defeat will be victorious, within a few years} was revealed, Abu Bakr made a wager with Quraysh, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have wagered with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not stipulate more carefully, for bid' is between three and seven."
"4016","147 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Saffar in Naysabur informed us that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When {Alif Lam Mim, the Romans have been defeated ... within a few years} was revealed, Abu Bakr wagered with Quraysh, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have wagered with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not stipulate more carefully, for bid' is between three and nine. Al-Jumahi said: Munahabah is wagering, and that was before it was prohibited. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this route."
"4017","Another, 148 - Abu al-Futuh Mas'ud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Karim al-Daqqaq at Bab al-Basrah in Baghdad informed us that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Samarqandi informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Husayn Ibn Akhi Mimi informed us, Isma'il - he is Ibn al-'Abbas al-Warraq - narrated to us, Abu 'Amr Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharzah al-Kufi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa al-'Absi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved a woman. One day he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sought permission for a need, and he permitted him. He went out on a rainy day and saw a woman at a pond washing. When he saw her, he sat with her as a man sits with his wife, then moved his private part, and it was like fringe (without erection). He stood remorseful, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray four rak'ahs. Then Allah revealed: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for the mindful}. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of al-Aswad and 'Alqamah from Ibn Mas'ud, and from the hadith of Abu Umamah al-Bahili, similarly. Al-Daraqutni said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa alone narrated it from Ibn 'Uyaynah from al-Zuhri."
"4018","Another, 149 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, from Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Dimashqi. Yahya said: I saw him, sat with him, and wrote nothing from him, from 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a cluster (of grapes) and said: Your Lord Almighty sends you greeting of peace and says: Eat this, or take this."
"4019","150 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Mihrabazd informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-'Asqalani informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Umar informed me, from 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah (Ha). 151 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad - known as Ibn al-Saffar in Naysabur - informed us that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abdullah al-Dhuhli informed us, Asbagh narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb informed me, from Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Dimashqi, from 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your Lord sends you greeting of peace, and has sent me to you with this cluster for you to eat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it ... Their wording is one."
"4020","Another, 152 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah (Ha). 153 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never aided anywhere as he was aided at Uhud. That was denied against him, so Ibn 'Abbas said: Between me and whoever denies is the Book of Allah; Allah says: {Allah fulfilled His promise to you when you were slaying them by His permission}. Ibn 'Abbas said: Hass (slaying) is killing, {until when you faltered}, to His saying: {And He pardoned you; Allah is bountiful to the believers}. He meant by this the archers. That is because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stationed them in an ambush post, then said: Guard our backs; if you see us being killed, do not aid us, and if you see us having taken spoils, do not share with us. When Allah granted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoils and permitted him the camp of the polytheists, all the archers broke away and entered the camp plundering. The ranks of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had closed together, they were like this, and he interlaced his right and left fingers. When the archers vacated that gap they were in, the cavalry entered from that place upon the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some struck others, many Muslims were killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions had from the start of the day until seven or nine of the standard-bearers of the polytheists were killed. The Muslims wheeled toward the mountain, not reaching where people say the cave; they were only beneath al-Mihras. Satan shouted: Muhammad has been killed. We did not doubt it was true; we remained not doubting he had been killed until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared between the two ravines, and I recognized him by his leaning when he walked. He said: We rejoiced as if what befell us had not befallen us. He said: He came apart toward us saying: Allah's wrath is severe upon a people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Another time he says: O Allah, they have no right to overcome us until they reach us. He stayed a while when Abu Sufyan shouted from below the mountain: Exalted be Hubal - meaning his god - where is the son of Abu Kabshah, where is the son of Abu Quhafah, where is the son of al-Khattab? 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not answer him? He said: Yes indeed. When he said: Exalted be Hubal, 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Allah is Higher and More Majestic. Abu Sufyan said: O son of al-Khattab, you have favored (i.e., done well). He repeated the like, saying: Where is the son of Abu Kabshah, where is the son of Abu Quhafah, where is the son of al-Khattab? 'Umar said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is Abu Bakr, this is I, 'Umar. Abu Sufyan said: A day for the day of Badr; days alternate, war has its turns. 'Umar said: Not equal; our slain in Paradise and your slain in Fire. He said: You claim that; then we have lost indeed. Then Abu Sufyan said: You will find among your slain mutilation, not by the view of our chiefs. Then Jahili zeal overtook him, saying: If that was so, we did not dislike it. This is the wording of the narration of 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz. In Imam Ahmad's narration from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, never aided anywhere as He aided on the day of Uhud. He said: We denied that. Ibn 'Abbas said: Between me and whoever denied that is the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saying on the day of Uhud: {Allah fulfilled His promise to you}, with variants noted in the parallel wording."
"4021","'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah Abu al-Mughirah from Ibn 'Abbas, 154 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in writing that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Jumhur - he is al-Tinnisi - narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Kindi narrated to us, from Abu al-Mughirah 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of my nation will recite the Qur'an and go deep in religion; Satan will come to them saying: If only you came to kings, took of their world, and kept apart from them with your religion. Yet that will only be as thorns alone are gathered from tragacanth; likewise nothing is gathered from nearness to them except sins. Al-Tabarani said: Hisham ibn 'Ammar alone narrated it, but it is not so; Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, similarly."
"4022","Another, 155 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, saying: Ibn 'Abbas was asked about Allah's saying: {And she certainly inclined toward him, and he inclined toward her}. Ibn 'Abbas said: He undid the waist-wrapper and sat with her as the circumciser sits (i.e., in the posture of intercourse)."
"4023","'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid al-Laythi al-Makki from Ibn 'Abbas, 156 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz (known as Qafak) in Isfahan informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Yunus informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-'Abid al-Makki narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid (who used to lead them in Ramadan in Makkah and lengthen with them), saying: Ibn Jurayj said to me: O Hasan, your grandfather 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I prayed last night behind a tree, recited Sad, and prostrated in it; the tree prostrated, and I heard it saying: O Allah, make for me thereby a remembrance with You, and establish for me thereby a treasure. Ibn 'Abbas said: So I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting Sad, prostrating in it, and I heard him saying what the man reported of the tree's saying."
"4024","157 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said to me: Your grandfather 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw myself this night in a dream as if praying by a tree, as if I recited the chapter of prostration and prostrated; I saw the tree as if it prostrated with my prostration, and as if I heard it saying: O Allah, write for me thereby a reward with You, remove from me thereby a burden, make it for me a treasure with You, and accept from me as You accepted from Your servant Dawud. Ibn 'Abbas said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the prostration chapter, and I heard him saying in his prostration as the man informed him of the tree's saying. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, saying: Ibn Jurayj said to me: O Hasan, 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw myself tonight asleep as if praying behind a tree; I prostrated and the tree prostrated for my prostration, and I heard it saying: O Allah, write for me thereby a reward with You, remove from me thereby a burden, make it for me a treasure with You, and accept it from me as You accepted it from Your servant Dawud. Al-Hasan said: Ibn Jurayj said to me: Your grandfather said to me: Ibn 'Abbas said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited a prostration chapter then prostrated. Ibn 'Abbas said: So I heard him saying the like of what the man informed him of the tree's saying. He said: This is a gharib hadith from the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas; we know it only from this route. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays, similarly."
"4025","Another, 158 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Adib Abu 'Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydullah Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan - he is Ibn 'Uyaynah - narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: Most people will not believe in the verse of permission: {Let those whom your right hands possess ask permission of you}. Then he said: I command this slave-girl of mine - a short white girl - that permission be sought of me. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Sarh, Ibn al-Sabbah, and Ahmad ibn 'Abdah, all from Sufyan."
"4026","Another, 159 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah informed us, my father narrated to me, Dawud ibn Mihran narrated to us, Dawud - meaning al-'Attar - narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man said: How much suffices me for ablution? He said: A mudd. He said: How much suffices me for washing? He said: A sa'. The man said: It does not suffice me. He said: May you have no mother; it sufficed one better than you: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4027","160 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-'Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and wash with a sa'. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the narration of 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jabir, from Anas ibn Malik. And in Sahih Muslim, from the narration of Safinah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4028","Another, 161 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas asked about al-A'raf, and he said: It is the elevated thing."
"4029","162 - With it: That he heard Ibn 'Abbas deeming desirable the delaying of 'Isha, reciting: {And in the watches of the night}."
"4030","163 - With it: From 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Yazid, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying regarding His saying: {Mention Allah's name over them standing in rows}, he said: Standing."
"4031","164 - With it: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas asked about Allah Almighty's saying: {He has not placed upon you in religion any hardship}. He said: Is there anyone of Hudhayl here? A man said: Yes, I. He said: What do you count haraj among you? The Hudhali said: The narrow thing. Ibn 'Abbas said: It is that."
"4032","165 - With it: Sufyan narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying regarding His saying: {The fornicator marries none but a fornicatress or a polytheist}, he said: It is a ruling between them."
"4033","166 - With it: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: {Al-Ma'un} is lending of household goods."
"4034","'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith - I think Ibn Hisham - al-Makhzumi from Ibn 'Abbas, 167 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sabiq al-Kharazi narrated to us - that 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, informed him, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; whoever falls into them is likely to sin, and whoever avoids them is more protective of his religion, like one pasturing beside a sanctuary; whoever pastures beside a sanctuary is about to fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is the unlawful. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir."
"4035","'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Alqamah, and it is said Ibn 'Alqam, from Ibn 'Abbas, 168 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib in Isfahan informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn 'Abd al-Salam and Waki' narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Alqamah who said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas about His saying: {Woe to those who write the Book with their hands}. He said: It was revealed concerning the polytheists and the People of the Book. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Habib al-Kirmani, from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr, from Waki', from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Alqam, with a saying concerning the People of the Book."
"4036","'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr al-Laythi al-Qass al-Makki from Ibn 'Abbas, 169 - Imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-'Ijli in Isfahan informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Kunayz the servant, the just jurist, freedman of Ahmad ibn Tulun, narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has pardoned for my nation mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced into. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Awza'i except Bishr; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"4037","170 - Abu al-Barakat Dawud ibn Ahmad ibn Mula'ib and Musa ibn 'Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili informed us that Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Banna informed them, 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Muradi in Egypt narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr al-Tinnisi narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has pardoned for my nation mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced into. Yahya said: This is a gharib hadith; we heard it only from him."
"4038","171 - Abu 'Ali Diya' ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn al-Khurayf in Baghdad informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, Abu al-Husayn - he is Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hasnun al-Narsi - informed us, Abu al-Qasim 'Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ... - recited to him - Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Muradi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr al-Tinnisi narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from 'Ata', from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has pardoned for my nation mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced into. Al-Daraqutni said: Bishr ibn Bakr alone narrated it; none narrated it from him except al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman and Ya'qub al-Buwayti the jurist. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah."
"4039","Another, 172 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iblis said to his Lord: O Lord, Adam has been sent down, and I know there will be a Book and Messengers; what are their Book and Messengers? He said: He said: Their messengers are the angels and the Prophets among them, and their books are the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, and the Furqan. He said: What is my book? He said: Your book is tattooing, your recitation is poetry, your messengers are soothsayers, your food is that over which Allah's name is not mentioned, your drink is every intoxicant, your truth is lying, your house is the bathhouse, your snares are women, your caller (mu'adhdhin) is the flute, and your mosque is the marketplaces. I say: I know it only through this isnad."
"4040","'Uthman ibn Hadir al-Himyari Abu Hadir from Ibn 'Abbas, 173 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Dumi al-Warraq informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun who said: I heard Abu Hadir al-Himyari narrating to my father Maymun ibn Mihran, saying: I went out for 'Umrah in the year the people of Syria besieged Ibn al-Zubayr in Makkah, and men of my people sent sacrificial animals with me. When we reached Syria they prevented us entering the Sanctuary, so I slaughtered the offering where I was, then exited ihram, then returned. The next year I went out to make up my 'Umrah, came to Ibn 'Abbas and asked him. He said: Replace the offering, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his Companions to replace the offering they slaughtered in the year of Hudaybiyah during the 'Umrah of Fulfillment. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"4041","Another, 174 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hadir al-Azdi, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Sacrificial camels were few in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded people with cows. Yazid ibn Harun narrated it making them one hadith."
"4042","175 - Abu 'Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Maymun informed us, from Abu Hadir - or Ibn Abi Hadir - from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The people of Hudaybiyah were commanded to replace the offering in the following year in which they entered Makkah, so they replaced. Camels were dear that year, so one who did not find a camel was permitted to buy a cow. The narration - sacrificial camels were few to its end - Ibn Majah narrated from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash."
"4043","'Ata' ibn Aslam Abu Rabah al-Makki Abu Muhammad the jurist from Ibn 'Abbas, 176 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ... Khurawst informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-'Attar al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not trot in the seven (circuits) in which he poured forth (i.e., the Ifadah tawaf)."
"4044","177 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us that Sa'd ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Mihrabazd informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-'Asqalani informed us, Harmalah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, from 'Ata', from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not trot in the seven in which he poured forth (Ifadah). Al-Daraqutni said: Ibn Wahb alone narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Hajjaj, Rawh, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar and others transmitted it mursal from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud narrated it from Sulayman ibn Dawud, from Ibn Wahb. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la and al-Harith ibn Miskin. Ibn Majah narrated it from Harmalah ibn Yahya."
"4045","Another, 178 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah who said: Ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer on a festival day falling on Friday early in the day, then we went to Friday prayer and he did not come out to us, so we prayed alone. Ibn 'Abbas was in Ta'if; when he came we mentioned that to him, and he said: He hit the Sunnah. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. Then he narrated from Yahya ibn Khalaf, from Abu 'Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata' who said: A Friday and a Fitr day coincided in the time of Ibn al-Zubayr, so he said: Two festivals have coincided in one day, so he combined them, praying them two rak'ahs in the morning, adding nothing to them until he prayed 'Asr. He did not mention Ibn 'Abbas in this route."
"4046","Another, 179 - Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili in Baghdad informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Karkhi informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, my uncle 'Umarah ibn Thawban informed me, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the softest of shoulders in prayer. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"4047","Another, 180 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr and 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The price of the shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams."
"4048","181 - Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Sibt in Baghdad informed us that his father Abu 'Ali al-Hasan informed them, my grandfather Abu Sa'd al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sibt informed us, Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim ... al-Khallal informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad - companion of Abu Sakhrah - narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The price of the shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was valued at ten dirhams. Al-Nasa'i narrated it like the narration of 'Ali ibn Muslim from Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi, from Ibn Numayr, and from 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd, from his uncle, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that 'Ata' narrated to him that Ibn 'Abbas used to say: Its price then was ten dirhams, and from Muhammad ibn Wahb, from Ibn Salamah, from Ibn Ishaq, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from 'Ata', with it, mursal, and from Humayd ibn Mas'adah, from Sufyan ibn Habib, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from 'Ata', his saying. Abu Dawud narrated similarly, with that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut the hand of a man for a shield worth a dinar or ten dirhams. Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Salamah and Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated it from Yahya ibn Ishaq, with its isnad."
"4049","Another, 182 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz, known as Qafak al-Khabbaz, in Isfahan informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Qilabah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, {except inadvertent lapses}: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, if You forgive, You forgive abundantly; which servant of Yours is without lapses?!"
"4050","183 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Faris informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan - he is Ibn 'Uyaynah - narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Al-lamam is that which occurs once. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi 'Uthman al-Basri, from Abu 'Asim, saying: A hasan sahih gharib hadith; we know it only from the hadith of Zakariyya."
"4051","Another, 184 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas: He invited his brother 'Ubaydullah on the day of 'Arafah to food. He said: I am fasting. He said: You are leaders followed; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call for a milking vessel on this day and drink. Yahya once said: A household followed."
"4052","185 - With it: My father narrated to me, 'Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: 'Ata' said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas invited al-Fadl ibn al-'Abbas to food on the day of 'Arafah, and he said: I am fasting. 'Abdullah said: Do not fast, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a milking vessel with milk on the day of 'Arafah and drank from it. So do not fast, for people follow your example. Ibn Bakr and Rawh said: They follow your example."
"4053","186 - With it: My father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Umar informed me that 'Ata' informed him that Ibn 'Abbas invited al-Fadl."
"4054","187 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Umar (?) informed me that 'Ata' informed him that Ibn 'Abbas invited al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas on the day of 'Arafah to food, and he said: I am fasting. 'Abdullah said: Do not fast, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a milking vessel with milk and drank from it this day, and people follow your example. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', like the narration of Imam Ahmad from Yahya. He also narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Qasimi, from Hajjaj, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', similarly, saying: al-Fadl instead of 'Ubaydullah, and did not mention Zakariyya ibn 'Umar. Perhaps Ibn Jurayj heard it from Zakariyya ibn 'Umar, then heard it from 'Ata'; if he did not hear it from 'Ata', we have narrated it from the narration of Zakariyya from 'Ata'. It is narrated in the Two Sahihs from the narration of 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl. And the saying of Ibn 'Abbas ... I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call for a milking vessel on this day and drink: he witnessed that, and he also narrated it from his mother."
"4055","Another, 188 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Qabisah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped both break fast. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Uqbah ibn Qabisah."
"4056","Another, 189 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Ja'far - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi - narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding things he forbade: And the price of the dog. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn 'Isa, from al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah."
"4057","Another, 190 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Abu al-Fath Isma'il ibn al-Fadl al-Sarraj informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Furak al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has lifted from my nation mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced into. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Musaffa. Bishr ibn Bakr al-Qaysi narrated it from al-Awza'i, from 'Ata', from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas; Bishr alone narrated it, and it has preceded in the narration of 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr."
"4058","Another, 191 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them in Baghdad, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Muqawwimi informed us, al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us, 'Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us, Abu Bishr Bakr ibn Khalaf and Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban, from his uncle 'Umarah ibn Thawban, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of you are the best to their families, and I am the best of you to my family. Thus Ibn Majah narrated it. With the isnad Ibn Majah narrated. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it with addition:"
"4059","192 - 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them, 'Ali ibn Muhammad informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, freedman of Thaqif, narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, my uncle 'Umarah ibn Thawban narrated to me, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, that the men sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to beat women, so he permitted them. He spent the night hearing a loud sound, and said: What is this? They said: You permitted men to beat women, so they beat them. He forbade them, saying: The best of you are the best to their families, and I am among the best of you to my family."
"4060","Another, 193 - With it: Bakr ibn Khalaf Abu Bishr narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban, from his uncle 'Umarah ibn Thawban, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman asks her husband for divorce without right but she will find the scent of Paradise, though its scent is found from a journey of forty years. Thus Ibn Majah narrated it."
"4061","Another [report]. 194 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj (H). 195 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal (brisk walking) in his Hajj and in all his Umrahs, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and the caliphs (may Allah be pleased with them). Imam Ahmad narrated it thus, and this is his wording. And in the narration of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah: in his Hajj and his Umrah, and Abu Bakr, Umar and the caliphs after. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Muawiyah alone narrated it from Ibn Jurayj."
"4062","Another [report]. 196 - And with the same chain, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me - that he heard Ibn Abbas saying (H)."
"4063","197 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, he heard Ibn Abbas saying: If you are able that no one goes out on the day of Fitr until he has eaten, let him do so. He said: So I have never left eating before going out since I heard that from Ibn Abbas - so I eat from the edge of the tarifah. I said: What is the tarifah? He said: thin flatbread, or I drink milk, or nabidh, or water. I said: On what basis is this interpreted? He said: I heard - I think - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: They would not go out until the forenoon had extended, and they would say: We eat so as not to hurry away from the prayer. He said: And sometimes I would go out having tasted nothing but water - Ibn Abbas is the speaker. The wording of the narration of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari. And in the narration of Imam Ahmad, he said: I never left eating before going out, and in it: so I eat a bite from the edge of the sariqah, or I drink milk or water. I said: On what basis do you interpret this? He said: I heard it, I think, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and its end: so as not to hurry away from our prayer. And in the narration of Ishaq: al-tarifah, and in the narration of Imam Ahmad with sad and qaf, and that is correct."
"4064","198 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Tamimi al-Hudhali narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: It is from the Sunnah that you do not go out on the day of Fitr until you have eaten, nor on the day of Nahr until you return. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Ulayyah; Ishaq ibn Abdullah alone narrated it."
"4065","Another [report]. 199 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Zayd - narrated to us, from Kathir - he is Ibn Shinzhir - from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The beginning of rapid driving (idah) came from the desert folk; they would stand at the edges of the people with sticks, quivers and cups hung up, and when they moved on, those rattled and the people rushed with them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was indeed seen with the two side-locks of his she-camel touching its withers, while he said with his hand: O people, calmness is incumbent upon you; O people, calmness is incumbent upon you. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus."
"4066","Another [report]. 200 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, my grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: We, the company of the prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast and delay our suhur, and to place our right hands over our left in prayer."
"4067","201 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Harmalah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that he heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of the prophets, have been commanded to delay our suhur, hasten our breaking of the fast, and hold with our right hands over our left in our prayer. Abu Hatim said: Ibn Wahb heard this report from Amr ibn al-Harith and Talhah ibn Amr from Ata. I said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Talhah ibn Amr al-Makki from Ata. And Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah - we brought him for corroboration. Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Karmani narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, and it has preceded."
"4068","Another [report]. 202 - Abu Ahmad ibn Abdullah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him; the she-camel swerved with him while he raised his hands not exceeding his head, and he proceeded in that manner until he reached Jam (Muzdalifah). Then he poured forth the next morning with al-Fadl ibn Abbas riding behind him, and he kept reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the jamrah. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus. And he also narrated it from Hushaym, from Abd al-Malik, in like manner."
"4069","Another [report]. 203 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Nuh ibn Jawwanah al-Sulami, a Khurasani, narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque while saying with his hand thus - and Abu Abd al-Rahman gestured with his hand toward the ground: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, or remits (his debt), Allah will protect him from the fierce heat of Hell. Verily the work of Paradise is rugged on a hill - three times; verily the work of Hell is easy on a plain. And the fortunate is he who is shielded from trials. And there is no draught more beloved to Allah than a draught of anger a servant swallows; a servant does not swallow it except that Allah fills his heart with faith. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus."
"4070","Another [report]. 204 - Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya - I think he is Ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Halabi - narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Show leniency and leniency will be shown to you. Imam Ahmad heard it from Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli, from al-Walid ibn Muslim. And Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated it from his father, found in his handwriting."
"4071","Another [report]. 205 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - recited to him - Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rabah informed me, that Ata narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, that a man became junub in winter, so he asked and was ordered to perform ghusl, so he performed ghusl and died. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What is with them, they killed him, may Allah kill them - three times - the earth, or tayammum, is purification. He doubted about Ibn Abbas, then affirmed him afterwards."
"4072","206 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Salih - he is al-Hakam ibn Musa - narrated to us, Hiql narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai saying: Ata said, from Ibn Abbas, that a man was wounded in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then janabah befell him, so he sought a fatwa and was given fatwa for ghusl, so he performed ghusl and died. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: They killed him, may Allah kill them; was not the cure for ignorance questioning. 207 - Ata said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that afterwards, so he said: If he had washed his body and left his head where the wound befell him, it would have sufficed him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu al-Mughirah, from al-Awzai, he said: It reached me that Ata ibn Abi Rabah, and its end: ignorance is questioning. And Abu Dawud narrated it likewise from Nasr ibn Asim al-Antaki, from Muhammad ibn Shuayb, from al-Awzai, that it reached him from Ata. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib, from al-Awzai, from Ata, in like manner. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah. As for the narration of al-Awzai, he did not hear it from Ata; as for the narration of al-Walid ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rabah, the nephew of Ata, he mentioned his hearing it from his uncle, and for that reason Ibn Khuzaymah included it in his Sahih, and al-Busti narrated it from him."
"4073","Another [report]. 208 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the rows of men is the first of them, and the worst of them is the last of them; and the best of the rows of women is the last of them, and the worst of them is the first of them. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim, from the narration of Abu Hurayrah."
"4074","Another [report]. 209 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Bariyyah narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Hassan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is best? He said: He whose seeing reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in knowledge, and whose knowledge reminds you of the Hereafter."
"4075","210 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abdullah Samuyah informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ubaydullah - he is Ibn Musa - narrated to us, from al-Mubarak, from Ibn Hassan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is most excellent? He said: He whose seeing reminds you of Allah - meaning - and whose speech increases your knowledge."
"4076","Another [report]. 211 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How are you? He said: Better than a people who have not visited a sick person, nor attended a funeral."
"4077","212 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them - recited to him while they listened - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah obligated upon them that one fight ten, so that was heavy upon them and hard upon them, so Allah lightened it from them to one man fighting two men. So Allah revealed concerning that: If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred, to the end of the verses - Were it not for a decree from Allah that preceded, you would have been touched for what you took by a great punishment, meaning the spoils of Badr. He says: Were it not that I do not punish one who disobeys Me until I have warned him beforehand. Then He said: O Prophet, say to those captives in your hands, the verse. So al-Abbas said: By Allah, it was concerning me, when I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of my Islam, and asked him to reckon for me the twenty ounces I had brought, so he gave me for them twenty slaves, each of them trading with wealth in his hand, besides what I hope for of the forgiveness of Allah."
"4078","213 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah obligated upon them that one fight ten, so that was heavy upon them, so He removed that from them and it was returned to their fighting the enemy when they were twice their number."
"4079","214 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas: It is not for a prophet to have captives - and he recited until he reached - a great punishment, meaning the spoils of Badr before He made them lawful for them. He says: Were it not that I do not punish one who disobeys Me until I have warned him beforehand, you would have been touched for what you took by a great punishment."
"4080","215 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas: Say to those captives in your hands, until he reached: was taken from you. He said: Al-Abbas used to say: By Allah, it was revealed concerning me, when I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of my Islam, and asked him to reckon for me the twenty ounces found with me, but he refused to reckon them for me, so Allah gave me for the twenty ounces twenty slaves, each of them trading with my wealth in his hand, besides what I hope for of the forgiveness of Allah. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: There was revealed: If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred. That was hard upon the Muslims when it was obligated upon them that one not flee from ten, so the alleviation came, and He said: Now Allah has lightened for you, to His saying: two hundred. He said: So when Allah lightened for them in number, He reduced of patience in proportion to what He lightened for them. And in what we have mentioned there is addition over what he mentioned."
"4081","Another [report]. 216 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ghilah, then said: If it harmed anyone it would have harmed Faris and Rum. Ibn Bukayr said: And ghilah (ightiyal) is that a man has intercourse with his wife while she is nursing. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Judamah bint Wahb."
"4082","Another [report]. 217 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad and al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Matar, from Ata (H). 218 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ata, that Ibn al-Zubayr prayed Maghrib and gave salam in two rakahs, then stood to touch the Corner, so the people glorified Allah, so he returned and prayed a rakah. He said: So I came to Ibn Abbas and informed him of that, so he said: He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The wording of Hisham. And in the narration of Matar: he gave salam in two rakahs and rose to touch the Stone, so the people glorified Allah, so he said: What is the matter with you? He said: So he prayed what remained and prostrated two prostrations. He said: So that was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, so he said: He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4083","Another [report]. 219 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Mandah ibn al-Walid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah, so he said: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. So he said: Perform Hajj on behalf of yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Amr except Hammad, nor from Hammad except Yazid; Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid alone narrated it. I said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father. And Yaqub is spoken about."
"4084","Another [report]. 220 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or himself, then conceals it and does not complain of it to people, it is a right upon Allah to forgive him."
"4085","221 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us of it, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or body and conceals it, and does not complain of it to people, it is a right upon Allah to forgive him."
"4086","Another [report]. 222 - And with both chains, Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has created the Garden of Adn; He created therein what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, nor has occurred to a human heart. Then He said to it: Speak, so it said: The believers have succeeded. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Jurayj except Baqiyyah; Hisham ibn Khalid alone narrated them. Their wording is one, except that in the narration of Muhammad ibn Ridhah from al-Tabarani: from Ibn Jurayj. The Hafiz Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mardawayh narrated it in his Tafsir from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim, from Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Muslim al-Abbar, with its chain, in like manner, and in it: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us."
"4087","Another [report]. 223 - Umm Hani Afifah bint Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Farqaniyyah - in Isfahan - informed us, that Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh al-Dashti informed them - recited to him while they listened - and Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad - by ijazah - both said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Abu al-Fadl al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Washsha narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people recite best? He said: He whom when you hear him reciting, you see that he fears Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"4088","Another [report]. 224 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Shabbabah narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wakes up pleasing to his parents - I think he said - two doors to Paradise are opened for him; and whoever wakes up displeasing to his parents, two doors of Hell are opened for him; and if one then one. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, even if they wronged him? He said: Even if they wronged him, even if they wronged him - three times."
"4089","Another [report]. 225 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, al-Haytham narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Ata, Tawus and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used the siwak while fasting."
"4090","226 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Ata, Mujahid and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram due to a pain he had, and used the siwak while in ihram. In the narration of al-Haytham: while fasting. And in this: while in ihram. As for cupping, it has been narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"4091","Another [report]. 227 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows remove the dross of iron."
"4092","228 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. Amr ibn Dinar narrated the first hadith from Ibn Abbas. Al-Daraqutni said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli alone narrated them both; weak."
"4093","Another [report]. 229 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi informed us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover the faces of your dead, and do not resemble the Jews. Al-Daraqutni said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih alone narrated it from Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"4094","Another [report]. 230 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied perfume before entering ihram."
"4095","231 - And my uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them - in Baghdad - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would apply perfume before entering ihram. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from his aunt Aishah bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq - may Allah be pleased with them. Al-Daraqutni said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak alone narrated it from Abd al-Aziz al-Qasmali from Ibn Jurayj."
"4096","Another [report]. 232 - Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani and others informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, and it was said to Abd al-Wahid: Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi informed you; both said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr al-Misri narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated with on the evening of Arafah was: O Allah, You see my place, hear my speech, and know my secret and open; nothing of my affair is hidden from You. I am the wretched poor one, the one seeking help and refuge, the fearful apprehensive one, the affirming one confessing his sin. I ask You the asking of the destitute, and implore You the imploring of the sinful lowly one, and call upon You the supplication of the fearful blind one, whose neck has humbled to You, whose body is abased, whose nose is in dust for You. O Allah, do not make me wretched by my supplication to You, and be to me Compassionate, Merciful, O best of those asked, O best of givers. Al-Tabarani also narrated it from Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Bukayr, Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj, and Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misriyyin, from Yahya ibn Bukayr, from Yahya ibn Salih, and said: None narrated it from Ata except Ismail, nor from him except Yahya; Ibn Bukayr alone narrated it. I said: Yahya ibn Bukayr did not alone narrate it, for Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari narrated it."
"4097","233 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi - in Damascus - informed us, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath ibn Ali al-Sulami informed them, Abu Nasr al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tallab al-Qurashi the Khatib informed us, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Jumay al-Ghassani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad - in Baghdad - he is Ibn Ibrahim al-Hamadhani al-Anmati - narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj was: O Allah, You hear my speech, see my place, and know my inward and outward; nothing of my affair is hidden from You. And I am the wretched poor one, the one seeking help and refuge, the fearful apprehensive one, the affirming one confessing his sin. I ask You the asking of the destitute, and implore You the imploring of the sinful lowly one, and call upon You the supplication of the fearful blind one, whose neck has humbled to You, whose tear has flowed for You, whose body is abased to You, whose nose is in dust for You. O Allah, do not make me wretched by my supplication to You, and be to me Compassionate, Merciful, O best of those asked, O best of givers. Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub al-Jawzajani, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Bukayr."
"4098","Another [report]. 234 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub Sahib al-Basri narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perfect the ablution."
"4099","Another [report]. 235 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to me, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, Ata narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd Manaf, if you are entrusted with this affair after me, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House or prays at any hour he wishes of night or day."
"4100","Another [report]. 236 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, he said: Ata said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep among his companions that day, and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas received a billy-goat and slaughtered it for himself. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah, he ordered Rabiah ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf, who stood beneath the forelegs of his she-camel - and he was a loud-voiced man - and said: Shout: Do you know what day this is? They said: The Greater Hajj. He said: Shout and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has made your blood and wealth sacred to you, like the sanctity of this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours, and like the sanctity of this day of yours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his Hajj, and said when he stood at Arafah: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. And he said when he stood upon Quzah: This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place. Al-Bukhari has narrated from the narration of Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people on the day of Nahr and said: O people, what day is this? They said: A sacred day. He said: What land is this? They said: A sacred land. He said: What month is this? They said: A sacred month. He said: Your blood, wealth and honour are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. And he repeated it many times, then raised his head and said: O Allah, have I conveyed? And in what we have mentioned is what he did not mention."
"4101","Another [report]. 237 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub - Sahib al-Maghazi - narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Aban ibn Salih and Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith in that journey of his while he was in ihram; the one who married her to him was al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah three days, then Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nasr ibn Malik ibn Hisl came to him with a group of Quraysh - and they had entrusted him with expelling the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah - and said: Your term has ended, so leave us. He said to them: What harm to you if you left me to consummate the marriage among you, and we prepared food for you and you attended it? They said: We have no need of your food, so leave us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left. As for the marriage, it has come from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram."
"4102","238 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated to us, Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none with a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr; he supported me with his wealth and his person, and married his daughter to me. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Artah; Muhammad ibn Salih alone narrated it. And al-Daraqutni said: Artah ibn al-Mundhir alone narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. I said: And Artah ibn al-Mundhir was declared trustworthy by Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Main, except that Muhammad ibn Salih gave his kunyah as Abu Hatim, while Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him and said: Artah ibn al-Mundhir al-Sakuni Abu Adi; and it is possible he had two kunyahs, and Allah knows best."
"4103","239 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us - recited to him - it was said to him: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abdullah ibn Mayyah al-Hadrami narrated to you - recited to him - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated to us, Artah Abu Hatim narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none with me of greater favor than Abu Bakr - may Allah have mercy on him - he supported me with his person and wealth, and married his daughter to me."
"4104","Another [report]. 240 - Muhammad and Fatimah informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of the prayer and other affairs of Madinah."
"4105","Another [report]. 241 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani brothers, and Umm Hani Afifah bint Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Farfaniyyah - in Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Tahir Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them - recited to him - while Muhammad and Abd al-Wahid were present and Afifah listened, and it was said to her: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you - by ijazah - both said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, while al-Sabbagh was present, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf informed us, Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Marzuq al-Buzuri narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that a man disputed with his wife before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes, and an addition. He said: As for the addition, then no. It has been narrated in al-Bukhari from the narration of Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I do not blame Thabit in religion or character, except that I fear disbelief in Islam. So he said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. So he ordered her to return it to him, and separated between them. We intended only this addition: As for the addition, then no."
"4106","Another [report]. 242 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - in Cairo - informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn al-Shaybani informed them, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us, Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun al-Harbi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Masud al-Nahdi narrated to us, Sufyan - he is Ibn Said al-Thawri - narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata who said: Ibn Abbas said: The saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: Then whoever performs Umrah with Hajj, he said: Mutah is for the one prevented and others."
"4107","Another [report]. 243 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas: And that you pardon is nearer to piety, he said: Whichever of them pardons, he is nearer to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"4108","Another [report]. 244 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas: concerning the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: the Station of Ibrahim, he said: Arafat, Mina, and all the rites."
"4109","Another [report]. 245 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us - in writing - and my uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us of it, that his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us, Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muala ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya ibn Ismail ibn Ubaydillah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not render your dead impure, for the Muslim is not impure, alive or dead. Al-Daraqutni narrated it thus."
"4110","Another [report]. 246 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi - in Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us - in Makkah - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu Ubaydillah Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi informed us, Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Then whatever hadi is feasible, he said: A sheep. It has been narrated in al-Bukhari: So when he rides to Arafah, whoever has feasible hadi of camels, cattle or sheep. End of another."
"4111","247 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-lamam, that one lapses a single time."
"4112","Another [report]. 248 - And with the same chain he said: I asked Ibn Abbas: Shall I seek permission upon my sister? He said: Yes. I said: She is in my care, and I maintain her. So Ibn Abbas recited: And when the children among you reach puberty, let them seek permission as those before them sought permission. So permission is obligatory upon all of Allah's creation."
"4113","249 - And with the same chain, from Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Jurayj - one of them adding over the other - from Ata who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: I have two sisters, shall I seek permission upon them? He said: Yes. He said: They are in my care and I maintain them and spend upon them. He said: Seek permission upon them. Would you like to see them naked? Allah said: O you who believe, let those whom your right hands possess and those who have not reached puberty among you seek your permission on three occasions, the verse. Then he said: And when the children among you reach puberty, let them seek permission as those before them sought permission. He said: So permission is obligatory upon all of Allah's creation."
"4114","Another [report]. 250 - And with the same chain, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: Have they not seen that We drive water to the barren land, he said: It is a land in Yemen."
"4115","Another [report]. 251 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas who said: Had the jinn known that among mankind there are grandfathers, they would not have said: Exalted is the grandeur of our Lord. And he recited: The religion of my fathers Ibrahim, and: What will you worship after me? They said: We will worship your God and the God of your fathers. And he used to say: The grandfather is a father."
"4116","Another [report]. 252 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: Fleeing from a lion (qaswarah), he said: It is the stir of people. Sufyan said: meaning their sense and voices."
"4117","Another [report]. 253 - And with the same chain, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: We have created man in hardship (kabad), he said: In severity of creation. Then he mentioned his birth and the growth of his teeth."
"4118","Another [report]. 254 - And with the same chain, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: By the racers panting, he said: They are horses. And I heard him swear by Allah: No mount ever panted except a dog or a horse. Then those striking fire, he said: Plotting is plotting; so he kindled, i.e., he acted and achieved. Then the raiders at dawn, he said: They are horses that raided at dawn. Then they raised dust therewith, he said: The dust of horses' hooves; the dust is the dust cloud. Then they penetrated thereby the multitude, he said: The multitude of the enemy."
"4119","255 - And with the same chain, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: I heard him imitate their panting: akh akh, and saying: No mount ever panted except a dog or a horse."
"4120","Another [report]. 256 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib - in Isfahan - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fajr is two fajrs: a fajr in which food is forbidden and prayer is permitted, and a fajr in which prayer is forbidden and food is permitted. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri alone narrated it from al-Thawri, connected. And al-Firyabi narrated it from al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mursal."
"4121","Another [report]. 257 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn al-Musallam al-Lakhmi and Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir ibn Barakat al-Qurashi - recited to each of them in Damascus - informed us, that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khidr al-Sulami informed them, Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Hinnai informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai informed us, Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Marwan ibn Shuja al-Jazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: I came to Ibn Abbas (H)."
"4122","258 - And the Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi - in Isfahan - informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata who said: I came to Ibn Abbas while he was drawing water in Zamzam, with the lower parts of his garments wet, so I said to him: There has been talk about qadar. He said: Have they done it? This verse was revealed only concerning them: Taste the touch of Saqar; indeed We created everything with qadar. Those are the worst of this ummah; do not visit their sick, nor pray over their dead. If you show me one of them, I will gouge his eyes with these two fingers of mine. The wording of Ahmad ibn Mani, and the narration of al-Hasan is in its meaning. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim, from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The polytheists of Quraysh came disputing with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about qadar, so there was revealed: On the day they are dragged in the Fire upon their faces: Taste the touch of Saqar; indeed We created everything with qadar."
"4123","Ata ibn Yasar al-Madini, freedman of Maymunah, from Ibn Abbas. 259 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said ibn Khalid, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhuayb, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them while they were seated and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people in station? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the head of his horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. Shall I inform you of the one next to him? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and withdrawing from the evils of people. Shall I inform you of the worst of people in station? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him."
"4124","260 - And Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Qariz, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhuayb, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them while they were seated and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people in station? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the head of his horse in the path of Allah until he is killed or dies. Shall I not inform you of the one next to him? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and withdrawing from the evils of people. Shall I inform you of the worst of people in station? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him."
"4125","261 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Khalid, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhib, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out while they were seated and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people in station? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the head of his horse - or a horse - in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. He said: Shall I inform you of the one next to him? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and withdrawing from the evils of people. Shall I inform you of the worst of people? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him."
"4126","262 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, both said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr - he is Ibn al-Harith - informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people? A man holding the rein of his horse in the path of Allah. And I inform you of the one following him: a man secluded among his sheep, rendering Allah's right in them. And I inform you of the worst of people: a man who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abu al-Nadr, Husayn, and Uthman ibn Umar, all three from Ibn Abi Dhib. And Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Ata, without mentioning Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said, from Ibn Lahiah, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Ata, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this وجه. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Khalid al-Qarizi, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata, in like manner. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Khalid [source continues similarly]."
"4127","Another [report]. 263 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution: he scooped a handful and washed his face, then scooped a handful and washed his right hand, then scooped a handful and washed his left hand, then scooped a handful and wiped his head and ears, inserting his forefingers inside them and passing his thumbs over the outside of his ears, wiping their inside and outside, then scooped a handful and washed his right foot, then scooped a handful and washed his left foot. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr (he is Ibn Abi Shaybah). We intended from it only the wiping of the ears; the rest al-Bukhari narrated in like manner."
"4128","Another [report]. 264 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when fruit was brought to him, would give it to the youngest of the children present."
"4129","265 - And Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani and others informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Tamimi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the first fruits were brought to him, would accept them and place them upon his eyes, then give them to the youngest of the children present. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Malik, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, in like manner."
"4130","Another [report]. 266 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi and Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Husayn ibn Wahb al-Ursufi - in the city of Ursuf - narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abi Hujr al-Ayli narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever ransoms a captive from the hands of the enemy, then I am that captive. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Zayd except Hisham, nor from him except Bakr ibn Sadaqah al-Juddi; Ayyub ibn Sulayman alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hujr al-Ayli narrated from Yunus ibn Yahya ibn Salamah al-Madini; I asked my father and Abu Zurah about him, and they said: We do not know him. My father said: And these hadiths he narrated are sound. And Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention Bakr ibn Sadaqah."
"4131","Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As al-Makhzumi al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas. 267 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas who said: I was in the house of Maymunah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray at night, so I stood with him on his left, so he took my hand and placed me on his right. Then he prayed thirteen rakahs; I estimated the measure of his standing in each rakah as the measure of: O you enwrapped."
"4132","268 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, that Ibn Abbas said: I was in the house of Maymunah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray at night, so I stood with him on his left, so he took my hand and placed me on his right. Then he prayed thirteen rakahs; I estimated the measure of his standing in each rakah as the measure of: O you enwrapped. Abu Dawud narrated it from Nuh ibn Habib and Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi, all three from Abd al-Razzaq. We intended from this hadith: I estimated the measure of his standing in each rakah as the measure of: O you enwrapped."
"4133","Another [report]. 269 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Ward, from al-Hasan ibn Jubayr and Kathir, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of a third, for that harms the believer, and Allah dislikes harming the believer. Al-Bukhari said in al-Tarikh: al-Hasan ibn Kathir, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of a third. Muhammad said it to me; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; and Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Ward narrated to us from al-Hasan. Abu Abdullah said: Ibn al-Mubarak said - in al-Rayy - from Ibn Abbas - and in his book it was mursal, and the others do not narrate it with chain from Ibn al-Mubarak. End of it; praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace. The sixty-fifth juz of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant abundant peace."
"4134","Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas. Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi from Ikrimah. 270 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi - in Isfahan - informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Hammam - he is al-Walid ibn Shuja ibn al-Walid al-Sakuni - narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a lahd (niche grave) was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4135","271 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz al-Harawi informed us, that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them, Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, Imran ibn Musa narrated to us, Mujahid ibn Musa al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail al-Suddi narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, Ali and al-Fadl: And an Ansari man leveled his lahd, he being the one who leveled the lahd graves of the martyrs on the day of Badr. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim, from the hadith of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: Sad said: Make a lahd for me and set unbaked bricks over me as was done for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4136","Another [report]. 272 - The Shaykh Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Yahya Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Zafrani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from al-Ashjai, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: Then judge between them or turn away from them, he said: It was abrogated by: And judge between them by what Allah has revealed."
"4137","Ishaq ibn Jabir al-Adani from Ikrimah. 273 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Husayn informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Musab ibn Abdullah ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ishaq ibn Jabir al-Adani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who entices a servant against his master, nor is of us he who corrupts a wife against her husband, nor is of us he who urges on horses on the day of racing. Ishaq ibn Jabir: Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in his book."
"4138","Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Ikrimah. 274 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the mukatab (contracted slave) dies leaving inheritance, or incurs a hadd, he inherits in proportion to what has been freed of him, and the hadd is applied upon him in proportion to what has been freed of him."
"4139","275 - And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, that Said al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the mukatab incurs a hadd or inheritance, he inherits in proportion to what has been freed of him, and the hadd is applied upon him in proportion to what has been freed of him. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Ismail, in like manner - and said: Wuhayb narrated it from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in like manner from Harun ibn Abdullah, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, and said: A hasan hadith. And he said: Thus Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated from Ikrimah. And it was narrated from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Ikrimah, from Ali, as his saying. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Isa al-Naqqash and Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim, both from Yazid ibn Harun, from Hammad, from Ayyub, in like manner. And from Muhammad ibn Isa, from Yazid, from Hammad, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Ali, as his saying."
"4140","Another [report]. 276 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah who said: The mukatab renders, for the portion he has paid, the blood-money of a free man, and for what remains, the blood-money of a slave. Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun. And al-Nasai narrated it from al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, and from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah. And from Abu Bakr ibn Ali, from al-Qawariri, from Hammad, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, mursal."
"4141","Another [report]. 277 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir - meaning Ibn Hazim - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - that a virgin girl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that her father had married her off while she was unwilling, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice."
"4142","278 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak and Abu Ahmad Abdullah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a virgin girl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that her father had married her off while she was unwilling, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice."
"4143","279 - And Abu al-Fath Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Shatil informed us - in his book - and the Imam al-Hafiz Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn al-Hafiz Abd al-Ghani al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on them both - narrated to us of it, that Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Khushaysh the scribe informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Najjad informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a virgin girl came to the Prophet and claimed that her father had married her off while she was unwilling, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Husayn ibn Muhammad, with its chain. And from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without mentioning Ibn Abbas. And thus people narrated it mursal. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu al-Saqr Yahya ibn Yazdad al-Askari, from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi, with its chain. And from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ikrimah, in like manner, connected."
"4144","Another [report]. 280 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - that Ali - peace be upon him - when Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), married Ali - peace be upon him - he said: Do you have anything? I said: No. He said: Where is your Hutamiyyah coat of mail? So I gave it to her."
"4145","281 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When Ali married Fatimah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give her something. He said: I have nothing. He said: Where is your Hutamiyyah coat of mail? Abu Dawud narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani, from Abdah. And from Kathir ibn Ubayd, from Abu Haywah, from Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from Ghaylan ibn Anas, from Ikrimah, more complete. And al-Nasai narrated it from Harun ibn Ishaq, from Abdah. Hammad narrated it from Ayyub, adding in the chain Ali, peace be upon him."
"4146","Another [report]. 282 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan with a ram, and for al-Husayn with a ram. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Mamar."
"4147","283 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn - may Allah be pleased with them both."
"4148","Another [report]. 284 - The Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi and Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast while at Arafah, so Umm al-Fadl sent him milk and he drank it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Ismail ibn Ulayyah. It has a witness in the two Sahihs, from the narration of Umm al-Fadl bint Abbas. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Khalid ibn Amr ibn al-Nadr, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, and in it: He was brought pomegranate on the day of Arafah, in like manner."
"4149","Another [report]. 285 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Ubaydillah informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us - as I see - Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi informed us (H). 286 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When there was revealed: And those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses, flog them eighty lashes, Sad ibn Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, if I see a worthless woman with a man astride her, I will not gather four until the other has fulfilled his need? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Listen to what your chief says! Then his cousin Hilal ibn Umayyah was tried: he was one night in his land, then came at night and found with his wife a man, so he accused her with him. They gathered before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: The flogging. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by Allah I looked until I was certain, and listened until I was certain, and Allah will surely clear my back of flogging. He said: While it was thus, the lian verses came down: And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves, then the testimony of one of them is four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is of the liars, and it averts the punishment from her that she testify four testimonies by Allah that he is of the liars, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. He said: So he invoked curses, and he made him swear four times. He said: Detain him at the fifth, for it is decisive. Then the woman also invoked curses four times, so he said: Detain her at the fifth, for it is decisive. She hesitated at the fifth until they thought she would confess, then she said: I will not disgrace my people all this day. So she persisted in her word, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, and it is longer than this, and in it is mention of the child and his description. And al-Nasai narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ahmad, from Abu al-Rabi. And al-Bukhari has mentioned this hadith in his book, from the narration of Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, except that in this narration there are wordings not in the narration of Hisham, among them: the saying of Sad ibn Ubadah, and the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Listen to what your chief says, and the speech of Hilal, his saying: I looked and listened, and his saying: So he made him swear four times, he said: Detain him at the fifth, for it is decisive, and likewise his saying to the woman, and his saying: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them."
"4150","Another [report]. 287 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not boast of your fathers who died in jahiliyyah, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nostrils is better than your fathers who died in jahiliyyah."
"4151","288 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham - meaning al-Dastuwai - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not boast of your fathers who died in jahiliyyah, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nostrils is better than your fathers who died in jahiliyyah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq (freedman of Thaqif), from Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi. And Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - without mentioning Ibn Abbas."
"4152","Another [report]. 289 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub (H). 290 - And Abdullah al-Harbi and al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (he said: I do not know except that he raised the hadith), he said: He used to command killing snakes, and say: Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of revenge is not of us. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: The jann (white snake) is the transformed of the jinn, as monkeys were transformed from the Children of Israel. The wording of the narration of Imam Ahmad. And in the narration of Ishaq: he raised the hadith: He used to command killing snakes, and said: Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of revenge, and the rest is like it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated from Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Snakes are from the transformed jann, as pigs and monkeys were transformed, and it will come, Allah willing, in the narration of Khalid from Ikrimah."
"4153","Another [report]. 291 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: And We have given you seven of the oft-repeated, he said: The Opening of the Book. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman: he was spoken about, though al-Bukhari narrated from him in his book. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari, from the hadith of Abu Said ibn al-Mualla: I was praying in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I did not answer him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was praying. He said: Did not Allah say: Respond to Allah and the Messenger when he calls you. Then he said to me: I shall teach you a surah that is the greatest of surahs in the Quran before we leave the mosque. Then he took my hand, and when he intended to leave, I said to him: Did you not say: I shall teach you a surah that is the greatest surah in the Quran? He said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; it is the seven oft-repeated, and the mighty Quran given to me. And in his Sahih also from the hadith of Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Mother of the Quran is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Quran."
"4154","Another [report]. 292 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhqani, in Isfahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Indeed We sent it down in the Night of Decree, he said: The Quran came down entire to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree; then whenever Allah willed to bring forth something of it, He brought it forth."
"4155","Bassam ibn Abdullah al-Sayrafi al-Kufi from Ikrimah. 293 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Bassam al-Sayrafi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jallalah sheep, the price of the dog, the stud fee of the stallion, and the earnings of the cupper. Bassam al-Sayrafi: Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy, and Abu Hatim al-Razi said: No harm in him, sound in hadith. Al-Daraqutni said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq alone narrated it from Bassam. I said: And our narration is from other than Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq, so Said did not alone narrate it then, and Allah knows best."
"4156","Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dayli al-Madini from Ikrimah. 294 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Asad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri and Abu al-Muzaffar al-Qushayri - he is Said ibn Mansur - informed us, both said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, he said: my grandfather, the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us, Abu Ammar narrated to us with a strange, strange report, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said - he is Ibn Abi Hind - from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glance in his prayer right and left, without turning his neck behind his back."
"4157","295 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glance in prayer right and left, without turning anything of it behind his back."
"4158","296 - And Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Yahya and al-Talaqani narrated to us, both said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray glancing right and left, without turning his neck behind his back. Al-Talaqani said: Thawr narrated to me from Ikrimah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would [do likewise]."
"4159","297 - And with the same chain, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from a man of the companions of Ikrimah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glance in his prayer without turning his neck."
"4160","298 - And with the same chain, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, Thawr narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glance in his prayer right and left, without turning his neck. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan and more than one, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Abdullah ibn Said, from Thawr ibn Zayd, and said: Gharib. And Waki opposed al-Fadl in his narration. And from Mahmud, from Waki, from Abdullah ibn Said, from some companions of Ikrimah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - in like manner. And al-Nasai narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, with its chain, in like manner. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah, from Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth. Al-Daraqutni said: Al-Fadl ibn Musa alone narrated it from Abdullah ibn Said, from Thawr, from Ikrimah, connected."
"4161","Another [report]. 299 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Thawr ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then dispatched them, and said: Go forth in the name of Allah. And he said: O Allah, help them - meaning the party he dispatched toward Kab ibn al-Ashraf."
"4162","300 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Thawr ibn Yazid - and the correct is Zayd - from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched Muhammad ibn Maslamah and his companions to Ibn al-Ashraf to kill him, he walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then dispatched them, then said: Go forth in the name of Allah; O Allah, help them. Then he returned."
"4163","301 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub Sahib al-Maghazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then dispatched them, and said: Go forth in the name of Allah; O Allah, help them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his house - meaning concerning the killing of Ibn al-Ashraf."
"4164","302 - And with the same chain, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them, and he mentioned in like manner."
"4165","Another [report]. 303 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deceives us is not of us, and whoever shoots at us by night is not of us."
"4166","Another [report]. 304 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad and al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted as fief to Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and lowlands, and where cultivation is feasible of Quds, and did not give him the right of a Muslim. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, gave to Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani: he gave him the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and lowlands, and where cultivation is feasible of Quds, and did not give him the right of a Muslim."
"4167","305 - And with the same chain, Abu Uways narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid - freedman of Banu al-Dayl ibn Bakr ibn Kinanah - narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in like manner. He did not exceed except the hadith of Ibn Abbas. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbas al-Duri, from Husayn ibn Muhammad, from Abu Uways, from Thawr ibn Zayd, in like manner. And Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb, adding in its chain a man between Zayd and Ikrimah."
"4168","306 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from his maternal uncle Musa ibn Maysarah - freedman of Banu al-Dayl - from Ikrimah - freedman of Ibn Abbas - from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and lowlands, and where cultivation is feasible."
"4169","Another [report]. 307 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa informed us, Ahmad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us (H). 308 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, from al-Darawardi: from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar asked Ibn Abbas, he said: What do you make of the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And do not display yourselves as in the former jahiliyyah - was there a jahiliyyah other than one? So Ibn Abbas said: O Commander of the Believers, we have not heard of a first except that it has a last. So Umar said to him: Is there in the Book of Allah what confirms this? He said: Allah says: And strive in Allah as you strove the first time. So Umar said: Whom were we commanded to strive against? He said: Makhzum and Abd Shams."
"4170","Another [report]. 309 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dayli, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - who said: The garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught on a tree on the day of Hunayn, with the people gathered around him asking him of the spoils, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thought they had seized his cloak, and said: Release my cloak; do you want to render me miserly! By Allah, if Allah bestowed upon you like the rock of Tihamah in livestock, I would divide it among you; then you would not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar. They said: Only a samurah tree had caught his garment, so they freed him. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of Jubayr ibn Mutim."
"4171","Another [report]. 310 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Drinkers were beaten in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with hands, sandals and sticks."
"4172","Another [report]. 311 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet and pledged him in the mosque, then left; then he stood, spread his legs and urinated, then urinated, so the people turned upon him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt the man's urination. Then he was called for, and he said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to urinate in our mosque? He said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I thought it only a plain of the plains, so I urinated in it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a bucket of water and poured it over his urine."
"4173","312 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pledged him in the mosque, then left; then he stood, spread his legs, then urinated, so the people turned upon him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt the man's urination. Then he said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to urinate in our mosque? He said: By Him Who sent you, I thought it only a plain of the plains, so I urinated in it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a bucket of water, and it was poured over his urine. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik."
"4174","Another [report]. 313 - Muhammad and Fatimah informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd and Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man (H)."
"4175","314 - And Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dayli and Dawud ibn al-Husayn, both narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about a man to whom it seems in his prayer that he has broken wudu, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you until he opens his seat, so it seems to him that he has broken wudu, while he has not. So if one of you finds that, let him not leave until he hears the sound of that with his ear, or finds the smell of that with his nose. The wording of Zuhayr ibn Harb. And in the narration of al-Asfati: in his prayer that he has broken wudu while he has not - and with him: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer - and with him: that he has broken wudu, and the rest is like it. It has a witness in the two Sahihs, from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Zayd."
"4176","Another [report]. 315 - Abu Jafar Muhammad and Fatimah informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Abu Uways, from Thawr ibn Zayd and Musa ibn Maysarah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mustahadah (woman with prolonged bleeding), so he said: That is a kick of Satan in her womb. Abu Uways's name is Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Amir al-Asbahi; narrations differ from the imams concerning him, and Muslim has narrated from him in his Sahih."
"4177","Habib ibn al-Zubayr from Ikrimah. 316 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh - Sahib al-Aqtab - narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it is eaten, nor wool upon a back, nor milk in an udder."
"4178","Another [report]. 317 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh - seller of saddles - narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper a dinar. What is intended of it is his saying: a dinar, only; for it has been narrated in the Sahih, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"4179","Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ikrimah. 318 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not establish a sunnah of anything except that I know it, other than three: I do not know whether he used to recite in Zuhr and Asr or not; nor do I know how he used to recite: And I have reached of old age utter decrepitude - itiyyan or isiyyan? Husayn said: And we have forgotten the third."
"4180","319 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Hafiz informed us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr or not. Thus Abu Dawud brought it in his Sunan."
"4181","Another [report]. 320 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us - that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us - from the original of his book - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A woman of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, everything is only for men; I do not see women mentioned with anything. So this verse came down: Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, the verse in al-Ahzab. Sulayman ibn Kathir and Jarir narrated it from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Umm Umarah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned in like manner."
"4182","Al-Hakam ibn Aban al-Adani from Ikrimah. 321 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi - in Isfahan - informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Uthman Said ibn Abi Amr al-Buhayri narrated to us, Abu Amr ibn Hamdan al-Hiri narrated to us, Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Balkhi narrated to us, Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man made zihar from his wife then had intercourse with her before expiating, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I made zihar from my wife then I fell upon her before expiating. He said: What carried you to that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: Do not approach her until you do what Allah has commanded."
"4183","322 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having made zihar from his wife, then fallen upon her, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I made zihar from my wife then fell upon her before expiating. He said: And what carried you to that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: Do not approach her until you do what Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has commanded you. Abu Dawud, al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasai narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, in like manner. And Abu Dawud also narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani, from Sufyan, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, that a man said, without mentioning Ibn Abbas. And from Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Ismail, from al-Hakam, from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in like manner. And from Abu Kamil, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar, from Khalid who said: A narrator narrated to me from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And from Muhammad ibn Isa, from Mutamir, from al-Hakam, with it, without mentioning Ibn Abbas. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith. And al-Nasai also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Hakam [in like manner]."
"4184","Another [report]. 323 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Abu al-Fath Muflih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Dumi al-Warraq informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath al-Sijistani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Salm ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: Such-and-such, one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), has died. So he fell prostrating. It was said to him: You prostrate at this hour! He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see a sign, prostrate; and what sign is greater than the passing of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abbas al-Anbari, from Yahya ibn Kathir, from Salm ibn Jafar - and he was trustworthy - in like manner, and said: Hasan gharib, we know it only from this وجه. Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Azdi spoke about Salm ibn Jafar, while al-Azdi's word is not relied upon, for he himself has been spoken about."
"4185","324 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn Ararah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, Salm ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas after he had prayed the prayer: Such-and-such, one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), has died. So he fell prostrating. He said: It was said to him: Do you prostrate now, or: Do you pray now! He said: Did he not, peace be upon him, say: When you see a sign, prostrate? So what sign is greater than the passing of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from among us?"
"4186","Another [report]. 325 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad the scribe narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked, it was said: O Ibn Abbas, did Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see his Lord? He said: Yes. I said to Ibn Abbas: Does not Allah say: Visions do not perceive Him, while He perceives visions? He said: May you be bereft of your mother; that is His light which is His light, which is His light: when He manifests with His light, nothing perceives Him."
"4187","326 - And with the same chain, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, Salm ibn Jafar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Lord. I said: Does not Allah say: Visions do not perceive Him, while He perceives visions? He said: That is when He manifests with His light which is His light; and he saw his Lord twice."
"4188","327 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, Salm ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Did Muhammad see his Lord? He said: I said: Does not Allah say: Visions do not perceive Him, while He perceives visions? He said: Woe to you; when He comes with His light which is His light. He said: And he said: Muhammad saw his Lord twice. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Nabhan ibn Safwan al-Thaqafi, and said: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Nasai narrated that Muhammad saw his Lord, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Yazid ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Hakam."
"4189","Another [report]. 328 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the best of you call the adhan for you, and let your reciters lead you in prayer."
"4190","329 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Uthman - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the best of you call the adhan for you, and let your reciters lead you in prayer. Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Daraqutni said: Husayn ibn Isa, brother of Sulaym al-Muqri, alone narrated it from al-Hakam."
"4191","Another [report]. 330 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us (H). 331 - Zahir said: And Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us, Abu Tahir ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, the Imam Abu Bakr, informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us - dictated in Kufah - Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz Abu Shuayb - he is the one called al-Qinbari; I heard him saying: My origin is Persian - narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban informed us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas (H)."
"4192","332 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Isa ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas: O my uncle, shall I not give you, shall I not grant you, shall I not bestow upon you, shall I not do for you ten qualities: if you do that, Allah will forgive you your sin, its first and last, old and new, secret and open, small and great, mistaken and deliberate: that you pray four rakahs, reciting in each rakah of them the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation in the first rakah, you say while standing: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest - fifteen times. Then you bow and say while bowing ten times. Then you raise your head and say while standing ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say while seated ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five; you do that in four rakahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of Alij, Allah would forgive you. The wording of Isa ibn al-Qasim. And the wording of Ibn Khuzaymah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: O Abbas, O my uncle, shall I not give you, shall I not bestow upon you, shall I not do for you ten qualities: if you do that, Allah will forgive you your sin, its first and last, old and new, mistaken and deliberate: you recite the Opening of the Book and a surah, and when you finish the recitation in each rakah you say while standing: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, fifteen times. Then you bow and say it while bowing ten times. Then you raise your head from bowing and say it ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five in each rakah; you do in four rakahs. If you are able to pray it every day once, do so; if you do not, then every Friday once; if you do not, then every month once; if you do not, then every year once; if you do not, then in your lifetime once. And in the narration of Abu Yala Ishaq [words missing in source] with the Opening of the Book, then you raise your head. Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr, like this narration of Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah from his Sahih."
"4193","Another [report]. 333 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, al-Hakam ibn Aban informed me, from Ikrimah - freedman of Ibn Abbas - who said: Ibn Abbas said: When the illness befell Abdullah ibn Ubayy in which he died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and they spoke words between them. So Abdullah said: I have understood what you say; bestow upon me and shroud me in your shirt, and pray over me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded him in that shirt of his and prayed over him. Ibn Abbas said: And Allah knows best what prayer it was; and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never deceived any person."
"4194","334 - And Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim al-Samani - in Marw - informed us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zahir al-Shahhami informed us, Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Mahmi informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Bilal informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul and said: I hear your speech; so bestow upon me today, shroud me in your shirt, and pray over me. He said: So he shrouded him in his shirt and prayed over him. Ibn Abbas said: Allah knows best which prayer it is; and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never deceived any person. In al-Bukhari and Muslim, from the hadith of Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the grave of Abdullah ibn Ubayy after he was buried, brought him out, blew upon him of his saliva, and clothed him in his shirt, and Allah knows best. And in the narration of al-Bukhari: When the day of Badr came, captives were brought, and al-Abbas was brought with no garment upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked for a shirt, and they found the shirt of Abdullah ibn Ubayy."
"4195","Another [report]. 335 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us - that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lying with Umm Salamah one night, she rose as if shy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What is with you - have you begun menstruating, meaning menstruated? She said: Yes. He said: No harm; take your ablution water and return to your bed."
"4196","336 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: While Umm Salamah one night was lying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she rose as if concealing herself. He said: What is with you - have you menstruated? She said: Yes. He said: No harm; take your ablution water and return to your place. It has a witness in the two Sahihs, from the narration of Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah. And Khalid narrated it from Ikrimah, in another chapter."
"4197","Another [report]. 337 - Muhammad and Fatimah informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Aishah - may Allah be pleased with her - would bathe from a single vessel, contesting the water."
"4198","338 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us (H). 339 - And the Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar al-Saffar - in Nishapur - informed us, that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, both said: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us, Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Aishah would bathe from a single vessel, contesting the water. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from his aunt Aishah: I would bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel, our hands differing in it, from janabah. Husayn ibn Isa, brother of Sulaym al-Muqri, alone narrated it from al-Hakam ibn Aban, al-Daraqutni said."
"4199","Another [report]. 340 - Muhammad and Fatimah informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion. An Arab Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we take a mangy sheep and cast it among the sheep, and they become mangy. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, who made the first mangy? It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah. And Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi: al-Razi Abu Hatim said: He is not strong. He narrated from al-Hakam ibn Aban rejected hadiths, though Abu Hatim al-Busti entered him in the book of al-Thiqat, and Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah narrated from him; and most of the hadiths we brought for him have witnesses in the Sahih."
"4200","Another [report]. 341 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When this verse came down: And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, Faris sent to Quraysh to dispute with Muhammad, saying to him: What you slaughter with your hand with a knife is lawful, and what Allah slaughters with a sword of gold is unlawful! So this verse came down: And indeed the devils inspire their allies to dispute with you. He said: The devils are of Faris, and their allies are Quraysh."
